hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2401","Another: 2589 - My maternal uncle the Imam, scholar Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi informed us - may Allah have mercy on him - that Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq informed them, my uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ismail narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad, from Anas who said: Of the Sunna is that when the muadhdhin says in the adhan of Fajr, Come to success, he says: Prayer is better than sleep, prayer is better than sleep, Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah. Thus al-Daraqutni narrated it. And he also narrated it from Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Wakil, from al-Hasan ibn Arafa, from Hushaym, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas similarly, and he did not say: of the Sunna."
"2402","Another: 2590 - The Imam Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Silafi informed us - by ijaza - that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Allaf al-Muqri informed them, Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran al-Muaddal narrated to us, Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Baqi ibn Qani informed us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zuhayr al-Qurashi narrated to us, Azhar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has an angel calling at every prayer: O children of Adam, stand to your fires which you kindled upon yourselves and extinguish them with prayer."
"2403","2591 - And the Imam Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli informed us - at Isfahan - that Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zuhayr al-Qurashi narrated to us, Azhar ibn Sad al-Samman narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has an angel calling at every prayer: O children of Adam, stand to your fires which you kindled upon yourselves and extinguish them. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Ibn Awn except Azhar; Yahya ibn Zuhayr is alone in it."
"2404","2592 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Mubarak ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mishaqq informed us - at Baghdad - that ... narrated to us, Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Baghawi informed us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim Abu al-Hasan al-Bayhaqi narrated to us - in the suburb of the Ansar - Yahya ibn Zuhayr al-Qurashi narrated to us, Azhar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Exalted, has an angel calling at every prayer: Stand to your fires which you kindled, and extinguish them with prayer."
"2405","Another: 2593 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us, that the Qadi Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them, Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Mamun informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us, Muhammad ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Hatim ibn al-Layth narrated to us, Yahya ibn Khulayf ibn Uqba narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Awn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Jibril used to present the Quran to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) every year once in Ramadan; in the year in which he died he presented it twice. Muhammad said: So I hope our recitation is upon the last presentation. Al-Daraqutni said: A gharib hadith from the hadith of Abd Allah ibn Awn, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas. Yahya ibn Khulayf is alone in it."
"2406","Another: 2594 - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isbahani informed us - by ijaza - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym al-Isbahani informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Yazid al-Tahhan narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade praying over funerals between graves. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Asim except Hafs; Husayn ibn Yazid is alone in it."
"2407","Another: 2595 - Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid - known as Lafalaji - informed us in his book - from Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Wardi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A slave does not reach the reality of faith until he guards his tongue. Al-Tabarani said: Zuhayr ibn Abbad is alone. Ibn Abi Hatim said: Dawud ibn Hilal al-Nasibi: Abu Sulayman, narrated from al-Masudi, Malik ibn Mighwal, Bakr ibn Khunays, and Asad ibn Amr. Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruwasi narrated from him."
"2408","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah from Anas. 2596 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hibat Allah al-Nahwi al-Darir informed us - at Baghdad - that al-Mubaraka Sitt al-Ikhwa bint Muhammad ibn Mansur informed them, Asim ibn al-Hasan informed us, Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us, Abu Ali Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Saffar informed us, Yusuf ibn al-Dahhak al-Faqih narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, Abu Hashim Ammar ibn Umara, companion of al-Zafarani, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to them that Fatima brought a morsel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is this morsel, O Fatima? She said: A disc I baked, and my soul was not content until I brought you this morsel. So he said: It is the first food to enter your father's mouth in three days."
"2409","2597 - And Abu al-Fakhr Asad ibn Said ibn Rawh informed us - at Isfahan - that Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Sawra al-Baghdadi narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu Hashim, companion of al-Zafarani, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to him that Fatima - may Allah be pleased with her - brought a morsel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is this? She said: A disc I baked, and my soul was not content until I brought you this morsel. He said: It is the first food to enter your father's mouth in three days."
"2410","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Sulaym from Anas. 2598 - Abu Tahir al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us - at Isfahan - that his grandfather Abu al-Qasim Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Khalid informed them, Abu al-Tayyib Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Zadham informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba narrated to us, Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad informed us, from Bukayr, he is Ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Sulaym, from Anas (Ha: chain transforms; matn in next narration)."
"2411","2599 - And Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth, meaning Ibn Sad, narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Sulaym, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rakas, and with Abu Bakr two rakas, and with Umar two rakas, and with Uthman two rakas at the beginning of his rule. And Hajjaj narrated it from al-Layth also. Al-Nasai brought it from Qutayba, from al-Layth. And Amr ibn al-Harith narrated it from Bukayr."
"2412","2600 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba informed us, Harmala ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed us, Amr ibn al-Harith and al-Layth ibn Sad informed me, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Sulaym, from Anas ibn Malik that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed for us at Mina two rakas, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq prayed for us at Mina two rakas, and Umar ibn al-Khattab prayed for us at Mina two rakas, and Uthman ibn Affan prayed for us at Mina two rakas at the beginning of his caliphate; in the end of his caliphate he completed the prayer at Mina as four."
"2413","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Uthman from Anas. 2601 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: And Salim informed me, that he heard Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Uthman narrate from Anas, that al-Juhani said: O Messenger of Allah, we are where you know and cannot attend the month, so inform us of Laylat al-Qadr that we may attend it. He said: Attend the last seven of the month. He said: I cannot do that. He said: Seek it on the night of seven remaining, and it is this night. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the night of twenty-three, which is eight remaining. So he said: No, this month decreases, and it is seven remaining."
"2414","Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi from Anas. 2602 - Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Abi al-Wafa al-Wathiq ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Bayhaqi al-Khayyat at Marw informed us, that Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Amr Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Mahmi informed us, Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Muzakki informed us, recitation to him in his book, Abu Jafar Ahmad ibn Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Asadi at Hamadhan informed us, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Isa ibn Mina Qalun al-Muqri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi who said: I came to Anas ibn Malik in Ramadan while he intended travel, his mount had entered, he had worn travel clothes, and sunset had drawn near, so he called for food and ate, then mounted. I said to him: Is this Sunna? He said: Yes. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ismail, from Said ibn Abi Maryam, from Muhammad ibn Jafar, and said: A hasan hadith."
"2415","Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab al-Zuhri from Anas. 2603 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them, Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us (Ha). 2604 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (Ha: matn in next narration)."
"2416","2605 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dayri narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gesture in prayer."
"2417","2606 - And Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Haddad informed us, that Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his word, al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Masud al-Ajami narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gesture in prayer. Abu Dawud brought it in his Sunan from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Shabbuwayh and Muhammad ibn Rafi, from Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Daraqutni narrated it in his book from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Dawud, from Salama ibn Shabib, Muhammad ibn Masud al-Ajami, and Khushaysh ibn Asram, from Abd al-Razzaq. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from Abu Yala, from Yahya. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Abd al-Razzaq abbreviated this phrase from the hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he became weak, so he put Abu Bakr forward and he prayed with the people. And he said: Abd al-Razzaq erred in abbreviating this phrase and entered it in the chapter of one who gestures with his finger in prayer, and it was suggested that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only gestured with his hand in the tashahhud, and it is not so. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: I said to my father: Was the gesture of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Abu Bakr in prayer or before entering prayer? So he said: As for in the hadith of Shuayb from al-Zuhri, it indicates nothing of this. I said: Others besides Abd al-Razzaq narrated this hadith."
"2418","2607 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl informed us - at Isfahan - that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ridha informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abd al-Samad ibn Muhammad al-Aynuni al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Abu Hubayra al-Walid ibn Muhammad al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Salama ibn Bishr narrated to us, Yazid ibn al-Simt narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to gesture in prayer. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from al-Awzai except Yazid; Salama is alone in it."
"2419","Another: 2608 - Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar at Naysabur informed us that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, Abu Said Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Hamdun al-Tajir informed us, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Dhuhli narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa al-Absi narrated to us, Usama narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: On the day of Uhud the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Hamza with his nose cut and mutilation done to him, and said: Were it not that Safiyya would feel grief in herself, I would have left him until Allah gathers him from the bellies of beasts and birds. And he was shrouded in a striped cloak; when his head was covered his feet appeared, and when his feet were covered his head appeared, so his head was covered, and he did not pray over any of the martyrs."
"2420","2609 - And Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl, known as al-Haddad - at Isfahan - informed us that Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Simsar informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his word, Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, Yaqub narrated to us, Safwan, he is Ibn Isa, narrated to us, he said: Usama informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over Hamza on the day of Uhud and saw him mutilated, and said: Were it not that Safiyya would feel grief in herself, I would have left him until predators eat him, until he is gathered from their bellies. Then he called for a striped cloak and shrouded him in it. He said: When it was drawn over his feet his head appeared, and when drawn over his head his feet appeared. He said: The slain were many and clothes few, so he would shroud two and three men in one garment, then bury them together in one grave. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would ask about the one with most Quran and put him forward toward the qibla, burying them, and he did not pray over them."
"2421","2610 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abd Allah al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Usama ibn Zayd, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: On the day of Uhud the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Hamza with his nose cut and mutilation done to him, and he mentioned it similarly, and in it: And he said: I am a witness over you today. And he would gather three in a striped cloak, and ask: Which of them has most Quran, and put him forward in the lahd, and shroud two and three men in one garment. Al-Daraqutni said: The hadith of Usama ibn Zayd resembles being preserved."
"2422","Another: 2611 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Usama narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar. Usama said: And al-Zuhri narrated to me from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Uhud he heard the women of the Ansar weeping. He said: But Hamza has no weepers. That reached the women of the Ansar, so they wept for Hamza. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept, then awoke while they wept, and said: Woe to them, have they continued weeping since today? Let them weep, but let none weep over a dead one after today."
"2423","Another: 2612 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Musawir narrated to us, Abu Mamar Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Wahb dictated to me from his memory, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no cutting on a plunderer, nor a snatcher, nor a traitor. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Ibn Wahb; Abu Mamar is alone in it."
"2424","Another: 2613 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Dharr informed them, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus who said: Abu Ali ibn Yazid narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it: And We prescribed for them therein: a life for a life, an eye for an eye, a nose for a nose. Abu Bakr recited it upon the recitation of the generality."
"2425","2614 - And with it, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Yunus, from Abu Ali, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it: And We prescribed for them therein: a life for a life, an eye for an eye, a nose for a nose. I say: Thus al-Hulwani narrated to me, so I said to him - or we said to him - and he said: This is a permissible beginning."
"2426","2615 - And Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shabur, he is al-Baghdadi, narrated to us, Abu Nuaym, he is Ubayd ibn Hisham al-Hanbali, narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from his brother Abu Ali, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it: an eye for an eye. Imam Ahmad brought it from Yahya ibn Adam, from Ibn al-Mubarak. And Abu Dawud brought it from Nasr ibn Ali, from his father. And al-Tirmidhi brought it from Abu Kurayb and Suwayd ibn Nasr - all - from Ibn al-Mubarak. And al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan gharib hadith, and he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail said: Ibn al-Mubarak is alone in this hadith. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: This is a munkar hadith; I know none who narrated it from Yunus ibn Yazid except Ibn al-Mubarak, and Abu Ali ibn Yazid is unknown. And he said: Uqayl narrates it from al-Zuhri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mursal. And I greatly fear this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It was said to him: Abu Ubayd says: This is a sahih hadith, so he answered - meaning with this."
"2427","Another: 2616 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah Samuwayh informed us, Said ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid informed us, Uqayl ibn Khalid informed us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah's prophet Ayyub, peace be upon him, his trial lasted eighteen years or months - so near and far abandoned him except two men of his brothers who were of his most devoted brothers, who would come to him morning and evening. One of them said to his companion one day: Do you know, by Allah, that Ayyub has committed a sin no one of the worlds has committed? His companion said to him: What is that? He said: For eighteen months Allah has not had mercy on him to remove what is with him. When they went to Ayyub the man could not restrain himself until he mentioned that to him. So Ayyub, peace be upon him, said: I do not know what you say, except that Allah, Exalted, knows that I would pass by two men disputing, mentioning Allah, and I would return to my house and expiate for them lest Allah be mentioned except in truth. And he would go out for his need; when he fulfilled his need his wife would hold his hand until he arrived. One day he was late for her, so it was revealed to Ayyub, peace be upon him, in his place: Strike with your foot; this is a cool bath and drink. She waited for him, and met him watching; he came to her with Allah, Exalted, having removed his trial, at his finest. When she saw him she said: O, may Allah bless you, have you seen Allah's prophet, peace be upon him, this afflicted one? By Allah, I never saw one resembling him more than you when he was healthy. He said: I am he. And he had two threshing floors, one for wheat and one for barley, so Allah, Exalted, sent two clouds; when one was over the wheat floor it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver into the barley floor until it overflowed. Imam Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated it in the hadith of al-Zuhri from Said ibn al-Hakam, and in it: eighteen years, without doubt. And Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated it from Nafi ibn Yazid."
"2428","2617 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Mihran ibn Mihrabazd informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba narrated to us, Harmala ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid informed me, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Ayyub, Allah's prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), remained in his trial eighteen years; near and far abandoned him except two men of his brothers who were of his most devoted brothers, who would come to him morning and evening. One of them said to his companion: Do you know, by Allah, Ayyub has committed a sin no one of the worlds has committed? His companion said to him: What is that? He said: For eighteen years Allah has not had mercy on him to remove what is with him. When he went to him the man could not restrain himself until he mentioned that to him. So Ayyub said: I do not know what you say, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knows that I would pass by two men quarreling, mentioning Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and I would return to my house and expiate for them out of dislike that Allah be mentioned except in truth. He said: And he would go out to his need; when he fulfilled his need his wife would hold his hand until he arrived. One day he was late for her, so Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to Ayyub, peace be upon him, in his place: Strike with your foot; this is a cool bath and drink. She waited for him, and met him watching; he came to her with Allah having removed his trial, at his finest. When she saw him she said: O, may Allah bless you, have you seen Allah's prophet, this afflicted one? By Allah, I never saw anyone resembling him more than you when he was healthy. He said: I am he. And he had two threshing floors, one for wheat and one for barley, so Allah sent two clouds; when one was over the wheat floor it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver into the barley floor until it overflowed. Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti brought it in his book from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba, from Harmala."
"2429","Another: 2618 - Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Samani at Marw informed us that Abu Muhammad Nasrak ibn Nawshtakin ibn Abd Allah al-Rumi informed them, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Shujai informed us, al-Nasr Abadhi, he is Ismail ibn Ibrahim, informed us, my father informed us, Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Azhar informed us, Said ibn Yaqub al-Talqani informed us, Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded with sandals and the ring."
"2430","Another: 2619 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Matush informed us - with my recitation to him on the western side of Baghdad - I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, recitation to him while you listened, so he acknowledged it; al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: There shall now appear to you a man of Paradise. Then a man of the Ansar appeared with his beard dripping from his wudu, holding his sandals in his left hand. The next day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the like, and that man appeared like the first time. On the third day the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said his saying also, and that man appeared in his first state. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As followed him and said: I quarreled with my father and swore not to enter upon him for three days; if you see fit to shelter me until they pass, do so? He said: Yes. Anas said: Abd Allah would narrate that he spent those three nights with him, and did not see him rise at night at all, except that when he stirred and turned on his bed he mentioned Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and said Allahu Akbar until Fajr prayer came. Abd Allah said: Except that I did not hear him say but good. When the three passed and I almost belittled his deeds, I said: O slave of Allah, there was no anger or desertion between me and my father, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say of you three times: There shall now appear to you a man of Paradise, and you appeared the three times. So I wanted to stay with you to see your deeds and follow them, but I did not see you do great deeds. So what brought you to what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? He said: It is only what you saw. He said: When I turned away he called me and said: It is only what you saw, except that I find in myself no deceit for any Muslim, nor envy any for good Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gave him. So Abd Allah said: This is what brought you, and it is what we cannot bear. Al-Nasai narrated it in the book of deeds of day and night, from Suwayd ibn Nasr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from Mamar similarly. And Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri: that Anas ibn Malik informed him, and he mentioned it."
"2431","Another: 2620 - Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Silafi informed us in his book that Abu al-Fath Ismail ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Maliki informed them - at Qazwin - he said: I heard Abu Yala al-Khalil ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad - he is Ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Khalil al-Hafiz - dictating - Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qadi and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Maymun narrated to me, both said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated to us, Salih ibn Muhammad al-Azadhwari narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: I read to Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating onion and leek raw. Al-Khalili said: None narrated it from Malik except Yahya, and he is trustworthy, an Imam, and it was only written from Salih from him. And al-Khalili said: Abu Muhammad Salih ibn Muhammad is a trustworthy shaykh who came to Qazwin long ago."
"2432","Another: 2621 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Abd Allah Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Anbari at Basra narrated to us, Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought help from some Jews in a battle and allotted shares to him. I did not see it from Malik except from Ismail, and Allah knows best. And Ali ibn al-Madini narrated it from Sufyan ibn Uyayna, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from al-Zuhri, mursal. And Sufyan said: We found this only with Yazid."
"2433","Another: 2622 - Abu al-Hajjaj Yusuf ibn Maali ibn Nasr al-Bazzaz al-Kinani al-Dimashqi there informed us that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Qubays al-Ghassani informed them, Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Dawud al-Antaki informed us, Tamam ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Junayd al-Razi informed us, Abu al-Tayyib Muhammad ibn Humayd ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Hawrani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamza narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Four I learned from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, no partner have You, here I am; indeed praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You. It was narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Umar."
"2434","Another: 2623 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Fatima bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridha informed us, Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered in Umrat al-Qada, with Ibn Rawaha before him saying:"
"2435","2624 - And it was read to Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn Tawus - while we listened at Damascus more than once - that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami informed them, he said: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, the Qadi Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf ibn Faris al-Mayanaji informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us - recitation to him - Muammal ibn Ihab narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered in Umrat al-Qada with Ibn Rawaha before him saying: Al-Daraqutni said: Abd al-Razzaq is alone in it from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, and it is said he erred in it, that he heard this hadith from Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai, from Thabit, from Anas, and its chain was inverted upon him; it is preserved from the hadith of Sad ibn Sulayman, from Thabit, from Anas. Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Qutayba, from Ibn Abi al-Sari, from Abd al-Razzaq."
"2436","Another: 2625 - Abu Tahir Muawiya ibn Ali ibn Muawiya al-Sufi informed us in his book that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Miqdam, he is Ibn Dawud ibn Isa ibn Talid al-Ruayni al-Misri, narrated to us, my uncle Said ibn Isa narrated to us, al-Mufaddal ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on al-Khumra and prostrate on it. Al-Daraqutni said: Al-Mufaddal ibn Fadala and Ibn Wahb narrated it from Yunus, from al-Zuhri. And Shabib ibn Said sent it mursal from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah knows best."
"2437","Another: 2626 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, al-Muqaddami and Abu Kamil narrated to us, both said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas."
"2438","2627 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized Asad ibn Zurara for a thorn. The wording is one."
"2439","2628 - And Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Shaybani informed them, Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us, Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Muzakki al-Naysaburi informed us, Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi informed us, Said ibn Yaqub al-Talqani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized Asad ibn Zurara for a thorn. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Humayd ibn Masada, from Yazid ibn Zuray, and said: A hasan gharib hadith. And al-Daraqutni said: Mamar narrates it from al-Zuhri, from Anas, and erred in it; he narrated it to them at Basra, and the sahih is from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cauterized Asad ibn Zurara."
"2440","Another: 2629 - Bint Khali Umm Ahmad Amina bint Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Qudama al-Zahida informed us - with my recitation to her at Busra - I said to her: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman informed you, by ijaza; Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Khayrun informed us, Abu Amr Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Allaf informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii informed us, Muhammad, he is Ibn Ghalib, narrated to us, Ruwaym ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to me, al-Layth narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Upon you is night travel, for the earth is folded at night."
"2441","2630 - And the Qadi Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi informed them, Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khallal informed us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Shihab al-Daqqaq al-Nafari informed us, al-Husayn, he is al-Mahamili, narrated to us, Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Ruwaym ibn Yazid narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you travel in fertility, descend from your mounts and give them their due of herbage; and when you travel in drought, proceed on them. And upon you is night travel, for the earth is folded at night. Al-Daraqutni said: Ruwaym ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated it from al-Layth, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, and Muhammad ibn Aslam al-Qurashi followed him, from Qabisa, from al-Layth, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Anas. And what is preserved is from Layth, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, mursal."
"2442","Another: 2631 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us - recitation to him while we listened - it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you; al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina while it was feverish, so the people fell ill with fever. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque while the people were sitting, and said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. So the people exerted themselves praying standing."
"2443","2632 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Dabari informed us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Anas ibn Malik informed me, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while it was feverish, so the people fell ill with fever. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while the people prayed sitting, and said: The prayer of one sitting is half the prayer of one standing. So the people exerted themselves for prayer standing."
"2444","Another: 2633 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Abbas al-Misri narrated to us, al-Rabi ibn Sulayman al-Jizi narrated to us, Abu Zura Wahb Allah ibn Rashid narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Muadh ibn Jabal: Shall I not teach you a supplication to supplicate with, by which if you had a debt like a mountain Allah would settle it for you? Say, O Muadh: O Allah, Owner of dominion, You give dominion to whom You will and take dominion from whom You will, honor whom You will and humble whom You will; in Your hand is good; indeed You are over all things Capable; Rahman of this world and the Hereafter and their Rahim, You give them to whom You will and withhold them from whom You will; have mercy on me with a mercy that suffices me from the mercy of any besides You. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from him except Wahb Allah."
"2445","Another: 2634 - Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi informed us, that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamza ibn al-Khadir al-Sulami informed them, Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kinani informed us, Tamam ibn Muhammad al-Razi informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Dahhak ibn Yazid al-Saksaki narrated to us - at Bayt Lahya - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Choose well for your sperm."
"2446","Another: 2635 - Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Umari informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them - recitation to him - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii informed us, Ibn Kazal, he is Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn Kazal, narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Nufayl narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank standing."
"2447","2636 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Miskin ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank standing. It has a witness in the Sahihayn from the hadith of Ibn Abbas."
"2448","Another: 2637 - Abu Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) let his forelock hang as long as Allah willed him to hang it, then parted it after. Al-Daraqutni said: Man, al-Qanabi, and Abu Musab narrated it from Malik, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, mursal, and the mursal is more correct."
"2449","Another: 2638 - Fatima bint Sad al-Khayr ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Ansari informed us - with my recitation to her at Cairo - I said to her: Abu al-Rikab Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Mubarak ibn Ahmad al-Anmati informed you - recitation to him while you listened - Qadi al-Qudat Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Damaghani informed us, Shaykh Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan al-Faqih, known as Ibn al-Quduri, informed us - recitation to him, so he acknowledged it while I listened - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Suwayd al-Muaddib informed us, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Akhi al-Imam at Aleppo narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The most beloved day to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to travel in was Friday."
"2450","Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas. 2639 - Abu al-Fadl Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yusuf al-Urmawi informed them, Abu al-Hasan Jabir ibn Yasin ibn Mahmawayh al-Attar informed us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallas informed us, Ubayd Allah, he is Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Sukkari, narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yusuf, he is Ibn Khalid al-Taghlibi, narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan al-Kinani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord for al-Lahin and He gave them to me. I said: What are al-Lahun, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The offspring of mankind. Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq also narrated it from Ibn al-Munkadir."
"2451","Another: 2640 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Ibn Ulayya narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas: that a man sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Evil is the brother of the clan, or: evil is the cousin of the clan. Then he permitted him, and he entered upon him, and he was cheerful to him and spoke with him. When he left, Aisha said: O Messenger of Allah, he sought permission upon you and you disliked him, then he entered and you were cheerful to him and spoke with him. And he said: Among the worst of people with Allah - Ayyub said: And I think he said: on the Day of Resurrection - is one whom people avoid for his foulness. And Ibn Mani said: I witnessed Salama ibn Salih narrate from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. Al-Daraqutni said: Salama ibn Salih al-Ahmar narrates it from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas, and erred in it; and Ayyub narrated it from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Aisha, mursal. And Ibn Uyayna, Mamar, and Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated it from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Urwa, from Aisha, and that is the sahih."
"2452","Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas. 2641 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: I heard Mukhtar ibn Fulful say: I asked Anas ibn Malik about drinking in vessels. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muzaffat, and said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"2453","2642 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Isbahani informed us - there - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail ibn Abi Samina narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar, from Anas - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a drink in Yemen called bit and mizr. So he said: Whatever intoxicates is unlawful."
"2454","2643 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Idris, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade vessels and said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. Abu Khaythama and Ahmad ibn Mani narrated it from Ibn Idris. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ziyad, from Ibn Idris."
"2455","Another: 2644 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me (Ha). 2645 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Abi Tahir ibn Abi Ghanim al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, both said: Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Messengership and Prophethood have been cut off, so there is no messenger after me nor prophet. He said: That weighed upon the people. He said: He said: But al-Mubashshirat. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what are al-Mubashshirat? He said: The dream of a Muslim man, and it is a part of the parts of Prophethood. The wording is Ahmad ibn Hanbal's. And in the narration of Zuhayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Messengership, and he said: The dream of a Muslim, and did not say man, and the rest is like it. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Zafarani, from Affan, and said: Sahih gharib from the hadith of al-Mukhtar."
"2456","Malik ibn Dinar al-Zahid from Anas. 2646 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Hisham, companion of al-Dastuwai, narrated to us, from al-Mughira, son-in-law of Malik ibn Dinar, from Malik, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came upon the lowest heaven on the night I was taken, and saw in it men whose tongues and lips were cut with scissors of fire. So I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: Preachers of your umma."
"2457","2647 - And Abu Tahir Muawiya ibn Ali ibn Muawiya al-Sufi informed us in his book that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwai, from al-Mughira, son-in-law of Malik ibn Dinar, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came on the night I was taken upon the lowest heaven, and in it were men whose tongues and lips were clipped with scissors of fire. So I said, O Jibril: Who are these? He said: These are the preachers of your umma. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from al-Mughira, son-in-law of Ibn Dinar, except Hisham al-Dastuwai. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn al-Minhal, and said: Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated this report from Hisham, from al-Mughira, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Thumama, from Anas, and erred in it; for Yazid ibn Zuray is more precise than two hundred like Abu Attab and his likes."
"2458","Another: 2648 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim al-Khabbaz informed us, Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Ajlan ibn Abd Allah of Banu Adi narrated to me, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When death came to Abu Salama, Umm Salama said: To whom do you entrust me? He said: O Allah, replace for Umm Salama better than Abu Salama. When he died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to her, and she said: I am old in age. He said: I am older than you in age; and dependents are upon Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); as for jealousy, I shall supplicate Allah to remove it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her and sent her a hand mill and a water jar."
"2459","Muslim ibn Ziyad al-Shami, freedman of Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Anas. 2649 - Abu al-Maali Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Hibat Allah informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn al-Zaghuni informed them, Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Bishri informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas informed us, Abd Allah, he is al-Baghawi, narrated to us, Luwayn narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ziyad informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whoever says in the morning: O Allah, we enter morning bearing witness to You, and bearing witness the bearers of Your Throne, Your angels, and all Your creation, that You are Allah, there is no god but You, alone without partner, and that Muhammad is Your slave and Messenger - Allah, Mighty and Majestic, frees a quarter of him from the Fire on that day; if he says it twice Allah frees half of him; if he says it three times Allah frees three quarters of him; if he says it four times Allah frees him that day from the Fire."
"2460","2650 - And Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamza ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us - at Damascus - that Abu al-Majd Maali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Taghlibi informed them, Abu al-Faraj Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfrayini informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Khallal informed us, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyuwayh al-Naysaburi informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali ibn Sinan ibn Bahr al-Nasai informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Baqiyya ibn al-Walid informed us, he said: Muslim ibn Ziyad, freedman of Maymuna, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in the morning: O Allah, I bear witness to You and bear witness the bearers of Your Throne, Your angels, and all Your creation, that You are Allah, there is no god but You, alone without partner, and that Muhammad is Your slave and Messenger - Allah frees a quarter of him that day from the Fire; if he says it four times Allah frees him that day from the Fire. Thus al-Nasai brought it in deeds of day and night. And from Amr ibn Uthman and Kathir ibn Ubayd, from Baqiyya. And al-Tirmidhi brought it from al-Darimi, from Haywa ibn Shurayh, from Baqiyya. And Makhul narrated it from Anas."
"2461","Mishaj ibn Musa al-Dabbi from Anas (Mishaj was declared trustworthy by Yahya ibn Main). 2651 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Amr ibn Awn narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughira who said: Al-Mishaj ibn Musa narrated to me, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stopped at a place and spoke in it, would not depart from it until he prayed Zuhr."
"2462","2652 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abd Allah al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from Mishaj al-Dabbi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, we would say: whether the sun declined or not, he prayed Zuhr then departed. Al-Daraqutni's note: Abu Dawud brought it from Musaddad, from Abu Muawiya."
"2463","2653 - And Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us - at Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, my grandfather Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Mishaj narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas say: When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, we would say: the sun has declined or not declined; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr with us then departed."
"2464","2654 - And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Muawiya narrated to us, Mishaj al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we would say: the sun has declined or not declined; he prayed Zuhr then departed."
"2465","Muadh ibn Harmala al-Azdi from Anas. 2655 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Muadh ibn Harmala al-Azdi narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people are rained upon with a general rain and the earth grows nothing."
"2466","2656 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Abu Bakr narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Harmalah al-Azdi narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There will come upon people a time when the sky rains a general rain, but the earth will grow nothing.' And Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated it from al-Husayn."
"2467","2657 - Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr, known as Habbuwayh, informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Baghban informed them: Abu Amr Abd al-Wahhab ibn Mandah informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his saying: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Ahmad, who is Ibn Mansur, narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: al-Husayn informed us: Mu'adh ibn Harmalah informed me: Anas narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The Hour will not come until people are rained upon with a general rain, but the earth will not grow.'"
"2468","2658 - Mughirah ibn Abi Qurrah al-Sadusi from Anas. Abu al-Daw Shihab ibn Mahmud ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Harawi informed us, there, that Abd al-Salam ibn Ahmad ibn Ismail, known as Bukayrah, informed them, recited to him: Muhammad ibn Abi Mas'ud al-Farisi informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh informed us; it was said to him: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to you: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: al-Mughirah ibn Abi Qurrah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I tie it and rely, or leave it loose and rely? He said: 'Tie it and rely.' Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Amr ibn Ali. Amr ibn Ali said: Yahya said: In my view this hadith is munkar (rejected)."
"2469","2659 - Mus'ab ibn Sulaym from Anas (he has one hadith in Muslim). Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us, recited to him while I listened; it was said to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you, by ijazah; and it was said to him: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ghazzal informed you, recited to him while you listened: Abu al-Fadl Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us; both said: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hamzah and Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Rustah narrated to us: Abu Ma'mar narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Mus'ab ibn Sulaym, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Many a man with two worn garments, paid no heed to, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill it; among them is al-Bara ibn Malik.' When the day of Tustar came and the people were exposed, they said to him: O Bara, swear by your Lord. He said: I swear upon You, O my Lord, that You grant us their shoulders (victory over them) and join me with Your Prophet. He said: So he was martyred."
"2470","2660 - Al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi from Anas. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, meaning: Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi narrated to us; he heard Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — with a chain transition —"
"2471","2661 - Abu Ghalib ibn Hamzah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Asadi informed us, at Damascus, that his grandfather al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Missisi informed us: Turab ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Katib informed us, in Egypt: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Nasih ibn Shuja' al-Faqih informed us: Ali ibn Ghalib ibn Salm al-Saksaki informed us, in the mosque of Bayt Lahya: Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Nujayh al-Madini narrated to us: Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi narrated to me: that he heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant.' Their wording is one."
"2472","2662 - Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Ahmad al-Mu'adhdhin informed us, at Isfahan, that Ismail ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Sufi informed them: Abu al-Wafa Muhammad ibn Badi' informed us, with a chain transition. 2663 - Abu al-Haytham Shadhrah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ala ibn Shadhrah al-Madini informed us, there, that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Qasim al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Amr Abd al-Wahhab ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Mandah informed us; both said: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah, who is Ibn Khurshid, informed us his saying: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad, who is Ibn al-A'rabi, informed us: Abu al-Fadl Ja'far ibn Amir al-Bazzaz narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'There is no faith for one who has no trustworthiness, and no religion for one who has no covenant.'"
"2473","2664 - Makhul al-Shami from Anas (Abu Mushir Abd al-A'la ibn Mushir mentioned that Makhul heard from Anas ibn Malik). Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us, by my recitation to him at al-Harbiyyah; I said to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed you, and he acknowledged it: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muslimah informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Mughirah Abu Salamah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, at Madinah: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Majid, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, from Makhul, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever says when he enters morning and when he enters evening: O Allah, I call You to witness, and I call the bearers of Your Throne, Your angels and all Your creation to witness, that You are Allah, there is no god but You alone, You have no partner, and that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is Your servant and Messenger — a quarter of him is freed from the Fire; whoever says it twice, Allah frees half of him from the Fire; whoever says it three times, Allah frees three quarters of him from the Fire; and whoever says it four times, Allah the Exalted frees him from the Fire.'"
"2474","2665 - The Imam, the Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ali ibn Surur al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Abu Rashid Ismail ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid al-Bayyi' informed them: Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Mutarriz informed us: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Qattan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rafi' narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Majid informed us, from Hisham ibn al-Ghaz ibn Rabi'ah, from Makhul al-Dimashqi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever says when he enters morning or evening: O Allah, I enter morning calling You to witness, and calling the bearers of Your Throne, Your angels and all Your creation to witness, that You are Allah, there is no god but You alone, You have no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger — Allah frees a quarter of him from the Fire; and if he says it four times, Allah frees him from the Fire.' Abu Dawud brought it out in his Sunan in similar form, from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Muhammad ibn Abi Fudayk, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Majid. And it is said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Salim ibn Abi Raja al-Makfuf."
"2475","2666 - Another. Abu Ali Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us, at al-Harbiyyah, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Muslimah informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya ibn Muhammad, who is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Makhul, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no household among whom no warrior wages war, nor do they equip a warrior, nor take his place among his family, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, afflicts them with a calamity before the Day of Resurrection.'"
"2476","2667 - Another. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zayd ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Abu Mu'id narrated to us: Makhul narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: It was said, O Messenger of Allah: When should we abandon enjoining good and forbidding evil? He said: 'When there appears among you the like of what appeared among the Children of Israel: when indecency is among your elders, rule among your young, and knowledge among your lowly ones.'"
"2477","2668 - Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us, by my recitation to him at al-Harbiyyah; I said to him: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed you, and he acknowledged it: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslimah informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us: Yazid ibn Abd al-Samad al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn A'idh narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us: Hafs, who is Ibn Ghaylan Abu Mu'id, narrated to us, from Makhul, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when is enjoining good and forbidding evil abandoned? He said: 'When there appears among you what appeared among the Children of Israel before you.' It was said: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'When flattery appears among your best, indecency among your worst, and understanding (of religion) among your lowest.' And Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated it from Ali al-Qurashi, from Makhul, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Anas ibn Malik, adding Kathir ibn Murrah. Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Dimashqi, from Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd, from al-Haytham ibn Humayd, from Abu Mu'id, from Makhul."
"2478","2669 - Musa ibn Anas from his father. Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a sukkah (a small vessel of perfume) from which he perfumed himself. Abu Dawud brought it out in similar form from Nasr ibn Ali. And al-Tirmidhi brought it out in al-Shama'il, from Muhammad ibn Rafi' — both — from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri, from Shayban al-Nahwi, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mukhtar, from Musa ibn Anas, from Anas, in similar form."
"2479","2670 - Another. The eminent Imam Muzaffar ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Hasan ibn Yataba al-Harimi informed us, by my recitation to him at al-Harim; I said to him: Abu Muhammad Sulayman ibn Mas'ud ibn al-Husayn al-Qassab informed you, recited to him while you listened, and he acknowledged it; he said: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah al-Raba'i informed us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Bazzaz informed us: Abu Amr Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Abu Qilabah Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqashi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Rumi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Anas, he said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, you would not enjoy rest on beds, you would not touch women, you would not enjoy food and drink, and you would go out to the open heights crying out to Allah and weeping.' It was brought out in the Two Sahihs from its beginning up to his saying: much; the rest they did not bring out, and Allah knows best."
"2480","2671 - Musa al-Qutabi Abu al-Ala from Anas. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us, by my recitation to him at Baghdad; I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, recited to him while you listened, and he acknowledged it: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Bahz narrated to us: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us: Musa Abu al-Ala informed us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray during winter days, and we did not know whether more of the day had passed or more remained."
"2481","2672 - And with it my father narrated to me: Abu Kamil and Affan narrated to us, both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Musa Abu al-Ala. Affan said in his hadith: Musa Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray the noon prayer during winter days, and we did not know whether more of the day had gone or more of it remained."
"2482","2673 - Musa ibn Maysarah al-Abdi from Anas (Sa'id narrated from him, and al-Haytham ibn Jammaz). Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Ka'b al-Abdi narrated to us: Musa ibn Maysarah al-Abdi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I intend a journey, so advise me. He said: When? He said: Tomorrow, if Allah wills. Then he came to him and he took his hand and said to him: 'In Allah's protection and shelter; may Allah provide you with piety, forgive your sin, and direct you to good wherever you are' — or 'wheresoever you are' — Sa'id doubted."
"2483","2674 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us, at Damascus, that Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn al-Fath al-Sulami informed them: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us: my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Samiri informed us: al-Abbas ibn Abd Allah al-Tarqufi narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Ka'b al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Maysarah al-Abdi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I intend a journey, so advise me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: When? He said: Tomorrow, if Allah wills. Then he came to him and he took his hand and said to him: 'In Allah's protection and in His shelter; may Allah provide you with piety, forgive your sin, and direct you to good wherever you are' — or 'wheresover you are' — Sa'id doubted one of the two wordings. Al-Darimi narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim. And al-Mahamili narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir ibn Jabalah, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Dawraqi, and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Qadi — all of them — from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, with its chain, in similar form."
"2484","2675 - Maymun ibn Siyah from Anas (al-Bukhari brought out one hadith from him). Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Isbahani informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik al-Zibaqi Abu Ishaq narrated to us: Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us: Maymun ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'No people sit remembering Allah, Mighty and Majestic, except that a caller from heaven calls to them: Rise forgiven; your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds.' Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Maymun ibn Ajlan except Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik. I say: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Sadusi has narrated it from Maymun ibn Ajlan."
"2485","2676 - Abu Ali ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali al-Nasri informed us, at Baghdad, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Bazzaz al-Ansari informed them, recited to him: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us, he said: Abu Muhammad Ubayd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ma'ruf informed us, recited to him: Abu al-Qasim Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muflis narrated to us, by dictation: al-Walid ibn Amr ibn al-Sukayn narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub Sahib al-Sil'ah narrated to us: Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a chain transition."
"2486","2677 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad, who is Ibn Ar'arah, narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub, meaning al-Sadusi, narrated to us: Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'There are no people who gather remembering Allah, seeking thereby nothing but His Face, except that a caller from heaven calls them: Rise forgiven; your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds.' Their wording is one."
"2487","2678 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, recited to him while we listened, at al-Harbiyyah; it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Maymun al-Mura'i informed us: Maymun ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'There are no people who gather remembering Allah, Blessed and Exalted, seeking thereby nothing but His Face, except that a caller from heaven calls them: Rise forgiven; your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds.'"
"2488","2679 - Another. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Sadusi narrated to us: Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: 'There is no Muslim servant who comes to a brother of his visiting him for Allah's sake, except that a caller from heaven calls him: You are good and Paradise is good for you; otherwise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says in the kingdom of His Throne: My servant visited for My sake, and upon Me is his hospitality, Paradise; so He is not pleased with any hospitality for him less than Paradise.'"
"2489","2680 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah al-Sulami informed us, recited to him while we listened; it was said to him: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you, by ijazah; and it was said to him: Abu Bakr Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed you, recited to him at Baghdad: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us; both said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, both said: Ali ibn al-Walid al-Fasawi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Sadusi narrated to us: Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'There is no Muslim servant who comes to a brother of his for Allah's sake visiting him, except that a caller from heaven calls: That you are good and Paradise is good for you; otherwise Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says in the kingdom of His Throne: My servant visited for My sake, and upon Me is his hospitality, and Allah will not be pleased with any hospitality for His friend less than Paradise.'"
"2490","2681 - Another. Afifah bint Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Farfaniyyah informed us, at Isfahan, that Abd al-Wahid ibn Qamar ibn Ahmad al-Sabbagh informed them: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us [...]: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed us [...]: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Sadusi narrated [...], from Ibn Ajlan, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There is no [...] — with a chain transition."
"2491","2682 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Sadusi narrated to us: Maymun ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 'There are no two Muslims who meet and one of them takes the hand of his companion, except that it is binding upon Allah to attend their supplication, and not to separate them until He forgives them.' Their wording is one, and Ibn Ajlan was not named in the narration of al-Fasawi."
"2492","2683 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us, at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Maymun al-Mura'i narrated to us: Maymun ibn Siyah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'There are no two Muslims who meet and one of them takes the hand of his companion, except that it is binding upon Allah to attend their supplication, and not to separate their hands until He forgives them.'"
"2493","2684 - Nubayt ibn Sharit from Anas. Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi informed us, recited to him while we listened, at Damascus; it was said to him: your grandfather the Hafiz Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed you, recited to him and he acknowledged it: al-Sharif Abu Nasr al-Zaynabi informed us: Abu Tahir al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated to us: Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us: Nubayt ibn Sharit narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I witnessed the sermon of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina; he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'Praise be to Allah, I praise Him and seek His help.' Then he asked them: Which day is most sacred? They said: This day. He said: Then which land is most sacred? They said: This land. He said: Then which month is most sacred? They said: This month. He said: 'Then your blood and your wealth are sacred to you like the sacredness of this day of yours in this land of yours. Have I conveyed?' They said: O Allah, yes."
"2494","2685 - Nafi' Abu Ghalib al-Basri al-Khayyat from Anas. Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Isbahani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Abu Ghalib narrated to us, he said: I witnessed Anas pray over a man, and he stood at the head of the bier; then a woman of Quraysh was brought and he prayed over her and stood near the middle of the bier. Among those who attended his funeral was al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi. When he saw the difference in his standing, he said: O Abu Hamzah, is this how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand for the woman and the man as you stood? He said: Yes. He said: So he turned to us and said: Memorize."
"2495","2686 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Shayban narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Abu Ghalib narrated to us, he said: I prayed with Anas over the funeral of a man, and he stood facing the bier; then he sat, and the funeral of a woman of Quraysh was brought. When they saw him they said: O Abu Hamzah, this is the funeral of so-and-so, daughter of so-and-so. He stood and prayed over her, standing facing the middle of the bier. Al-Ala ibn Ziyad witnessed the prayer with him. When he saw the difference of his standing for the man and the woman, they said: O Abu Hamzah, is this how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do, standing for the man as you stood and standing for the woman as you stood? He said: Yes. He said: So al-Ala ibn Ziyad turned to us with his face and said: Memorize."
"2496","2687 - Zahir informed us that al-Husayn informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us: Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Nafi' Abu Ghalib narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik led us in prayer over the funeral of a man and stood facing his chest; he said: And he prayed over a woman and stood facing her hips. Al-Ala ibn Ziyad said to him: O Abu Hamzah, is this how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray? He said: Yes. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Sahba also narrated it from Nafi'. And Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated it, both, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Hammam. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Dawud ibn Mu'adh, from Abd al-Warith. And al-Tirmidhi brought it out from Abd Allah ibn Munir, from Sa'id ibn Amir, from Hammam, abridged. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Nasr ibn Ali, from Sa'id ibn Amir, abridged."
"2497","2688 - Another. Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Nafi' Abu Ghalib al-Bahili narrated to us; he witnessed Anas ibn Malik, he said: Al-Ala ibn Ziyad al-Adawi said: O Abu Hamzah, at the age of which men was the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he was sent? He said: A son of forty years. He said: Then what was next? He said: Then he was in Makkah ten years and in Madinah ten years, so sixty years were completed for him; then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, took him to Himself. He said: Of the age of which men was he then? He said: Like the most youthful of men, the handsomest, the most beautiful and the most fleshy. He said: O Abu Hamzah, did you wage war with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, I warred with him on the day of Hunayn. The idolaters came out in multitude and charged us until we saw our horses behind our backs. Among the idolaters was a man who charged and crushed us and broke us. When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that, he dismounted, and Allah routed them and they turned. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood when he saw the victory, and they began to be brought to him as captives, man by man, and they pledged to him upon Islam. A man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon me is a vow: if the man who today kept crushing us is brought, I shall strike his neck. He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent, and the man was brought. He said: When he saw the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: O Prophet of Allah, I repent to Allah; O Prophet of Allah, I repent to Allah. He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held back, pledging him, so that the other might fulfill his vow. He said: He kept looking at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for him to order his killing, and he feared to kill him in awe of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw that he did nothing, he pledged him. He said: O Prophet of Allah, my vow! He said: 'I only held back from him since today so that you might fulfill your vow.' He said: O Prophet of Allah, did you not signal to me? He said: 'It is not for a prophet to signal.' Its beginning has been mentioned in the Sahih, and in it are things not in the Sahih, and Allah knows best."
"2498","2689 - Another. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Sahba narrated to us: Nafi' Abu Ghalib al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'People will be raised on the Day of Resurrection while the sky drizzles upon them.'"
"2499","2690 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Sahba narrated to us: Abu Ghalib narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala ibn Ziyad say to Anas ibn Malik: How will people be raised on the Day of Resurrection? He said: They will be raised while the sky drizzles upon them. In it there is no mention of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2500","2691 - Al-Nadr ibn Anas from his father. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, recited to him while we listened, at al-Harbiyyah; it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed you: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yunus narrated to us: Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: I asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to intercede for me on the Day of Resurrection. He said: He said: I shall do it. He said: Where shall I seek you on the Day of Resurrection, O Prophet of Allah? He said: Seek me the first you seek me upon the Sirat. He said: I said: If I do not meet you upon the Sirat? He said: Then I am at the Balance. He said: I said: If I do not meet you at the Balance? He said: Then I am at the Hawd; I do not miss these three stations on the Day of Resurrection. Muslim narrated a hadith by this route: Yunus, from Harb, from al-Nadr, from Anas. Al-Tirmidhi brought it out in al-Zuhd, from Abd Allah ibn al-Sabbah al-Hashimi, from Badal ibn al-Muhabbar, from Harb, and said: Hasan gharib, we know it only from this route."
"2501","2692 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Abd Allah al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us, he said: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to me, he said: Harb ibn Maymun narrated to me, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, where shall I meet you on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Upon the Sirat. I said: If I do not find you? He said: At the Hawd. I said: If I do not find you? He said: At the Balance; I do not miss these three places."
"2502","2693 - Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl al-Haddad informed us, at Isfahan, that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his saying: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Fadl al-A'raj, who is Ibn Sahl, narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Harb narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I asked the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to intercede for me on the Day of Resurrection. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall do that. He said: Where shall I seek you on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Seek me the first you seek me at the Sirat. He said: I said: If I do not meet you? He said: Then we are at the Balance. He said: I said: If I do not meet you at the Balance? He said: Then I am at the Hawd; I do not miss these three stations on the Day of Resurrection. Mention of the continuity of this hadith and the hearing of some of them from others."
"2503","2694 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Mas'ud al-Busiri informed us, at Cairo, that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Umar al-Farra informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Hasan ibn Ismail al-Darrab informed us, recited to him while I listened: my father Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Marwan informed me, recited to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Marwan ibn Muhammad ibn Malik al-Dinawari al-Maliki informed us: Ismail ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Harami ibn Hafs narrated to us: Harb ibn Maymun al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Anas narrated to me: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Your little servant Anas, intercede for him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: I shall do it. He said: Where shall I seek you? He said: Seek me the first you seek me at the Sirat; if you find me, otherwise I am at the Balance; if you find me, otherwise I am at the Hawd; I do not miss these three places."
"2504","2695 - Another. Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harimi informed us, by my recitation to him on the western side of Baghdad; I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you, and he acknowledged it: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan ibn Malik informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Harb ibn Maymun Abu al-Khattab al-Ansari narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me: 'I am standing waiting for my Ummah crossing the Sirat when Isa came to me.' He said: He said: These prophets have come to you, O Muhammad, asking, or he said: gathering to you, and calling upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to separate the gathering of nations to where Allah wills, because of the grief they are in. Creation is bridled in sweat: as for the believer, it is upon him like a cold in the head, and as for the disbeliever, death overwhelms him. He said: Isa said: Wait until I return to you. He said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went and stood beneath the Throne, and met what no chosen angel nor sent prophet met. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to Jibril to go to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and say to him: Raise your head; ask, you shall be given, and intercede, you shall be granted intercession. He said: So I was granted intercession for my Ummah, to take out of every ninety-nine persons one. He said: I kept returning to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and I did not stand a station but I was granted intercession, until Allah gave me of that when He said: O Muhammad, admit of your Ummah, of Allah's creation, whoever bore witness that there is no god but Allah for one day sincerely and died upon that...'"
"2505","2696 - Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Haddad informed us, at Isfahan, that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his saying: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Fadl al-A'raj narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Harb ibn Maymun Abu al-Khattab al-Ansari narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me: 'I am standing waiting for my Ummah crossing the Sirat when Isa came to me.' He said: He said: These prophets have come to you, O Muhammad, asking, or gathering to you, and calling upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, to separate the gathering of nations to where Allah wills, because of the grief they are in. They are bridled in sweat: as for the believer, it is upon him like a cold, and as for the disbeliever, death overwhelms him. Isa, peace be upon him, said: Wait until I return to you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went and stood beneath the Throne, and met what no chosen angel nor sent prophet met. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to Jibril, peace be upon him, to go to Muhammad and say: Raise your head; ask, you shall be given, and intercede, you shall be granted intercession. He said: So I was granted intercession for my Ummah, to take out of every ninety-nine one. I kept returning to my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, and I did not stand a station but I was granted intercession, until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gave me that when He said: O Muhammad, admit of your Ummah, of Allah's creation, whoever bore witness that there is no god but Allah for one day sincerely and died upon that. There has come in the Sahih, from the hadith of Anas, the hadith of intercession, except that in this are wordings not in that, and Allah knows best.'"
"2506","2697 - Another. The Imam Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Haddad informed us, at Isfahan, that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his saying: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili informed us: Fadl al-A'raj narrated to us: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Harb narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a funeral passed. He said: What is this funeral? They said: The funeral of so-and-so, son of so-and-so; he used to love Allah and the Messenger, act in obedience to Allah and strive in it. He said: It is binding, it is binding. And another passed, and he said: What is this? They said: The funeral of so-and-so, son of so-and-so; he used to hate Allah and His Messenger, act in disobedience to Allah and strive in it. He said: It is binding, it is binding. They said: O Messenger of Allah, your saying regarding the two funerals and the praise upon them — the first was praised with good and the other with evil — your saying regarding them, binding? He said: Yes, indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has angels on earth who speak upon the tongues of the children of Adam what is in a person of good and evil. In the Sahih there is narrated, from the narration of Thabit, similar to this hadith, but his saying: Indeed Allah has angels, to its end, is not in the narration of Thabit, and Allah knows best."
"2507","2698 - Al-Sharif Abu Muhammad Yunus ibn Yahya ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Hashimi informed us of it, in Egypt, that Abu al-Waqt Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa al-Sufi informed them: Bibi bint Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Ansari informed us: Ja'far ibn Isa ibn Muhammad al-Hulwani informed us: Abu Ja'far, meaning Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Munadi, narrated to us: Yunus, meaning Ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib, narrated to us: Harb narrated to us, from al-Nadr, from Anas, he said: I was sitting, and he mentioned in similar form, and in it: binding, binding, binding, in both places."
"2508","2699 - Another. Abu Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Qasim, known as Ibn al-Tawilah, informed us, recited to him while we listened; it was said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad informed you, and he acknowledged it: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Aziz ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Kharaqi informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Daqiqi, who is Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa al-Zamin narrated to us: Isa ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna al-Ansari, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Fingers suffice in place of the siwak.'"
"2509","2700 - Umm al-Fadl Karimah bint Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn al-Khidr informed us, recited to her at Damascus; it was said to her: Abu Abd Allah al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Rustumi informed you, by ijazah: Mahmud ibn Ja'far al-Kawsaj informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, who is Ibn Abd al-Karim al-Razi, narrated to us: al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sadir narrated to us: Isa ibn Shu'ayb informed us: Abd Allah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Fingers stand in place of the siwak.'"
"2510","2701 - Another. Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed us, at Baghdad, that Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us: Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn al-Fadl al-Katib narrated to us: Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us: Maysur ibn Khalid al-Usfuri narrated to me: Amir ibn Yasaf narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 'Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah sincerely thereby, and dies upon that, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, forbids him to the Fire.' Al-Nadr said: My father ordered us to write this hadith, and he did not order us to write any hadith other than it. Al-Daraqutni said: Amir ibn Yasaf narrates it from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith Anas did not hear from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated it from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Itban ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Anas said: Then I met Itban ibn Malik and asked him, and he narrated it to me. And it is the sound version from Anas."
"2511","2702 - Another. As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh al-Isbahani informed us, there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O man with two ears. And Asim narrated it from Anas, and it has preceded in his biography."
"2512","2703 - Another. Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-A'la al-Bawsi al-San'ani narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, promised me to admit to Paradise of my Ummah four hundred thousand.' Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Increase us, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And like this, and he joined his two palms. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Enough, O Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Leave me, O Umar; what is it to you if Allah admits us all to Paradise? Umar said: If Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wills He admits us to Paradise with one palm. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umar spoke the truth."
"2513","2704 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Mahdi al-Ubulli narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Indeed Allah promised me to admit of my Ummah to Paradise four hundred thousand.' Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Increase us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And like this also. Abu Bakr said: Increase us, O Messenger of Allah. Umar said: Enough for us, O Abu Bakr. Abu Bakr said: Leave us, O Umar; what is it to you if Allah admits us all to Paradise? Umar said: If Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wills He admits us with one palm. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He spoke the truth. It was said: Hisham narrated it from Qatadah, from Abu Bakr ibn Anas, from Abu Bakr ibn Umayr al-Ansari, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Daraqutni said: The word is what Hisham said, and Allah knows best."
"2514","2705 - Al-Nadr Abu Ubayd Allah from Anas. Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, at Baghdad, that Abu al-Fath Muflih ibn Ahmad al-Dawraqi informed them: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit informed us: al-Qasim ibn Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar informed us: Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Jabalah ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us: Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn al-Nadr, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: There was darkness in the time of Anas ibn Malik. He said: I came to Anas and said: O Abu Hamzah, did the like of this befall you in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Allah forbid; when the wind blew fiercely we hastened to the mosque fearing the Hour. Thus Abu Dawud brought it out in his Sunan."
"2515","2706 - Waqdan Abu Ya'fur from Anas. Abu al-Tahir Ismail ibn Salih ibn Yasin ibn Imran al-Shari'i informed us, at al-Shari' between Egypt and Cairo, that Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed them: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Sari al-Muqri informed us, in Egypt: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya al-Naysaburi informed us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i informed us, he said: Qutaybah informed us: Abu Awanah informed us, from Abu Ya'fur, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about wiping over the khuffs, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over them. It was said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah and Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated it from Abu Awanah as mawquf. I say: Nu'aym ibn al-Haytham raised it."
"2516","2707 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil ibn al-Husayn ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Khaffaf informed us, at Baghdad, that Abu Mansur Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur al-Bazzar informed us: Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us: Abu Muhammad Nu'aym ibn al-Haytham al-Harawi narrated to us, by dictation from his book: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ya'fur, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about wiping over the khuffs, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over them. Ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from Muhammad ibn al-Junayd, from Qutaybah."
"2517","2708 - Al-Walid ibn Zarwan from Anas. Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim al-Khabbaz informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Malih al-Raqqi narrated to me, from al-Walid ibn Zarwan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I performed wudu for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he washed his face, he took a handful of water and ran it through his beard from within, and said: 'Thus my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me.'"
"2518","2709 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu al-Wafa Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed them, while he was present: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi Ali informed us, by ijazah: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan informed us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Hasan informed us: Salih ibn Ahmad narrated to us [...]: Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us: Abu al-Malih narrated to me, from al-Walid ibn Zarwan, from Anas, in like form exactly. Abu Dawud brought it out from Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi', from Abu al-Malih al-Hasan ibn Umar."
"2519","2710 - Muhammad ibn Safi ibn Abd Allah al-Naqqash informed us, at Baghdad, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Hajji informed you, recited to him: al-Sharif Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah narrated to us: Abu Ahmad, who is Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Qasim ibn Jami' al-Dahhan, informed us: Muhammad ibn Sa'id, who is Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Isa ibn Marzuq al-Harrani, informed us: Hilal ibn al-Ala narrated to us: my father and Ibn Ja'far narrated to us, both said: Abu al-Malih narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Zarwan narrated to us, from Anas, he said: I performed wudu for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when [...] his wudu, he took a handful of water and ran it through his beard. And Abu al-Malih showed us and said: Thus my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me."
"2520","2711 - Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas from his grandfather. Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, with a chain transition."
"2521","2712 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harimi informed us, at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Bahz narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If the Hour comes while a seedling is in the hand of one of you, if he is able not to rise until he plants it, let him do so.' The wording is one, except that in the narration of Yazid is 'and he is able.' Ahmad also narrated it from Waki', from Hammad ibn Salamah. And Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated it from Hammad."
"2522","2713 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If the Hour comes while a seedling is in the hand of one of you, if he is able that the Hour not come until he plants it.' And Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated it from Hammad."
"2523","2714 - Al-Adl Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Sadaqah ibn Nasr ibn Zuhayr ibn al-Muqallid al-Harrani informed us, at Baghdad, that al-Sharif Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Makki informed them: al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i al-Makki informed us, in the Sacred Mosque: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Firas al-Abqasi al-Makki narrated to us, at Makkah: Abu al-Fadl al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani narrated to us, at Makkah: Ubayd, who is Ibn Adam ibn Abi Iyas, narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Hisham ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If the Hour comes while a seedling is in the hand of one of you, if he is able not to let it come until he plants it, let him do so.' And Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated it from Hammad."
"2524","2715 - Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Zayd ibn Anas, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If the Hour were to come while a seedling is in the hand of one of you, if one of you is able not to let it come until he plants it, let him do so.' And Abd ibn Humayd narrated it from Abu al-Walid and Arim, from Hammad ibn Salamah, in similar form."
"2525","2716 - Harun ibn Riyab. Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, recited to him while I listened, at Isfahan; it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed you, recited to her: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Sa'id Yahya ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us: Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Harun ibn Riyab, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The people of Paradise enter Paradise hairless, beardless, with kohl.'"
"2526","2717 - Yusuf ibn Hibat Allah ibn Mahmud ibn al-Tufayl informed us, at Cairo, that Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yusuf informed them, recited to him: Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali informed us, he said: It was recited to Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali: Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Khalid and Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, both said: Umar narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Harun ibn Riyab, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The people of Paradise will be raised upon the image of Adam at the birth of thirty-three years, hairless, beardless, with kohl; then they will be taken to a tree in Paradise, and inscribed in it; their garments will not wear out, nor will their youth perish.'"
"2527","2718 - Harun ibn Abi Dawud al-Habati from Anas. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Hilal ibn Abi Dawud, meaning al-Habati, Abu Hisham, narrated to us; my brother Harun ibn Abi Dawud said: and he narrated to me, he said: I came to Anas ibn Malik and said: O Abu Hamzah, the place is far, and we like to visit you. He raised his head and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Any man who visits a sick person wades in mercy; and when he sits with the sick person, mercy covers him.' He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the healthy one who visits the sick; so what is for the sick? He said: 'His sins are removed from him.' Hilal was declared trustworthy by Yahya ibn Ma'in. And in the book of Ibn Abi Hatim: Marwan instead of Harun."
"2528","2719 - Shadhrah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ala al-Khayyat al-Madini informed us, at the city of Isfahan, by my recitation to him there; I said to him: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baghban informed you, recited to him while you listened, and he acknowledged it: Abu Amr Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Mandah informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf ibn Yawah informed us, recited to him: Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Hakim al-Madini informed us, by dictation: Abu Hatim, who is Muhammad ibn Idris, narrated to us: Abu Salamah narrated to us: Hilal ibn Abi Dawud al-Habati narrated to us: my brother informed me, he said: We came to Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, visiting him, and I said to him: O Abu Hamzah, the place is far, and we like to visit you. He raised his head and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Indeed the one who visits the sick wades in mercy; and when he sits, it covers him.' It was said: O Abu Hamzah, this is for the healthy; so what is for the sick? He said: 'His sins are removed from him.'"
"2529","2720 - Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari from Anas. Abu al-Fakhr As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh and Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Abi Mansur al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi and Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Muhammad al-Ramli narrated to us, at Akka: Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray at the prayer place, meaning toward the short spear."
"2530","2721 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Rijal al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Eid at the prayer place screened by his spear."
"2531","2722 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah Sammuyah narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal informed me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Eid at the prayer place screened by his spear. And Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated it from Ibn Wahb."
"2532","2723 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Su'ud al-Busiri informed us, at Fustat of Egypt, that Abu Ja'far Yahya ibn al-Musrif ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Tammar informed them: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Ahmad ibn Nafis al-Muqri informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Bundar ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Bundar, judge of Adhana, informed us, in Egypt: Abu Tahir al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil al-Asadi al-Balisi informed us: Abu Umayyah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bazzar narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran al-Khuza'i narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at the prayer place screened by his spear. Al-Nasa'i brought it out from Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la. And Ibn Majah brought it out from Harun ibn Sa'id, both from Ibn Wahb, in similar form."
"2533","2724 - Another. Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Buhayri informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya al-Adl informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sarakhsi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-A'yan Abu al-Wazir narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed the dawn prayer on a journey would walk."
"2534","2725 - Ahmad ibn Hamzah al-Sulami informed us, at Damascus, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by ijazah; and Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed them, recited to him: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us; both said: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us: Abu al-Wazir Muhammad ibn A'yan, executor of Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed the dawn prayer on a journey would walk a little from his mount."
"2535","2726 - Another. Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Hani al-Darir narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever has two daughters or two sisters and shelters them and suffices them until they separate or die, I and he will be in Paradise like these two,' and he separated between his fingers. In the Sahih there is narrated from the hadith of Anas similar to this."
"2536","2727 - Another. Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Musarrih al-Harrani narrated to us: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Hafs ibn Maysarah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Days and nights will not pass until the happiest of people with this world is Luka' ibn Luka'.' Abu Hatim al-Busti brought it out from Ahmad ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Malik, from his uncle al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik, in similar form."
"2537","2728 - Another. Abu Ismail Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Mashadhah al-Isbahani informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Ya'la Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni informed us: Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Musa al-Simsar narrated to us: the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us: Asim ibn Suwayd narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Usayd ibn al-Hudayr al-Ashhali came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a chain transition."
"2538","2729 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi and Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us, at Baghdad, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun informed us: Ali, who is Ibn Umar al-Harbi, informed us: Ja'far, who is Ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, narrated to us: Asim ibn Suwayd ibn Jariyah al-Ansari narrated to us, at Quba: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Usayd ibn al-Hudayr, the Naqib, al-Ashhali, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: He spoke to him about a household of Banu Zafar, most of them women, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportion to them from something he apportioned among the people. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'You left us, O Usayd, until what was in our hands was gone; when you hear of food that has come to me, come to me and mention to me the people of that house, or mention them to me.' He said: He remained as long as Allah willed. He said: Then there came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) food from Khaybar, barley and dates. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportioned among the people. He said: Then he apportioned among the Ansar generously. He said: Then he apportioned to that house generously. Usayd said to him gratefully: May Allah reward you, O Messenger of Allah, with the best reward — or good — Asim doubted. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'And you, company of Ansar, may Allah reward you with good, or with the best reward; for all of you, as far as I know, are chaste and patient. You will see after me preference over yourselves and in command; so be patient until you meet me at the Hawd.' This is the wording of Ibn al-Sabbah. The hadith of Ali ibn Hujr says: Usayd ibn Hudayr al-Ashhali came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he had apportioned food, and mentioned to him a household of the Ansar of Banu Zafar in need; most of that household were women. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'You left us, O Usayd, until what was in our hands was gone; when you hear of something that has come to us, mention to me the people of that house.' He said: After that there came to him food from Khaybar, barley or dates. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) apportioned among the people, apportioned among the Ansar generously, and apportioned to the people of that house generously. He said: Usayd ibn Hudayr said to him gratefully: May Allah reward you, O Prophet of Allah, on our behalf with the best reward — or he said: good. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'And you, company of Ansar, may Allah reward you with the best reward — or he said: good; for you, as far as I know, are chaste and patient. You will see after me preference in command and apportionment; so be patient until you meet me at the Hawd.' Al-Nasa'i brought it out from Ali ibn Hujr. And Ibn Hibban narrated it in his book from Abd Allah ibn Qahtabah, from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah."
"2539","2730 - Another. Sa'id ibn Rawh ibn Abrawayh al-Mu'allim al-Salhaniyy informed us, at Isfahan, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Mustamli informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Hamdan informed us: Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi' informed us: Muhammad ibn Khallad narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The gray hair that was on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was seventeen hairs."
"2540","2731 - Another. Abu al-Fath Mas'ud ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Jandani informed us, by my brother's recitation to him while I listened, may Allah have mercy on them both; he said to him: Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed you, and he acknowledged it: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Mada'ini, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, with a chain transition. And Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us, by permission, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Mada'ini narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: There was mentioned in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a sinking of the earth toward the east. Some people said: O Messenger of Allah, will land in which are Muslims be sunk? He said: 'Yes, when most of its people are filth.' Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Yahya except Anas ibn Iyad; al-Musayyibi is alone in it."
"2541","2732 - Another. Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani informed us that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Isa ibn Muhammad al-Simsar al-Wasiti narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Sufyan al-Madani informed us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'This Ummah will split into seventy-three sects, all of them in the Fire except one.' They said: What is that sect? He said: 'What I am upon today and my companions.' Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Abd Allah ibn Sufyan."
"2542","2733 - Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i from Anas (Muslim narrated one hadith from him). Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yazid, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who had a wife under him and divorced her thrice; she then married after him a man who divorced her before consummating with her — is she lawful to her first husband? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'No, until the other has tasted of her honey and she has tasted of his honey.'"
"2543","2734 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id al-Balkhi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Dinar al-Tahi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yazid, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who divorced his wife thrice; she married a husband who died before consummating with her — may the first marry her? He said: No, until he tastes her honey."
"2544","2735 - Abu Ya'la said: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us also, from Yahya ibn Yazid, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in similar form. And Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Dinar."
"2545","2736 - Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us, by permission, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym al-Isbahani informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Muslim, who is Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Kashshi, narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Dinar al-Tahi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'She is not lawful to the first until the second tastes her honey.' Al-Tabarani said: Muhammad ibn Dinar is alone in it."
"2546","2737 - Abu al-Tayyah Yazid ibn Humayd from Anas. As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us, at Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Qazzaz narrated to us: Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Render the trust to one who entrusted you, and do not betray one who betrayed you.' Ibn Adi narrated it in al-Kamil from Ibn Qutaybah, from Muhammad ibn Nuh al-Hadhdha and Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Ramli, from Ayyub ibn Suwayd, from Ibn Shawdhab, and said: It is munkar by this chain."
"2547","2738 - Yazid ibn Abi Zuhayr from Anas (Ibn Abi Hatim said: Yazid ibn Zuhayr), and Allah knows best. Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym al-Isbahani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud Sammuyah informed us: Ali and Yahya narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail narrated to us — and Yahya said: from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail — from Harb ibn Zuhayr, from Yazid ibn Abi Zuhayr al-Duba'i, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Hajj is the path of Allah; expenditure in it is multiplied seven hundredfold.' This is the wording of Ali."
"2548","2739 - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isbahani informed us, by permission, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail, from Harb ibn Zuhayr, from Yazid al-Duba'i, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Hajj is the path of Allah; expenditure in it: the dirham for seven hundred.' Al-Tabarani said: Thus Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail narrated it; Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated it from Harb ibn Zuhayr, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father; he said: None narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail except Muhammad ibn Bishr; Husayn ibn Abd al-Awwal is alone in it. I say: Husayn was not alone in it."
"2549","2740 - Yazid ibn Abi Nushbah from Anas. Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Nushbah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Three are of the foundation of Islam: withholding from one who says there is no god but Allah — not declaring him a disbeliever for a sin, nor expelling him from Islam for a deed; jihad continues since Allah sent me until the last of my Ummah fights the Dajjal — neither the tyranny of a tyrant nor the justice of a just one diverts it; and faith in all the decrees.' Abu Dawud brought it out from Sa'id ibn Mansur, from Abu Mu'awiyah, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn Abi Nushbah, from Anas."
"2550","2741 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, both said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, with its chain, in like form — except that he said: since He sent me; and in it: neither the tyranny of a tyrant nullifies it; and the rest is like it."
"2551","2742 - Abu Asma al-Sayqal from Anas. Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Asma al-Sayqal, from Anas, he said: We went out crying out with Hajj; when we arrived at Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to make it Umrah. Then he said: 'Had I faced of my affair what I have turned back upon, I would have made it Umrah; but I drove the sacrificial animal and joined.'"
"2552","2743 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman, who is Ibn Iqal al-Harrani, narrated to us: Abu Ja'far al-Buqayli narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Asma, from Anas, he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) crying out."
"2553","2744 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Asma al-Sayqal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: We went out crying out with Hajj; when we arrived at Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered us to make it Umrah, and said: 'Had I —' and al-Buqayli said: 'Indeed if I had faced of my affair what I have turned back upon, I would have made it Umrah; but I drove the sacrificial animal and joined Hajj and Umrah.' Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik, from Zuhayr."
"2554","2745 - Abu Bakr ibn al-Nadr ibn Anas from his grandfather. Abu al-Mafakhir Uthman ibn Mahmud, known as Habbuwayh, informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baghban informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his saying: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mansur Zaj narrated to us: al-Nadr narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Ubayd informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Nadr ibn Anas informed me, he said: I was with Anas and he prayed with them the noon prayer, letting them hear his recitation in the first rak'ah. When he finished his prayer, he turned to them with his face and said: Deliberately I let you hear my recitation of these two surahs; I prayed with the Messenger of Allah the noon prayer and he recited these two surahs: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming. Al-Nasa'i brought it out from Muhammad ibn Shuja', from Abu Ubaydah, from Abd Allah ibn Ubayd. And similar to this is narrated from Qatadah, Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, mentioned in the narration of Qatadah."
"2555","2746 - Abu Talhah al-Asadi from Anas. Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu Muhammad Hamzah ibn al-Abbas ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Alawi informed them, while he was present: Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Makfuf narrated to us: Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Sharik ibn al-Fadl ibn Khalid al-Asadi al-Walibi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Yunus al-Yarbu'i narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Hatib, from Abu Talhah al-Asadi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and saw a lofty dome. He said: What is this? His companions said to him: It belongs to a man of the Ansar. He said: He remained silent and kept it in himself until when its owner entered and greeted the people, he turned away from him. He did that with him repeatedly, until the man recognized anger in his face and turning away from him. He complained of that to his companions and said: By Allah, I find the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed; I do not know what has happened to me and what I have done? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and saw your dome, and asked about it, and we informed him. The man returned to his dome and demolished it until he leveled it with the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day and did not see it. He said: What happened to the dome that was here? They said: Its owner complained to us of your turning away from him, and we informed him, and he demolished it. He said to us: 'Indeed every building built is a calamity upon its owner on the Day of Resurrection, except what is indispensable [...]'."
"2556","2747 - Abu Abd Allah al-Asadi from Anas. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, there, that Abu al-Qasim ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me: Abu Abd Allah al-Asadi narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Fear the supplication of the wronged, even if he is a disbeliever, for there is no veil before it.'"
"2557","2748 - And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt.'"
"2558","2749 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ishaq Abu Zakariyya al-Saylahini narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Misri narrated to us, from Abu Abd Allah al-Asadi, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Fear the supplication of the wronged, even if it is from a disbeliever.'"
"2559","2750 - Abu Isam from Anas (Muslim narrated one hadith from him). Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us: Hisham Sahib al-Dastawa'i narrated to us, from Abu Isam, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm Sulaym while in the house was a hanging waterskin; he took it and drank from its mouth while standing. He said: Umm Sulaym cut the mouth of the waterskin, and it is with us. It is narrated from al-Bara ibn Zayd, son of the daughter of Anas, from Anas, from his mother."
"2560","2751 - Abu Amr ibn Anas from his father. Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us: Abu Musa al-Zamin narrated to us: Isa ibn Shu'ayb al-Darir Abu al-Fadl narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to me, from Abu Amr ibn Anas ibn Malik, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever restrains his anger, Allah restrains His punishment from him; whoever stores his tongue, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, covers his nakedness; and whoever apologizes to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, He excuses him.' And Abu Ya'la also narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Zayd ibn al-Hubab, from Ibn Sulayman, from Abu Amr, freedman of Anas ibn Malik, that he heard Anas ibn Malik."
"2561","1 - Those named Sa'sa'ah: Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Husayn ibn Ubadah ibn Nazzal ibn Mu'ah ibn Ubayd ibn al-Harith ibn Amr ibn Sa'd ibn Zayd Manah ibn Tamim ibn Murrah, uncle of al-Ahnaf — he used to reside at Basra — may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, uncle of al-Farazdaq, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he recited to him: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.' He said: It suffices me; I care not, or I shall hear no other."
"2562","2 - And with it my father narrated to me: Abu Amir narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan: Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, uncle of al-Farazdaq, narrated to us, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard him recite this verse, and he mentioned its meaning."
"2563","3 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to me: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, uncle of al-Ahnaf, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard him recite this verse: 'So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it.' I said: By Allah, I care not to hear other than it; it suffices me, it suffices me. In the narration of Yazid and Abu Amir: uncle of al-Farazdaq. In the narration of Hudbah: uncle of al-Ahnaf. I think one of the two sayings is a mistake, for the lineage of al-Farazdaq is not this, and Allah knows best."
"2564","4 - Sa'sa'ah ibn Najiyah ibn Iqal ibn Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Mujashi' ibn Darim — grandfather of al-Farazdaq the poet, al-Mujashi'i — he used to reside at Basra — may Allah be pleased with him. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Marzuq al-Basri narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Harb al-Hilali narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq ibn Dahah al-Muzani narrated to me: Iqal ibn Shabbah ibn Iqal ibn Sa'sa'ah al-Mujashi'i narrated to me, he said: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from his father Sa'sa'ah, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, sometimes a surplus remains which I store for a calamity and the traveler. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, the nearest, the nearest.'"
"2565","5 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Marzuq informed us: Abd Allah ibn Harb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn As'ad, nicknamed Ibn Dahah, narrated to me, he said: Iqal ibn Shabbah ibn Iqal ibn Sa'sa'ah ibn Najiyah al-Mujashi'i narrated to me: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from his father Sa'sa'ah ibn Najiyah al-Mujashi'i, he said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, sometimes a surplus remains for me which I store for a calamity and the traveler. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, the nearest, the nearest.'"
"2566","6 - Another. Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Harb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Iqal ibn Shabbah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Guard what is between your jaws and between your legs.' He said: I turned away saying: It suffices me."
"2567","7 - Those named Safwan: Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf ibn Wahb ibn Hudhafah ibn Jumah ibn Amr ibn Husays ibn Ka'b, Abu Wahb al-Jumahi — may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Sa'id, meaning Ibn Abi Arubah, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Tariq ibn Muraqqa', from Safwan ibn Umayyah, that a man stole a cloak, and he raised him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered his cutting. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have pardoned him. He said: 'Why was this not before you brought him to me, O Abu Wahb?' So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut him."
"2568","8 - And with it my father narrated to me: Rawh narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Abd Allah ibn Safwan, from his father, that Safwan ibn Umayyah ibn Khalaf was told: Ruined is he who did not emigrate. He said: I said: I shall not reach family until I come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I rode my mount and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they claim that ruined is he who did not emigrate? He said: 'Not at all, O Abu Wahb; return to the valleys of Makkah.' He said: While I was sleeping, the thief came, took my garment from under my head, and I caught him. I brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This stole my garment. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to be cut. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is not what I intended; it is charity upon him. He said: Why not before you brought him to me."
"2569","9 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Abbas ibn Hamdan al-Hanafi narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us: Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Humayd, son of the sister of Safwan ibn Umayyah, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: I was sleeping in the mosque upon a khamisah of mine worth thirty dirhams. A man came to me and snatched it. The man was seized and brought to the Prophet, and he ordered him to be cut. I came to him and said to him: Do you cut him for thirty dirhams? It is his. He said: 'Why was this not before you brought him to me.'"
"2570","10 - And with it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Ibn Shihab, from Safwan ibn Abd Allah ibn Safwan, from his grandfather, he said: It was said to Safwan: Indeed whoever did not emigrate is ruined. He called for his mount, rode it, and came to Madinah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'What brought you, O Abu Wahb?' He said: It reached me that there is no religion for one with no emigration. He said: 'Return to the valleys of Makkah.' He returned, entered the mosque, and pillowed his cloak. A man came and stole it. He was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: O Messenger of Allah, this stole my cloak. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his cutting. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my cloak did not reach that for which a man's hand is cut; I have made it charity upon him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Why not before you brought him to me.' Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Husayn ibn Muhammad, from Sulayman ibn Qarm, from Simak, from Ju'ayd, son of the sister of Safwan, from Safwan; and from Affan, from Wuhayb, from Ibn Tawus, from Umayyah, from Safwan, in similar form. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Faris, from Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah, and in it: Jumayd, son of the sister of Safwan. Abu Dawud said: Za'idah narrated it from Simak, from Ju'ayd ibn Hujayr, he said: Safwan slept. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim, from Amr, from Asbat, with its chain, in similar form; and from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahim, from Asad ibn Musa, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Safwan, in similar form; and from Hilal ibn al-Ala, from his father, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Safwan, in similar form; and from Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from his father. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Shabbabah ibn Sawwar, from Malik ibn Anas, from al-Zuhri, from Abd Allah ibn Safwan, from his father, in its meaning."
"2571","11 - Another. Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them; it was said to him: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed you: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us: Shadhan and Yahya narrated to us, both said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Umayyah ibn Safwan, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed coats of mail of iron from Safwan on the day of Hunayn. He said: O Muhammad, guaranteed; some of them were lost. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If you wish, we shall compensate you for it.' He said: No, I am more desirous of Islam than that."
"2572","12 - And with it Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Nasr ibn Ata narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Ata, from Ya'la ibn Safwan ibn Umayyah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'When my messengers come to you, give them such and such.' He said: I think thirty coats of mail. I said: Is the loan to be returned? He said: Yes."
"2573","13 - The Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qurashi informed us that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Yazid narrated to us: Sharik ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Umayyah ibn Safwan, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed coats of mail from him on the day of Hunayn. He said: By seizure, O Muhammad? He said: 'Rather a guaranteed loan.' He said: Some of them were lost, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) offered him to compensate him for it. He said: Today, O Messenger of Allah, I am more desirous of Islam. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, like the narration of Ahmad ibn Mani', except that he said: coats of mail, and with him: to guarantee it for him. And Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad and Salamah ibn Shabib, from Yazid ibn Harun. Abu Dawud said: This is the narration of Yazid at Baghdad, and in his narration at Wasit other than here; and from Abu Bakr, from Jarir, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from some people of the family of Abd Allah ibn Safwan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'O Safwan, do you have weapons?' the hadith; and from Musaddad, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay', from Ata, from some people of the family of Safwan, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed, and he mentioned its meaning. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Sharik, with its chain, in similar form; and from Ahmad ibn Sulayman, from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, from Isra'il, from Abd al-Aziz, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan ibn Umayyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed coats of mail from Safwan, and he mentioned it."
"2574","14 - Another. Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Daqqaq informed us: Abd Allah, who is al-Baghawi, narrated to us: Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Umar al-Qawariri, narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, whose name is Abd al-Rahman, from Amir ibn Malik, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Plague, the belly, drowning and childbirth are martyrdom.'"
"2575","15 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: al-Taymi, meaning Sulayman, narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, meaning al-Nahdi, from Amir ibn Malik, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, he said: Plague, the belly, drowning and childbirth are martyrdom. Abu Uthman narrated it to him repeatedly, and once he raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2576","16 - And with it my father narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sulayman, meaning al-Taymi, informed us, from Abu Uthman, meaning al-Nahdi, from Amir ibn Malik, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Plague is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, the belly and childbirth.' Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abi Adi, from Sulayman, like the narration of Yahya ibn Sa'id. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abu Qudamah Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'id, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, like the narration of Imam Ahmad from Yahya."
"2577","17 - Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi — may Allah be pleased with him. Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman, Muhammad ibn Ja'far, Abu Dawud and Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us, all said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Salamah, from Safwan, he said: A Jew said to his companion: Take us to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a chain transition."
"2578","18 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, Abu Khalifah and Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Sawrah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, all said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salamah, from Safwan ibn Assal, that two Jews, one of them said to his companion: Let us go to this Prophet. He said: Do not say to him Prophet, for if he hears you he will have four eyes. They went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: 'And We gave Musa nine clear signs.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Do not associate anything with Allah, do not kill the soul which Allah forbade except by right, do not commit adultery, do not steal, do not walk with an innocent one to a ruler to kill him, do not consume usury, do not slander a chaste woman, do not flee from battle; and upon you especially, O Jews, not to transgress on the Sabbath.' They kissed his hand and said: We bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: What prevents you from following me? They said: Dawud prayed that there remain among his progeny a prophet, and we fear if we follow you the Jews will kill us. The wording of the hadith of Abu al-Walid; the mention of magic fell from this narration. The narration of Muhammad ibn Bashshar: Take us to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we ask him about this verse: 'And We gave Musa nine clear signs.' He said: Do not say to him Prophet, for if he hears you he will have four eyes. They asked him, and he said: 'Do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill the soul which Allah forbade except by right, do not practice magic, do not consume usury, do not walk with an innocent one to a ruler to kill him, do not slander a chaste woman' — or he said: 'flee from battle' — Shu'bah the doubter — 'and you, O Jews, upon you especially not to transgress on the Sabbath.' They kissed his hand and his foot. Both said: We bear witness that you are a prophet. He said: What prevents you from submitting? He said: Dawud prayed that there remain among his progeny a prophet, and we fear the Jews will kill us."
"2579","19 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, with a chain transition. 20 - He said: And Yazid narrated to us: Shu'bah informed us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Salamah narrate from Safwan ibn Assal. Yazid said: al-Muradi. He said: A Jew said to his companion: Go to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yazid said: To this Prophet, until we ask him about this verse: 'And We gave Musa nine clear signs.' He said: Do not say to him Prophet, for if he hears you he will have four eyes. They asked him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill the soul which Allah forbade except by right, do not practice magic, do not consume usury, do not walk with an innocent one to a ruler to kill him, do not slander a chaste woman' — or he said: 'flee from battle' — Shu'bah the doubter — 'and you, O Jews, upon you especially do not transgress.' Yazid said: 'Nor transgress on the Sabbath.' They kissed his hand and his foot. Yazid said: They kissed his hands and his feet and said: We bear witness that you are a prophet. He said: 'What prevents you from following me?' Both said: Dawud prayed that there remain among his progeny a prophet, and we fear — Yazid said: if we submit — the Jews will kill us. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Shu'bah, in similar form. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Ibn Idris and Abu Usamah, from Shu'bah, and said: Hasan sahih hadith; and from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Abu Dawud, Yazid ibn Harun and Abu al-Walid, from Shu'bah, in similar form, and said: sahih. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Ibn Idris, from Shu'bah; and from Abu Kurayb and Abu Qudamah, from Ibn Idris. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ibn Idris, Ghundar and Abu Usamah, from Shu'bah, in part, in the mention of kissing."
"2580","21 - Another. Abu Rawh al-Harawi informed us, there, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi informed us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim, with a chain transition. 22 - Abu Bakr said: And Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us: Asim narrated to us, with a chain transition. 23 - He said: And Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi asking him about wiping over the khuffs. He said: What brought you, O Zirr? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: O Zirr, the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks. He said: I said: Something occurred in myself about wiping over the khuffs after relieving oneself, and you were a man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say anything about that? He said: Yes, he used to order us when we were on travel to not remove our khuffs three days and their nights except from janabah, but from stool and urine. This is the hadith of al-Makhzumi. Ahmad ibn Abdah said in his hadith: He said: It has reached me that the angels lower their wings."
"2581","24 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi. He said: What brought you? I said: I came seeking knowledge. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'There is no one who goes out of his house seeking knowledge except that the angels lay their wings for him, pleased with what he does.' I said: I came to ask you about wiping over the khuffs. He said: Yes, I was in the army which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent, and he ordered us to wipe over the khuffs when we had put them on in purity, three when we traveled, and a night when we stayed, and not to remove them for stool, urine or sleep, and not to remove them except from janabah. He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Indeed in the west is a door opened for repentance, seventy years' journey; it is not closed until the sun rises from its west.' 25 - And with it, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, with a chain transition."
"2582","26 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad also informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us: Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: I heard Sufyan ibn Uyaynah say: Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: What brought you? I said: I came seeking knowledge. He said: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks. He said: I said: There occurred in myself, or in my chest, wiping over the khuffs after stool and urine; did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that? He said: Yes, he used to order us when we were on travel to not remove our khuffs three days and their nights except from janabah, but from stool, urine and sleep. I said: Did you hear him mention love? He said: Yes, while we were with him on a journey, a Bedouin called him with a loud voice and said: O Muhammad. He answered him in like manner of his speech: Hah. And he said: What do you think of a man who loved a people but has not joined them? He said: 'A person is with whom he loved.' Then he kept narrating to us: 'Indeed before the west is a door which Allah opens for repentance, the breadth of its passage forty years; it is not closed until the sun rises,' meaning from it. The wording of the hadith of Muhammad ibn Asim. In the narration of Abd al-Razzaq he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal. He said: What brought you? I said: Seeking knowledge. With him: I said: There occurred in my chest wiping over the khuffs after stool and urine, and you were a man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I came to ask you about that; did you hear from him anything about that? He said: Yes. With him: or we were travelers. With him: I said: Did you hear him mention love? With him: with a loud voice — or he said: resonant — Ibn Uyaynah doubted. He said: With him: He answered him in like manner of his speech, and said: Mah. He said: What do you think. With him: but did not join them. He said: 'He is on the Day of Resurrection with whom he loved.' He said: He kept narrating to us until he said: 'Indeed before the west is a door, the breadth of its passage seventy years; Allah opened it for repentance the day He created the heavens and the earth, and He does not close it until the sun rises from its direction.'"
"2583","27 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali al-Sufi and Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Ma'mun informed us: Ali ibn Umar, who is al-Harbi, informed us: Abu Khubayb, who is al-Abbas ibn Ahmad al-Birti, narrated to us: Sawwar narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal and stood at his door. He came out to me and said: What brought you? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks. What do you ask about? I said: About wiping over the khuffs. He said: When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on travel, he ordered us not to remove it three, except from janabah, but from stool, urine or sleep. He said: A man came to him and called with a loud voice: What do you think of a man who loved a people but did not come to them? He said: 'You are with whom you loved.'"
"2584","28 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Su'ud al-Busiri informed us, in Egypt, that Murshid ibn Yahya informed them: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Naysaburi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh informed us: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us: Amr ibn Ali and Ismail ibn Mas'ud informed us, both said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim, from Safwan ibn Assal, he said: When we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on travel, he ordered us not to remove it three, except from janabah, but from stool, urine and sleep."
"2585","29 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I went in the morning to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi intending to ask him about wiping over the khuffs. He said: What brought you? I said: Seeking knowledge. He said: Shall I not give you glad tidings? I said: Yes. He raised the hadith, he said: 'The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks.' Then I asked him about wiping over the khuffs. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The traveler wipes over the khuffs three days and their nights, from urine, stool or sleep, except from janabah.' Then he began narrating to us; he said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, a Bedouin called him with a loud voice: O Muhammad, O Muhammad, O Muhammad. We said: Lower your voice, for you were forbidden to raise your voice. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him in like manner of what he heard from him, and said: Here I am. Then he asked him about love: about a person who loves a people but has not joined them? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'A person is with whom he loved.' Then he began narrating to us and said: The door of repentance is opened from before the west, its breadth seventy years' journey; it is not closed until the sun rises from before it. Then he recited this verse: 'Do they await but that the angels come to them,' to the end of the verse."
"2586","30 - The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Saffar informed us, at Naysabur, that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us: al-Mu'ammal ibn al-Hasan ibn Isa informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar informed us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, he said: I came to Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi. He said: What brought you? I said: I came seeking knowledge. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no one who goes out of his house seeking knowledge except that the angels lay their wings for him, pleased with what he does. He said: I came to ask you about wiping over the khuffs. He said: Yes, I was in the army which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent, and he ordered us to wipe over the khuffs when we had put them on in purity, three when we traveled, and a night when we stayed, and not to remove them for stool or urine, and not to remove them except from janabah. And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed in the west is a door opened for repentance, seventy years' journey; it is not closed until the sun rises toward it."
"2587","31 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf informed us, in his book — and my maternal uncle the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us from him — that Abu Ghalib Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Karkhi informed them: Abu Tahir Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Mu'addib informed us: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ishaq al-Sawwaf informed us: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman, who is al-Muqri, narrated to us: Sa'id, who is Ibn Abi Ayyub, narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Marzuq narrated to me, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi; he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Allah opened a door for repentance from the west, seventy years' journey; it is not closed until the sun rises from its direction.' Many imams narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud; among them one who mentioned part of it, and among them one who narrated it in full. Sufyan, Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, Za'idah, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah, Hammam ibn Yahya ibn al-Harith, Abu al-Ahwas, Ikrimah ibn Ibrahim, Abu Awanah, Mis'ar ibn Kidam, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, Amr ibn Qays al-Mula'i, Mubarak ibn Fadalah, Khalid ibn Kathir al-Hamdani, Malik ibn Mighwal, Ali ibn Salih, Rawh ibn al-Qasim, Shayban, Sa'id al-Jurayri, Salih ibn Salih, Habib ibn Hassan, Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' al-Yuhmadi, and others narrated it from him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar; and from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; and from Yahya ibn Adam, from Sufyan, from Asim; and from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah; and from Hasan ibn Musa, from Hammad ibn Zayd, in similar form. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ibn Abi Umar, from Sufyan; and from Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi, from Hammad ibn Zayd, both from Asim, in similar form, and said: Hasan sahih hadith; and from Hannad, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Asim, part of it (wiping), and said: Hasan sahih hadith. He narrated: A man loud-voiced came and said: O Muhammad, a man loves a people... the hadith abridged, from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, from Yahya ibn Adam, from Sufyan; and from Ahmad ibn Abdah, from Hammad ibn Zayd, and said: sahih hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawir, from Hammad, from Asim, and in it there is no wiping; and from Qutaybah, from Sufyan (wiping); and from Ahmad ibn Sulayman, from Yahya ibn Adam, from Sufyan al-Thawri, Malik ibn Mighwal, Zuhayr, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash and Ibn Uyaynah, from Asim; and from Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shu'bah; and from Amr ibn Ali and Ismail ibn Mas'ud, from Yazid ibn Zuray', from Shu'bah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, from Isra'il, from Asim (the story of repentance); and from Abu Bakr, from Sufyan (the story of wiping). There is narrated 'There is no one who goes out seeking knowledge' to his saying 'pleased with what he does,' from Muhammad ibn Yahya. Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih as we mentioned it. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated 'O Muhammad, with a loud voice' from al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Ma'shar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Bajali, from Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah, from Asim. He narrated his saying: What brought you? to his saying 'pleased with what he does,' from Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah, from Muhammad ibn Yahya and Muhammad ibn Rafi', from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar. He narrated the mention of wiping from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar. He narrated the mention of knowledge from Abu Ya'la, from Harun ibn Ma'ruf, from Sufyan, in similar form."
"2588","32 - Another. Abu Tahir ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yunus and Affan narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Abu Rawq Atiyyah ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Abu al-Gharif narrated to us. Affan said: Abu al-Gharif Ubayd Allah ibn Khalifah, from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in a detachment and said: 'Raid in the name of Allah, in the path of Allah; do not defraud, do not betray, do not mutilate, do not kill a child. For the traveler three wipings over the khuffs, and for the resident a day and a night.' Affan said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me."
"2589","33 - Abu al-Majd al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us: Abu Rawq Atiyyah ibn al-Harith al-Hamdani narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Gharif narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Assal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us as a detachment and said: 'Go in the name of Allah; fight the enemies of Allah; do not defraud, do not betray, do not mutilate, do not kill a child. Let one of you, when traveling, when he has put his feet in while pure, wipe three days and their nights; and if resident, a day and a night.' Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Harun ibn Abd Allah. Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, both from Abu Usamah, besides what is at its end of the mention of wiping. Abu al-Gharif: Abu Hatim said: They spoke about him; al-Bukhari mentioned him and mentioned nothing about him. The narration of al-Nasa'i by his route strengthens his case. Abu Hatim did not clarify who spoke about him, nor clarify what the criticism is. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Surayj, from Abd al-Wahid, in similar form."
"2590","34 - Another. Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Humayd ibn Suhayl al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, at Baghdad: Muhammad ibn Habban al-Basri narrated to us: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us: al-Sa'q ibn Hazn narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Basri narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, he said: Safwan ibn Assal narrated to me, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque reclining upon a red cloak of his. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I came seeking knowledge. He said: 'The seeker of knowledge is indeed surrounded by the angels with their wings; then some of them mount upon others until they rise to the lowest heaven, out of their love for what he seeks.' He said: 'What did you come seeking?' Safwan said: O Messenger of Allah, we keep traveling between Makkah and Madinah; what do you think about wiping over the khuffs? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Three days and their nights for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident.'"
"2591","35 - Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us, both said: Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us: al-Sa'q ibn Hazn narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi narrated: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque reclining upon a red cloak of his. I said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I came seeking knowledge. He said: Welcome to the seeker of knowledge; the seeker of knowledge is indeed surrounded by the angels, and they shade him with their wings; then some of them mount upon others until they reach the lowest heaven, out of their love for what he seeks. What did you come seeking? He said: Safwan said: O Messenger of Allah, we keep traveling between Makkah and Madinah; give us a ruling about wiping over the khuffs. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: 'Three days for the traveler, and a day and a night for the resident.' Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali al-Qadi, from Shayban ibn Farrukh."
"2592","36 - Another. My maternal uncle the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Abu Zur'ah Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Tahir al-Maqdisi informed them, recited to him: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn al-Haytham al-Muqawwimi informed us: al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Mundhir al-Khatib informed us: Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Salamah ibn Bahr al-Qattan informed us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Majah narrated to us: Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Uqbah narrated to us, he said: Hudhayfah ibn Abi Hudhayfah al-Azdi narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Assal, he said: I poured water for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for wudu in travel and residence. Thus Ibn Majah narrated it."
"2593","37 - Abu Muhammad Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Katib al-Baghdadi informed us of it, there, that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them, recited to him: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Busri informed us, recited to him: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas al-Mukhallis informed us, by ijazah. 38 - Ibn al-Samarqandi said: And Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Allanah informed us, by ijazah, he said: Abu Tahir al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa'id, narrated to us: Bishr ibn Adam, son of the daughter of Azhar al-Samman, narrated to us, at Basra: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Uqbah al-Qaysi narrated to us, he said: Hudhayfah ibn Abi Hudhayfah al-Azdi narrated to me, from Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, he said: I poured water for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for wudu in travel and residence, and he used to wipe over the khuffs."
"2594","39 - Safwan ibn Qudamah — may Allah be pleased with him. Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim al-Sam'ani informed us, at Marw, that Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Furawi informed them: Fatimah bint Abi Ali al-Daqqaq informed us: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan informed us: Abu Awanah Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: Hafs ibn Umar al-Sayyari narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ali Karraz narrated to us: Mahdi ibn Musa ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from his father, from Safwan ibn Qudamah, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I love you. He said: 'A person is with whom he loved.' Thus Abu Awanah brought it out in his Sahih. I did not see in the Tarikh of al-Bukhari nor the book of Ibn Abi Hatim any mention of Safwan ibn Qudamah, nor of any of the men of this chain. Musa ibn Harun al-Hammal narrated it from Musa ibn Maymun ibn Musa al-Mara'i, from his father Maymun, from his father, from his grandfather Abd al-Rahman ibn Safwan, he said: My father Safwan emigrated to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged to him upon Islam, and said: I love you, O Messenger of Allah... and he mentioned it. Likewise Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani narrated it from Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Anbar al-Basri, from Musa ibn Maymun."
"2595","40 - Safwan ibn Makhramah al-Zuhri — father of al-Qasim, brother of al-Miswar — may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Waki' narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Salman, from al-Qasim ibn Safwan, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Delay the noon prayer, for the severity of heat is from the breath of Hell.'"
"2596","41 - And with it my father narrated to me: Ya'la narrated to us: Abu Ismail, meaning Bashir, narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Safwan al-Zuhri, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Delay the noon prayer, for heat is from the breath of Hell.'"
"2597","42 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Isbahani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Bashir ibn Salman narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Safwan, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Delay the noon prayer, for the severity of heat is from the breath of Hell.' It has a witness in Sahih al-Bukhari from the narration of Abu Salih, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."
"2598","43 - Silah ibn al-Harith al-Ghifari — may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh: al-Harith ibn Shaddad al-San'ani narrated to me, that Abu Salih Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ghifari informed him, that Sulaym ibn Itr al-Tujibi used to address the people while standing. Silah ibn al-Harith al-Ghifari, who is among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said to him: By Allah, we neither abandoned the covenant of our Prophet nor severed our kinship until you and your companions stood among us."
"2599","44 - Al-Sunabih, and it is said: al-Sunabihi ibn al-A'sar al-Ahmasi — may Allah be pleased with him. Abu Tahir ibn al-Ma'tush informed us, at Baghdad, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ismail: I heard Qays say: I heard al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Indeed I am your predecessor at the Hawd, and I shall vie with the nations through you; so do not fight one another after me.'"
"2600","45 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Ishaq al-Jabiri al-Mawsili informed us, at Basra, recited to him: Muhammad ibn Ahmad, who is Ibn Abi al-Muthanna, narrated to us: Ja'far, meaning Ibn Awn, narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I heard al-Sunabih say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Indeed I am your predecessor at the Hawd, and I shall vie with the nations through you; so do not fight one another after me.'"
"2601","46 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Bakr, who is Ibn Abi Shaybah, narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak and Waki' narrated to us, from Ismail, from Qays, from al-Sunabihi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'I am a predecessor at the Hawd, and I shall vie with the nations through you; so do not fight one another after me.'"
"2602","47 - And with it Abu Bakr narrated to us: Ibn Numayr and Abu Usamah narrated to us, both said: Ismail narrated to us, from Qays, from al-Sunabihi al-Ahmasi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in like form. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Numayr, from his father and Muhammad ibn Bishr, both from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, from al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid. Al-Daraqutni mentioned al-Sunabih ibn al-A'sar among what the inclusion of his hadith requires upon the doctrine of al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"2603","48 - Suhayb ibn Sinan ibn Amr al-Namiri Abu Yahya, known as al-Rumi — the Romans had captured him — freedman of Banu Taym — may Allah be pleased with him. Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us, at Isfahan, that his grandfather Ghanim ibn Khalid informed them: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa ibn Shammah informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Nabil, owner of the cloak, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Suhayb, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and I greeted him, and he returned to me by gesture; and he said: I know only that he said: by gesture with his finger."
"2604","49 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, at Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Yazid al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, with a chain transition. 50 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us: Bukayr ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Nabil, owner of the cloak, from Ibn Umar, from Suhayb, he said: I passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was praying, and I greeted him, and he returned to me by gesture. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hajjaj ibn Muhammad, from al-Layth, like the narration of Isa ibn Hammad. Abu Dawud narrated it from Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Mawhab and Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from al-Layth. Al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah. Al-Tirmidhi said: Hasan hadith, we know it only from the hadith of Bukayr. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Qutaybah, from Yazid ibn Mawhab, from al-Layth."
"2605","51 - Another. Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed would murmur something we did not understand and would not tell us of it. He said: Did you notice me? We said: Yes. He said: 'I remembered a prophet among the prophets who was given armies of his people, and said: Who can match these, or who can stand to these, or other speech. Allah revealed to him to choose for his people one of three: either that an enemy from other than them dominate, or hunger, or death. He consulted his people about that, and they said: You are the Prophet of Allah; we entrust that to you; choose for us. He stood to prayer — and when they were alarmed, meaning they hastened to prayer — and prayed as long as Allah willed. He said: O my Lord, as for an enemy from other than them, no; or hunger, no; but death. So He set death upon them three days, and seventy thousand of them died. The murmur which you see me say is: O Allah, by You I fight, by You I assail, and there is no power nor strength except by Allah.'"
"2606","52 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed Asr would murmur — murmuring in the saying of some of them is moving his lips as if speaking something — and it was said to him: O Prophet of Allah, when you pray Asr you murmur. He said: 'A prophet among the prophets was impressed by his Ummah and said: Who can stand to these? Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to him to give them choice between that I take vengeance upon them, or that I set their enemy upon them. They chose vengeance, so He set death upon them, and seventy thousand of them died in a day.' He said: When he narrated this hadith, he narrated this other hadith. He said: There was a king, and that king had a soothsayer who soothsayed for him. The soothsayer said to him: Look for me a boy, intelligent — or he said: quick to learn — that I teach him this knowledge of mine, for I fear to die and this knowledge be cut off from you. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith at length."
"2607","53 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us, from his book: Sulayman, meaning Ibn al-Mughirah, narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed would murmur something we did not understand and would not tell us of it. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you notice me? A speaker said: Yes. He said: I remembered a prophet among the prophets who was given armies of his people, and said: Who can match these? — or a word like this — Sulayman doubted. He said: It was revealed to him: Choose for your people among one of three: either that I set upon them an enemy from other than them, or hunger, or death. He said: He consulted his people about that, and they said: You are the Prophet of Allah; we entrust that to you, so choose for us. He said: He stood to his prayer. He said: They used to hasten when alarmed to prayer. He said: He prayed. He said: As for an enemy from other than them, no; or hunger, no; but death. He said: So He set death upon them three days, and seventy thousand of them died. My murmur which you see me say is: O Allah, O my Lord, by You I fight, by You I assail, and there is no power nor strength except by Allah.'"
"2608","54 - And with it my father narrated to me: Rawh narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he met the enemy would say: 'O Allah, by You I move, by You I assail, and by You I fight.' Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Sulayman; and from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan and Abd ibn Humayd, from Abd al-Razzaq, in similar form, and said: Hasan hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it in the book of the Deed of Day and Night from Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan, from Bahz ibn Asad, from Hammad ibn Abi Zayd, from Thabit, in similar form. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili; and from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Sulayman ibn Harb, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit, in similar form. Muslim narrated more than one hadith in his Sahih from the narration of Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Suhayb; among that the hadith of the soothsayer, so for that we did not mention the rest of his hadith."
"2609","55 - Another. Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Qudamah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque of Quba, and men of the Ansar entered upon him greeting him while he was praying. I asked Suhayb, who was with him: How did he do when greeted while praying? He said: He gestures with his hand. Sufyan said: I said to an old man: Ask him: Did you hear from Abd Allah ibn Umar? The man said to him: Did you hear this from Abd Allah ibn Umar? He said: As for me, I saw Ibn Umar and spoke to him."
"2610","56 - Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, with a chain transition. 57 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us: Umayyah ibn Bistam narrated to us, both said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the mosque of Quba and was praying; people began entering and greeting him. When he went out, I asked him: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) return to them? He said: With his hand like this, and he gestured with it."
"2611","58 — Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa al-Aquli informed us, in Baghdad, that Sadaqah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Mahlaban informed them; Asim ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us, recited to him; al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Ayyash informed us; al-Hasan — he is Ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Za'farani — narrated to us; Ali narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; Zayd ibn Aslam informed us, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, the mosque of Banu Amr ibn Awf, which is the mosque of Quba, and prayed in it, and men of the Ansar came to him greeting him while he was in prayer. So I asked Suhayb: What would the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when they greeted him while he was praying? He said: He would gesture with his hand. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Muhammad ibn Mansur, and Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad, both from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, similarly."
"2612","Another, 59 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us, there, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us; Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan, from his father, from Ka'b al-Ahbar who said: We find in the Torah that Dawud, the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he finished his prayer, would say: O Allah, set right for me my religion which You made the protection of my affair, and set right for me my worldly life in which You placed my livelihood; O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the wealth of the wealthy does not avail him against You. Ka'b al-Ahbar said: And Suhayb informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would finish his prayer with this supplication."
"2613","60 — Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them; Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Suwayd — he is Ibn Sa'id — narrated to us; Hafs — he is Ibn Maysarah — narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan, from his father: that Ka'b swore to him by the One Who parted the sea for Musa: we find in the Torah that Dawud, peace be upon him, used to supplicate with these words when finishing his prayer: O Allah, set right for me my religion which You made a protection for me, and set right for me my worldly life in which You placed my livelihood; O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the wealth of the wealthy does not avail him against You. He said: And Suhayb narrated to me that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say them when finishing his prayer."
"2614","61 — Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there, that Zahir al-Shahhami informed them; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; my grandfather, the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad, informed us; Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la al-Sadafi narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Hafs ibn Maysarah Abu Umar al-San'ani informed me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan, from his father: that Ka'b swore to him by the One Who parted the sea for Musa: we find in the Torah that Dawud, the Prophet of Allah, when he finished his prayer, would say: O Allah, set right for me my religion which You made a protection for me, and set right for me my worldly life in which You placed my livelihood; O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, and I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You; O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the wealth of the wealthy does not avail him against You. He said: And Ka'b narrated to me that Suhayb, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to him that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say them when finishing his prayer. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Amr ibn Sawwad, from Ibn Wahb, from Hafs ibn Maysarah; and from Muhammad ibn Nasr, from Ayyub ibn Sulayman, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Sulayman, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Abu Suhayl ibn Malik, from his father, Ka'b said; and from Harun ibn Abdillah, from Sa'd ibn Abd al-Hamid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mughith who narrated to him, who said: Ka'b said; and from Ibrahim ibn Ya'qub, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli, from Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ata Abu Marwan, from his father, from Abu Mughith ibn Amr: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah, from Ibn Abi al-Sari, from Hafs ibn Maysarah. It is possible that Abu Marwan heard it from Ka'b saying to him that Ka'b swore, and heard it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mughith, from Ka'b; and Ka'b's statement in the hadith, ""we find in the Torah that Dawud,"" may be something appended into the Torah which is not from it, for the Torah came long before Dawud, peace be upon him, and this is something not hidden, and Allah knows best."
"2615","Another, 62 — The Imam Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq, son of Shaykh Abd al-Qadir ibn Abi Salih al-Jili, informed us, in Baghdad, that Sadaqah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mahlaban informed them; Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Ayyash informed us; al-Hasan — he is Ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah — narrated to us; Sa'd ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Hamid ibn Yazid ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from Suhayb who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while dates were before him and he was eating, and he said: Take some of this food. So I began eating from the dates, and he said: You eat dates while you have ophthalmia? I said: I only chew from the other side. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed."
"2616","63 — Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn Ishaq informed us. 64 — And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us; both said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Amr ibn Awn al-Wasiti narrated to us; Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us; Abd al-Hamid ibn Sayfi — a man from the descendants of Suhayb — narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that Suhayb said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while dates and bread were before him, and he said: Come near and eat. So I began eating from the dates, and he said: Do you eat dates while you have ophthalmia? I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I suck it from the other side. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahhab, from Musa ibn Isma'il, from Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sayfi, from his father, from his grandfather Suhayb. So it is in the Sunan of Ibn Majah as Abd al-Rahman ibn Sayfi. And al-Bukhari and Abu Hatim al-Razi mentioned Abd al-Hamid ibn Sayfi. And Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Hashim ibn al-Qasim, from Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak with its chain, and with him: dates and bread were before him."
"2617","Another, 65 — Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ar'arah narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb narrated to us; Abd al-Hamid ibn Ziyad ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather who said: Suhayb al-Khayr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives a woman a dowry while intending not to pay it to her, then dies before paying it, will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, as an adulterer; and whoever takes a loan while intending not to repay its owner, then dies before repaying its owner, will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, as a thief. Part of this hadith dropped from our shaykh's hearing from al-Khallal; and Zahir informed us of it, that Sa'id al-Sayrafi informed them, by ijazah if not by hearing; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us with its chain."
"2618","66 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Fasawi narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb, from his father Muhammad ibn Yazid and his uncle Abd al-Hamid ibn Yazid ibn Sayfi, from Sayfi ibn Suhayb, from Suhayb who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives a woman a dowry while intending not to pay it to her will meet Allah Most High as an adulterer; and whoever takes a loan while intending not to repay it will meet Allah as a thief. The Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hushaym, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Ansari, from a man of al-Namir ibn Qasit who said: I heard Suhayb ibn Sinan, and he mentioned it with its meaning. And Ibn Majah narrated from it the mention of debt, from Hisham ibn Ammar, from Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Sayfi ibn Suhayb, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ziyad ibn Sayfi, from Shu'ayb ibn Amr, from Suhayb; and from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir, from Yusuf, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Ziyad, from his father, from his grandfather Suhayb."
"2619","Another, 67 — Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan, from his father, that Ka'b swore by the One Who parted the sea for Musa. 68 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Umari the judge narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us. 69 — Al-Tabarani said: And al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi al-Basri narrated to us; Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us; both said: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Abi Marwan, from his father: that Ka'b swore by Allah Who parted the sea for Musa that Suhayb narrated to him that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never saw a town he intended to enter except that he said when he saw it: O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, and Lord of the seven earths and what they bear, and Lord of the devils and what they mislead, and Lord of the winds and what they scatter; we ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people and the evil of what is in it. This is the wording of Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili's narration. And al-Tabarani's narration: that Suhayb narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with him: we ask You, and the rest is the same. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah, from Ibn Abi al-Sari, from Hafs ibn Maysarah, similarly."
"2620","Another, 70 — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf al-Misri narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Adi narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from his great-grandfather, from Suhayb who said: I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before revelation came to him."
"2621","Another, 71 — With it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn Kurdi narrated to us. 72 — Al-Tabarani said: And Sahl ibn Musa Shiran narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; both said: Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil, from Suhayb who said: I prepared food for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and came to him while he was sitting among a group. So I stood facing him and gestured to him, and he gestured to me, ""And these?"" I said: No. So he fell silent and I stood in my place. When he looked at me I gestured to him, and he said: ""And these?"" I said: No, twice; he did that two or three times. Then I said: Yes, and these, though it was only a little thing I had prepared for him. So he came and they came with him and ate, and I think he said: and some remained."
"2622","73 — Abu Zur'ah Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us; Ja'far ibn Abdillah informed us; Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us; Ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Bundar Abu Bakr al-Basri narrated to us; Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us; Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Salil, from Suhayb who said: I prepared food for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and came to him and invited him, and I gestured to him, and he said: ""And these?"" I said: No, though it was only a little thing I had prepared for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then I gestured to him, and he said: ""And these?"" I said: Yes. So they came and ate and some remained. Salim ibn Nuh was criticized by some of the imams. And Imam Ahmad said: I see no harm in him, and I wrote from him. And Abu Zur'ah said: There is no harm in him, truthful, trustworthy, and Muslim narrated from him in his Sahih."
"2623","Another, 74 — Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Talib Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Hamzah ibn Suhayb, from his father, from Umar that he said: O Suhayb, were it not for three traits in you. He said: And what are they? He said: You took a kunyah though you have no child, and you ascribed yourself to the Arabs though you are a man of the Romans, and there is extravagance in you regarding food. He said: O Commander of the Believers, as for your saying: you took a kunyah though you have no child, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunyah Abu Yahya; and as for your saying: you ascribed yourself to the Arabs though you are a man of the Romans, I am a man of al-Namir ibn Qasit, taken captive from al-Mawsil after I was a boy who knew his family and lineage; and as for your saying: extravagance in food, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of you is he who feeds food."
"2624","75 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us; my father narrated to us. 76 — Al-Tabarani said: And Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us; Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us; both said: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Hamzah ibn Suhayb, from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: O Suhayb, you took a kunyah though you have no child, and you ascribed yourself to the Arabs though you are a man of the Romans. He said: O Commander of the Believers, as for your saying: you took a kunyah though you have no child, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunyah Abu Yahya; and as for your saying: you ascribed yourself to the Arabs though you are a man of the Romans, I am a man of al-Namir ibn Qasit, taken captive from al-Mawsil after I was a boy who knew his family and lineage."
"2625","77 — Al-Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Akhdar informed us, in Baghdad, that Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Tarrah informed them; Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn al-Naqqur informed us; Abu al-Qasim Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us. 78 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; both said: Mus'ab — he is Ibn Abdillah ibn Mus'ab ibn Thabit ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam — narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Rabi'ah ibn Uthman, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father who said: I went out with Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, until I entered with him upon Suhayb in a walled garden in al-Aliyah. When Suhayb saw him, he said: O people... O people. Umar said: What is with him, may he have no father, supplicating against the people? He said: He was only calling a boy of his called Yuhannas. He said: O Suhayb, there is nothing in you I criticize except three traits, and were it not for them I would prefer no one over you. He said: What are they? For you are outspoken. He said: You will not inform me of anything but I will believe you in it. He said: I see you squander your wealth, and take a kunyah with a prophet's name, Abu Yahya, and claim Arab lineage while your tongue is non-Arab. He said: As for my squandering my wealth, I spend it only in its right; and as for my kunyah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me the kunyah Abu Yahya, shall I abandon it for your saying? And as for my ascribing myself to the Arabs, the Romans took me captive when I was small, and I do not remember my household; even if I were split open from dung I would ascribe myself to it. This is the wording of al-Baghawi's hadith, and what was written is the narration of Abdillah ibn Ahmad. Imam Ahmad narrated it similarly from Bahz, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, that Umar did not mention Aslam. And he narrated it from Zakariyya ibn Adi, from Ubaydullah ibn Amr, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Hamzah, from his father... and he mentioned the kunyah and food only. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr, from Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil. I say: As for the mention of lineage, al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih on sales, from Bundar, from Ghundar, from Shu'bah, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from his father who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf said to Suhayb: Fear Allah and do not claim to other than your father. He said: It would not please me to have such-and-such, and that I said that; but I was stolen when I was a boy."
"2626","Another, 79 — Shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Tamimi informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Rustah narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Sulayman al-Duba'i narrated to us; Awf narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Suhayb who said: When I intended to emigrate from Makkah to Madinah, Quraysh said to me: O Suhayb, you came to us with no wealth, and you leave, you and your wealth? By Allah, that will never be. So I said to them: What if I hand over my wealth to you, will you let me go? They said: Yes. He said: So I handed over my wealth to them and they let me go. So I left until I arrived at Madinah, and that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Suhayb has profited, Suhayb has profited, twice. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from al-Nadr and Rawh and Abu Usamah, all from Awf ibn Abi Jamilah."
"2627","Chapter of Dad: Those named Dahhak. Dahhak ibn Abi Jubayrah, may Allah be pleased with him — so says Hammad ibn Salamah, but he is actually Abu Jubayrah ibn al-Dahhak. 80 — Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Hudbah ibn Khalid and Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Dahhak ibn Abi Jubayrah who said: They had nicknames in the Jahiliyyah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called a man by his nickname, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, he dislikes it. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And do not insult one another by nicknames, to the end of the verse."
"2628","81 — Al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Isma'il narrated to us; Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi; Abu Jubayrah ibn al-Dahhak narrated to me, saying: Concerning us it was revealed, concerning Banu Salimah: And do not insult one another by nicknames. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah and there was no man among us but he had two or three names. When he called one of them by one of those names, they would say: O Messenger of Allah, he becomes angry at this. He said: So it was revealed: And do not insult one another by nicknames. Imam Ahmad also narrated it, titled Hadith of Abu Jubayrah al-Dahhak ibn al-Dahhak, from Hafs ibn Ghiyath, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Jubayrah ibn al-Dahhak, from uncles of his, and he mentioned it. Abu Hatim al-Razi said about him: I do not know of companionship for him."
"2629","Another, 82 — Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn informed them; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Hudbah narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Dahhak ibn Abi Jubayrah who said: The Ansar used to give charity and give what Allah willed until a year of drought struck them and they withheld. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw yourselves with your hands into destruction, and do good; indeed Allah loves the doers of good."
"2630","83 — Shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar informed them; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Abu Qirsafah Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us. 84 — Ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us; both said: Adam narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Dahhak ibn Abi Jubayrah who said: The Ansar used to give charity and spend from their wealth, then a year of drought struck them and they withheld from spending in the way of Allah; so it was revealed: And do not throw yourselves with your hands into destruction."
"2631","Al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan ibn Awf ibn Ka'b al-Kilabi, may Allah be pleased with him. 85 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I do not see the blood money except for the paternal relatives, for they pay it on his behalf; has any of you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that? So al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi said — and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had appointed him over the Bedouins —: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from her husband's blood money. So Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, acted upon that."
"2632","86 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, used to say: The blood money is for the paternal relatives, and the wife does not inherit anything from her husband's blood money, until al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi wrote to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from her husband's blood money."
"2633","87 — Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Dharr al-Salhanji informed them; Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us; Abu Bakr Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us; Abu Bakr — he is Ibn Abi Shaybah — narrated to us; Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib: that Umar used to say: The blood money is for the paternal relatives, and the wife does not inherit anything from her husband's blood money, until al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi wrote to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from her husband's blood money."
"2634","88 — And with it Abu Bakr — he is Ibn Abi Shaybah — narrated to us; Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab stood and asked: Who has knowledge of the wife's inheritance from her husband's blood money? So al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi stood and said: Enter your tent until I inform you. So he entered, and he came to him and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to me to give the wife of Ashyam inheritance from her husband's blood money."
"2635","89 — Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Sufyan narrated to us, saying: I heard it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id: that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The blood money is for the paternal relatives, and the wife does not inherit from her husband's blood money, until al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dibabi inheritance from her husband's blood money. So Umar retracted his statement. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah and Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Qutaybah and Ahmad ibn Mani' and Abu Ammar al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, from Sufyan, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah and Muhammad ibn Mansur, from Sufyan, from al-Zuhri; and from Muhammad ibn Mansur, from Sufyan, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Zuhri. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. Al-Daraqutni mentioned, among what al-Bukhari and Muslim are required to include of his hadith, a group, among them: al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan; al-Zuhri narrated his hadith from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from him."
"2636","Al-Dahhak ibn Qays ibn Khalid al-Akbar ibn Wahb ibn Tha'labah al-Fihri, may Allah be pleased with him. 90 — Abu al-Fath Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi and Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal al-Sufi, the two Isfahanis, informed us, in their books: that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Daw'i informed them; Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali al-Nasa'i narrated to us; Qutaybah narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Umamah that he said: The Sunnah regarding prayer over the funeral is to recite the Mother of the Qur'an quietly in the first takbirah, then say takbir three times, and the taslim at the last one."
"2637","91 — And with it, from Ibn Shihab, from Muhammad ibn Suwayd al-Thaqafi, from al-Dahhak ibn Qays, similarly. So al-Nasa'i narrated it in his book."
"2638","Another, 92 — Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Asbahani informed us, in Damascus, that his grandfather al-Hafiz Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn al-Fadl al-Tamimi informed them; Ahmad ibn Abdillah al-Rassas informed us; Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Jurjani informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Rafi' narrated to us, from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from al-Dahhak ibn Qays, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Most High says: I am the best partner; whoever associates with Me, he belongs to My partner. O people, purify your deeds for Allah, for Allah accepts of deeds only what is sincere; and do not say: this is for Allah and for kinship, for it is for kinship and there is nothing in it for Allah; and do not say: this is for Allah and for your faces, for it is for your faces and there is nothing in it for Allah."
"2639","Dirar ibn al-Azwar — and al-Azwar's name is Malik ibn Aws ibn Khuzaymah ibn Sa'id ibn Malik ibn Tha'labah ibn Dudan ibn Asad ibn Khuzaymah ibn Mudrikah ibn Ilyas ibn Mudar. 93 — Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us; al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar who said: My family sent me with a milch camel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered me to milk it. He said to me: Leave the milk that remains in the udder."
"2640","94 — And with it my father narrated to me; Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ya'qub ibn Buhayr — a man of the tribe — who said: I heard Dirar ibn al-Azwar say: We gifted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a milch camel. He said: So I milked it. He said: When I began to milk it thoroughly, he said: Do not do that; leave the milk that remains in the udder."
"2641","95 — And with it my father narrated to me; Abd al-Rahman — he is Ibn Mahdi — narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abdillah ibn Sinan, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he was milking and said: Leave the milk that remains in the udder."
"2642","96 — And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri and Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi and Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuza'i al-Asbahani narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abdillah ibn Sinan, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me or by a man milking and said: Leave what keeps the milk coming. Al-Tabarani said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from al-A'mash, from Abdillah ibn Sinan, while al-A'mash's companions differed, narrating it from al-A'mash, from Ya'qub ibn Buhayr."
"2643","97 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to me; al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar who said: We gifted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a milch camel, so I milked it for him. When I began to milk it thoroughly, he said: Do not do that; leave what keeps the milk coming."
"2644","98 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Dawud narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ya'qub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar who said: My family sent me with a milch camel to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a gift to him, and he said to me: Milk it, and leave the milk that remains in the udder. And he supplicated for me."
"2645","99 — And with it Musaddad narrated to us; Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ya'qub ibn Buhayr, from Dirar ibn al-Azwar who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a she-camel as a gift, and he said to me: Stand and milk it. So I stood and milked it. When I went to milk it thoroughly, he said: Leave the milk that remains in the udder. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from Abu Khaythamah, from Waki'."
"2646","Damrah ibn Tha'labah al-Sulami then al-Bahzi, may Allah be pleased with him. 100 — Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us; Baqiyyah — meaning Ibn al-Walid — narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, from Damrah ibn Tha'labah: that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing two Yemeni garments, and he said: O Damrah, do you think these two garments of yours will admit you into Paradise? He said: If you seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah, I will not sit until I remove them from me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive Damrah ibn Tha'labah. So he went quickly until he removed them from himself. Al-Tabarani narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari, from Sulayman ibn Salamah al-Khabayiri, from Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid; Abu Salamah ibn Sulaym narrated to us, and he mentioned it. I say: And al-Khabayiri is criticized, and we only mentioned that as corroboration for Baqiyyah's statement: Abu Salamah narrated to us. Dumayrah ibn Sa'd al-Sulami: his hadith was mentioned earlier under his father."
"2647","Chapter of Ta: Tariq ibn Ashyam al-Ashja'i, may Allah be pleased with him. 101 — Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Abu Malik informed us, saying: I said to my father: O father, you prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman and Ali, may Allah's pleasure be upon them, here in Kufa for nearly five years; did they perform qunut? He said: O my son, it is an innovation."
"2648","102 — And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to me. 103 — Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar al-Basri narrated to us; Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us; both said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i who said: I asked my father about qunut in the dawn prayer, and he said: O my son, I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and I did not see any of them perform qunut. O my son, it is an innovation; he said it three times."
"2649","104 — And with it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Abu Malik al-Ashja'i informed us, from his father who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman, and Ali here in Kufa for about five years, and they would not perform qunut in Fajr. Then he said: O my son, it is an innovation."
"2650","105 — And with it Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Hafs ibn Ghiyath and Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani', from Yazid ibn Harun; and he narrated it from Salih ibn Abdillah al-Tirmidhi, from Abu Awanah, similarly, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah, from Khalaf ibn Khalifah, from Abu Malik with its meaning. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ibn Idris and Hafs and Yazid. Muslim narrated in his Sahih two hadiths from the narration of Yazid ibn Harun, from Abu Malik, from his father, besides what we mentioned."
"2651","Another, 106 — Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us that Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed them; Muhallam ibn Isma'il al-Dabbi informed us; the judge Abu Sa'id al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi narrated to us; Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi al-Sarraj informed us; Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Khalaf — he is Ibn Khalifah — narrated to us, from Abu Malik, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me."
"2652","107 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me."
"2653","108 — Abu al-Qasim ibn Ma'ali ibn Shidqini and Abu Ali ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn al-Harif and Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them; Umar ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim al-Khaffaf informed us; Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Zayyat informed us; Ibrahim — he is Ibn Abdillah ibn Ayyub al-Mukharrimi — narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Awn Abu Muhammad al-Kharraz narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us; Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from his father — who had prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me, for Satan cannot take my form. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Husayn ibn Muhammad, from Khalaf ibn Khalifah. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it in the book al-Shama'il from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2654","Another, 109 — Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz and others informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Bakr ibn Isa Abu Bishr al-Basri al-Rasibi narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us; Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us, saying: I heard my father, and I asked him, and he said: Our dye alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was wars and saffron."
"2655","Another, 110 — My uncle, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us that Abu al-Ma'ali Ahmad ibn Abd al-Ghani ibn Muhammad ibn Hanifah al-Bajisra'i informed them, in Baghdad; Abu Ali Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Baqqal informed us, saying: It was recited to Abu Abdillah Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili, while we were listening; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i informed us; Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Abu Malik al-Ashja'i Sa'd ibn Tariq informed us, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Being killed suffices for my Companions."
"2656","111 — And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, in Baghdad; Abu Malik al-Ashja'i Sa'd ibn Tariq informed us, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Being killed suffices for my Companions. My father said: Yazid narrated to us in Wasit, without ""he heard"" in it."
"2657","Another, 112 — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Asbahani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Zakariyya ibn Hamdawayh al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Surayj narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said:... [truncated in source: matn is only the letter Ha]."
"2658","113 — And Muhammad also informed us that Fatimah informed them, recited to her; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahawi narrated to us; Surayj ibn al-Nu'man al-Jawhari narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. It has a witness in Sahih al-Bukhari from the hadith of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and Abdillah ibn Amr and Salamah ibn al-Akwa', and in the two Sahihs from the hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah."
"2659","Another, 114 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Mawsili narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from his father who said: Drink would be prepared overnight for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a stone vessel. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari."
"2660","Another, 115 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi al-Dumayk narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Hammad al-Hadrami narrated to us; Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from his father who said: When a man accepted Islam in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they would teach him the prayer."
"2661","Another, 116 — And with it Sulayman informed us; Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami and Abdan ibn Ahmad and al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Qudamah narrated to us; Sa'd ibn Tariq narrated to us, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulating the House, and when the people crowded at the Stone he would touch it with a curved staff in his hand. Muslim narrated from the narration of Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulated the House in the Farewell Pilgrimage upon his mount, touching the Stone with his curved staff so the people could see him, and so he would be prominent, and so they could ask him, for the people thronged him. And Abu al-Tufayl narrated, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) circumambulating the House and touching the corner with a curved staff with him, and kissing the staff."
"2662","Another, 117 — And with it Sulayman informed us; Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us. 118 — Sulayman said: And Ahmad ibn Bahram al-Idhaji narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ziyad al-Attar narrated to us; both said: Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Ata al-Khurasani narrated to us; Abu Malik al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from his father who said: We used to sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while we were boys, and I never saw a man longer in silence than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When his Companions spoke and spoke at length, he would smile. Muslim narrated from the hadith of Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: They would sit conversing and delve into matters of the Jahiliyyah, laughing, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would smile."
"2663","Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Hadrami, may Allah be pleased with him. 119 — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us; Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il al-Hadrami, from Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Hadrami who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in our land there are grapes we press and drink from. He said: No. So I repeated to him, and he said: No. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we seek healing with it. He said: That is not a healing, but it is a disease."
"2664","120 — And Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Bahz and Abu Kamil narrated to us, both saying: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Simak narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il, from Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Hadrami, that he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in our land there are grapes we press and drink from. He said: No. So I repeated to him, and he said: No. I said: We seek healing with it for the sick. He said: That is not a healing, but it is a disease. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, from Shu'bah, from Simak, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il, from his father, mentioning Tariq ibn Suwayd, or Suwayd ibn Tariq. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Affan ibn Muslim, from Hammad ibn Salamah, with its chain, from Tariq ibn Suwayd, without doubt. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from Ghassan ibn al-Rabi', from Hammad ibn Salamah; and Abu Hatim did not say ""narrated to us,"" so I do not know whether it dropped or he did not hear it from Abu Ya'la. And Muslim narrated from the hadith of Shu'bah, from Simak, from Alqamah ibn Wa'il: that Tariq ibn Suwayd asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wine... and he mentioned it. So, Allah knows best, Alqamah ibn Wa'il heard it from his father and from Tariq ibn Suwayd."
"2665","Tariq ibn Shihab ibn Abd Shams al-Bajali, Abu Abdillah al-Ahmasi, may Allah be pleased with him. 121 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Huraym ibn Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Friday prayer is obligatory upon every Muslim except a slave, or a sick person, or a woman, or a child. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim, from Ishaq ibn Mansur."
"2666","Another, 122 — Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad narrated to us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Alqamah, from Tariq who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Which jihad is best? He said: A word of truth before an unjust ruler."
"2667","123 — And with it my father narrated to me; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Tariq ibn Shihab, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he had placed his foot in the stirrup: Which jihad is best? He said: A word of truth before an unjust ruler. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi."
"2668","Another, 124 — Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: Two men became junub; one of them performed tayammum and prayed, while the other did not pray. So they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not criticize either of them. Al-Nasa'i narrated it similarly from Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, from Umayyah ibn Khalid, from Shu'bah, with the wording: A man became junub and did not pray."
"2669","Another, 125 — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: A delegation of Qays came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Begin with the Ahmasis before the Qaysis; O Allah, bless the Ahmasis and their men."
"2670","126 — And al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq who said: A delegation of Ahmas and a delegation of Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begin with the Ahmasis before the Qaysis. Then he called the Ahmas and said: O Allah, bless Ahmas and its horses and its men, seven times."
"2671","127 — And with it my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mukhariq, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: A delegation of Bajilah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Clothe the Bajalis and begin with the Ahmasis. He said: A man of Qays lagged behind, saying: Until I see what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says to them. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for them five times: O Allah, send blessings upon them, or: O Allah, bless them; Mukhariq is the one who doubts."
"2672","Another, 128 — Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I campaigned in the caliphates of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, thirty-three or thirty-four, from expeditions to detachments."
"2673","129 — And Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us; Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I campaigned in the caliphate of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2674","130 — And with it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I campaigned in the caliphates of Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, thirty-three or forty-three, between expeditions and detachments."
"2675","Another, 131 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Bahram al-Idhaji narrated to us; al-Ashja'i narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: The Jews came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Inform us what the people of Paradise eat first when they enter. He said: The first thing they eat is whale liver. In Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in the hadith: that a Jewish scholar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is their first gift when they enter Paradise? He said: The extra lobe of the fish's liver."
"2676","Another, 132 — And with it Sulayman informed us; Ishaq ibn Dawud al-Sawwaf narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us; Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Walid, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would frequently mention the Hour until it was revealed: In what position are you to mention it; to your Lord is its finality."
"2677","133 — And Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Hurrbadaqani informed us, in Isfahan, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baghban informed them, while he was present; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us; al-Hafiz Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Asim narrated to us; Amr ibn Sa'id ibn Sinan narrated to us; Abbad ibn Suhayb narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Tariq ibn Shihab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would speak much about the Hour until this verse was revealed: In what position are you to mention it. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He saw him but has no companionship, and the hadith narrated by al-Thawri from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Tariq ibn Shihab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which jihad is best? He said: A word of truth before an unjust ruler; and he said: This hadith is mursal. Al-Daraqutni said: Mentioning hadiths of men among the Companions who narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whose hadiths were narrated through sound chains whose transmitters are not impugned, yet they — meaning al-Bukhari and Muslim — did not include anything from their hadiths, so including them is required by their methodology. Then Tariq ibn Shihab was mentioned: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I campaigned in the caliphate of Abu Bakr; Shu'bah said: from Qays ibn Muslim. And Ibn Abi Za'idah and others narrated, from Isma'il, another hadith from him. And praise belongs to Allah alone, and may Allah send blessings upon Muhammad and his family and grant them peace."
"2678","Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi, may Allah be pleased with him. 134 — Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi al-Khushu'i informed us, in Damascus, that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Qubays al-Ghassani informed them, in Damascus, saying: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hadid informed us, recited to him; my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman al-Sulami informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Samiri al-Kharaiti informed us; Umar — he is Ibn Shabbah — narrated to us; Yahya — he is Ibn Sa'id al-Qattan — narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right; spit behind you or toward your left if it is empty, otherwise like this beneath your left foot. And he scraped beneath his foot on the ground."
"2679","135 — And Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi al-Shuruti informed us, in Damascus, that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami informed them, recited to him; it was said to him: Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd ibn Sa'dan al-Shahid informed you, in Damascus; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Rab'i informed us; Abu al-Abbas Hajib Tirarakin al-Farghani informed us, as I read to him; Muhammad ibn Jabir ibn Bujayr Abu Bujayr narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, from his father; Ghaylan ibn Jami' al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you spit, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit toward your left if it is empty, or beneath your foot."
"2680","136 — Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us, there, that Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them; Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri and Abu al-Muzaffar al-Qushayri — he is Sa'id ibn Mansur — informed us, both saying: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us; my grandfather the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad informed us; Bundar and Abu Musa narrated to us, both saying: Yahya — he is Ibn Sa'id — narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come in prayer, do not spit to your right, but behind you, or toward your left, or beneath your left foot. This is Bundar's hadith. And Abu Musa said: He said: Mansur narrated to me; and he also said: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, and said: And spit behind you or toward your left if it is empty, otherwise like this beneath your left foot."
"2681","137 — And with it my grandfather the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad informed us; Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you are in prayer, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit toward your left, and if it is not empty then beneath your left foot, then rub it. Mansur said: Meaning, rub it on the ground."
"2682","138 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present; Abu Nu'aym informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; al-Thawri informed us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right; spit toward your left if it is empty, otherwise beneath your foot. And he gestured with his leg and scraped the ground."
"2683","139 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us; Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you are in prayer, do not spit toward your face nor to your right, but to your left if it is empty, otherwise beneath your foot."
"2684","140 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us; Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us; Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi — a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit toward your left if it is empty, or beneath your foot. It was narrated from Mansur by a group besides those we mentioned: Sulayman ibn Mihran, Abu al-Ahwas, Qays ibn al-Rabi', Mufaddal ibn Muhalhil, Ja'far ibn al-Harith, and Ubaydah ibn Humayd. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, with its ending: and he rubbed beneath his feet; and from Muhammad ibn Ja'far, from Shu'bah, adding: then rub it; and from Ubaydah ibn Humayd, from Mansur, in it: then rub it. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Hannad, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Mansur, similarly. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Sa'id, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, similarly. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki', from Sufyan, similarly. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer, he is conversing with his Lord, so let him not spit before him nor to his right, but to his left beneath his foot. And from the hadith of Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw phlegm in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it with a pebble, then forbade a man to spit to his right or before him, but to spit to his left or beneath his left foot."
"2685","Another, 141 — Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal al-Sufi and Abu al-Fath Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi, the two Isfahanis, informed us, in their books from Isfahan, that Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them; Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar al-Dinawari informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali al-Nasa'i narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Isa narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us; Yazid — he is Ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd — narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Tariq al-Muharibi who said: We came to Madinah and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing on the pulpit addressing the people, saying: The giving hand is the upper one; begin with those you support: your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then the nearest, then the nearest."
"2686","142 — And with it, from Tariq al-Muharibi, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, these are Banu Tha'labah ibn Yarbu' who killed so-and-so in the Jahiliyyah, so take our revenge for us. So he raised — meaning his hands — until we saw the whiteness of his armpits, saying: No mother wrongs on behalf of her child, twice. So al-Nasa'i included it in his book; it is one hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated this latter one from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abdillah ibn Numayr, from Yazid. And Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated the first one, the giving hand, from Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah, from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth, from al-Fadl. And the hadith is longer than this, and this is part of it."
"2687","143 — And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Adib informed us; the Sayyid Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi al-Husayn al-Alawi al-Hamadhani narrated to us, by dictation; Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Hisni al-Ahwazi narrated to us — he came to us in Hamadhan; Abu Sa'id Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us; Yazid ibn Ziyad narrated to me; Jami' ibn Shaddad narrated to me, from Tariq al-Muharibi who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the market of Ukaz calling out: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will prosper. And a man followed him with stones, having bloodied his ankle, saying: O people, do not obey him, for he is a liar. I said: Who is this? They said: This is the youth of Banu Abd al-Muttalib, and the one following him is Abd al-Uzza — meaning Abu Lahab."
"2688","144 — And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us that Tamim ibn Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them; Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzi informed us; Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us; Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Azdi narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the market of Dhu al-Majaz wearing a red garment, saying: O people, say: There is no god but Allah, you will prosper. And a man followed him throwing stones at him, having bloodied his ankles and heels, saying: O people, do not obey him, for he is a liar. I said: Who is this? It was said: This is the youth of Banu Abd al-Muttalib. I said: Who is this following him throwing stones at him? It was said: This is Abd al-Uzza, Abu Lahab. He said: When Islam prevailed, we set out in a caravan until we alighted near Madinah, and with us was a woman in a litter. While we were sitting, a man wearing two white garments came to us, greeted, and said: From where has the party come? We said: From al-Rabadhah. He said: And with us was a camel. He said: Will you sell this camel? We said: Yes. He said: For how much? We said: For such-and-such sa's of dates. He said: So he took it without bargaining us down, and said: I have taken it. Then he disappeared behind the walls of Madinah, and we blamed one another among ourselves, saying: You gave your camel to a man you do not know. The woman in the litter said: Do not blame one another, for I saw the face of a man who would not betray you; I never saw anything more like the moon on the night of fullness than his face. He said: In the evening a man came to us, greeted us, and said: I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to you, saying: You may eat until you are full and measure until you take your full due. He said: So we ate until we were full and measured until we took our full due. He said: Then we came to Madinah the next day, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing delivering a sermon on the pulpit, saying: The giving hand is the upper one; begin with those you support: your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then the nearest, then the nearest. Then a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, these are Banu Tha'labah ibn Yarbu' who killed so-and-so in the Jahiliyyah, so take our revenge from them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, and said: No mother wrongs on behalf of a child; no mother wrongs on behalf of a child. So Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it in his book. Al-Daraqutni said: Tariq ibn Abdillah al-Muharibi has two hadiths; one was narrated by Rib'i ibn Hirash from him, and the other by Abu Sakhrah Jami' ibn Shaddad, and both meet their conditions — meaning al-Bukhari and Muslim. Al-Thawri and Shu'bah and the people narrated it from Mansur, from Rib'i, from him. And Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrated it from Abu Sakhrah; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah said it, from Ibn Numayr, from him. Al-Bukhari narrated from the hadith of Hakim ibn Hizam that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"2689","Tariq ibn Alqamah, may Allah be pleased with him. 145 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Hasan ibn Hammad ibn Fadalah al-Sayrafi al-Basri narrated to us; Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj informed us; Ubaydullah ibn Abi Yazid informed me that Abd al-Rahman ibn Tariq ibn Alqamah informed him, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he came to a place near the house of Ya'la ibn Munabbih, would face the House and supplicate."
"2690","Takhfah, also said Tihfah ibn Qays, also said Qays ibn Takhfah, also said Abdillah ibn Tihfah al-Ghifari, may Allah be pleased with him. 146 — Abu Abdillah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us, in al-Harim of Baghdad, that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuwa'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Ya'ish ibn Takhfah al-Ghifari who said: My father was among the people of al-Suffah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding them, and a man began to take a man and two men with him until I remained the fifth of five. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go forth. So we went with him to A'ishah's house, and he said: O A'ishah, feed us. He said: So she brought jashishah and we ate, then she brought haysah like a sandgrouse and we ate, then he said: O A'ishah, give us drink. So she brought a large cup and we drank, then she brought a small cup with milk in it and we drank. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, spend the night, and if you wish, go to the mosque. We said: No, rather we will go to the mosque. He said: While I was in the mosque lying on my stomach, a man moved me with his foot and said: This is a lying position Allah hates. So I looked, and it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2691","147 — And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Anbari informed us, in Baghdad; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated to us, from Yahya, from Ya'ish ibn Takhfah, that he said: My father was among the people of al-Suffah. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding them, so a man would go with a man, and a man with two men, until I remained the fifth of five. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Go forth. So we went with him to A'ishah's house, and he mentioned the hadith with its meaning."
"2692","148 — And with it Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us; Abu Bakr — he is Ibn Abi Shaybah — narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shayban, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah: that Ya'ish ibn Qays ibn Takhfah narrated to him from his father — who was among the people of al-Suffah — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, go with this one with you; O so-and-so, go with this one with you. So I remained the fourth of four. He said: Go forth. So we went until we came to A'ishah's house, and he said: Feed us. So she brought jashishah, then he said: Feed us. So she brought hays like a sandgrouse, then he said: Give us drink. So she brought a large cup and we drank. He said: Give us drink. So she brought a small cup with milk in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, sleep here, and if you wish, go to the mosque. We said: Rather we will go to the mosque. While I was sleeping on my stomach before dawn, a man pushed me with his foot and said: This is a lying position Allah hates. So I raised my head, and it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2693","149 — And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari informed us; Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us; Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us; Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, that Ya'ish ibn Takhfah narrated to him, from his father — who was among the people of al-Suffah — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, go with this one with you; O so-and-so, go with this one with you. So I remained the fourth of four. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Go forth. So we went until we came to A'ishah's house. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed us. So she brought jashishah and we ate, then he said: O A'ishah, feed us. So she brought hays like a sandgrouse, then he said: O A'ishah, give us drink. So she brought a small cup with milk in it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: If you wish, sleep here, and if you wish, enter the mosque. We said: Rather we will enter the mosque. While I was sleeping on my stomach before dawn, a man pushed me with his foot and said: Like this, for this is a lying position Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates. So I raised my head, and it was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2694","150 — And Abu Ahmad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr — meaning Ibn Halhalah — from Nu'aym ibn Abdillah, from Ibn Takhfah al-Ghifari who said: My father informed me that he was a guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group, and we spent the night with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out checking and saw him lying face down, so he struck him with his foot to wake him and said: This is the lying of the people of the Fire."
"2695","151 — And with it my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ya'ish ibn Tihfah al-Ghifari, from his father who said: I was a guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the needy who were his guests. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at night checking on his guest, and saw me lying on my stomach, so he struck me with his foot and said: Do not lie in this position, for it is a lying Allah, Mighty and Majestic, hates."
"2696","152 — And with it my father narrated to me; Yazid narrated to us; Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman who said: While I was sitting with Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, a man of Banu Ghifar, a son of Abdillah ibn Tihfah, came upon us. Abu Salamah said: Will you not inform us of your father's report? He said: My father Abdillah ibn Tihfah narrated to me: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when guests were many with him, would say: Let every man return with his guest. Until one night many guests gathered with him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let every man return with his companion. He said: I was among those who returned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he entered, he said: O A'ishah, is there anything? She said: Yes, a small haysah I prepared for your iftar. He said: So she brought it in a small bowl of hers. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a little from it and ate it, then said: Take, in Allah's name. So we ate from it until we would not look at it. Then he said: Do you have any drink? She said: Yes, a little milk I prepared for you. He said: Bring it. So she brought it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it, raised it to his mouth, and drank a little, then said: Drink, in Allah's name. So we drank until, by Allah, we would not look at it. Then we went out, and I came to the mosque and lay on my face. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out waking the people: Prayer... Prayer. And when he went out he would wake the people for prayer. He passed by me while I was on my face and said: Who is this? I said: I am Abdillah ibn Tihfah. He said: This is a lying Allah, Mighty and Majestic, dislikes."
"2697","153 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us of it, in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present; Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Anbari informed us, in Baghdad; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us; Asim ibn Ali narrated to us; Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, saying: While I was with Abu Salamah, a man of Banu Ghifar — the son of Abdillah ibn Tihfah — came upon us. Abu Salamah said: Narrate to us your hadith from your father. He said: Abdillah ibn Tihfah narrated to me: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when guests gathered, would say: Let every man return with his guest. Until one night many guests gathered in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let every man return with his companion. He said: I was among those who returned with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When he entered, he said: O A'ishah, is there anything? She said: Yes, a small haysah I prepared for your iftar. He said: Bring it. So she brought it in a small bowl of theirs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate something from it, then presented it to us, then said: In Allah's name, eat. So we ate from it until, by Allah, we would not look at it. Then he said: Do you have drink? She said: A little milk I prepared for your iftar. He said: Bring it. So she brought it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank something from it, then said: In Allah's name, drink. So we drank until, by Allah, we would not look at it. Then we went out to prayer, and he would wake his household when he went out, saying: Prayer... Prayer. Then he saw me lying face down and said: Who is this? I said: I am Abdillah. He said: It is a lying Allah dislikes. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Hashim ibn al-Qasim, from Abu Mu'awiyah Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Ya'ish ibn Takhfah ibn Qays, similarly. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Muthanna, from Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, from Ya'ish ibn Takhfah ibn Qays who said: My father was... and he mentioned it, without saying: from his father. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ibn Muthanna with its chain; and from Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la, from Khalid, from Hisham with its chain, similarly; and from Shu'ayb ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Sa'id, from Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq, from al-Awza'i — Yahya narrated to me; Abu Salamah narrated to me; Qays ibn Takhfah al-Ghifari narrated to me; my father narrated to me, similarly; and from Ibrahim ibn Ya'qub, from al-Hasan ibn Musa, from Shayban, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah: that Ya'ish ibn Qays ibn Takhfah narrated to him, from his father. And he narrated it through other chains. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah in part; and from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Qays ibn Tihfah, from his father, with the story of his sleeping on his stomach. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Sallam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya, from Ibn Qays ibn Tihfah, from his father, similarly. Abu Ishaq Ibrahim al-Harbi said: This hadith was narrated from Abu Salamah by al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Abi Dhi'b said: And Yahya ibn Kathir; and Hisham and Shayban and al-Awza'i and Ma'mar and Muhammad ibn Jabir narrated it from Yahya. As for Ma'mar, he sent it as mursal, so it is neither proof for him nor against him. As for Ibn Jabir, he erred in parts of it: he did not mention Abu Salamah, and said: Ayyash, intending to say Ya'ish ibn Tihfah; and said: Ibn Abi Tihfah; and said: Hisham from Ya'ish ibn Takhfah, from his father. And Shayban said: Ya'ish ibn Qays ibn Tihfah, from his father. And al-Awza'i said: From Ibn Qays ibn Tihfah, from his father; all of this I do not recognize. The view with me is the statement of al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, from the son of Abdillah ibn Tihfah, from his father: this is a man of Ghifar who came to Madinah and accepted Islam, then returned to Ghayfah and al-Safra', settling there. If they had not said Qays ibn Takhfah and Ibn Qays ibn Takhfah, from his father — all of this I do not recognize; the view with me is the statement of al-Harith. Abu Ishaq said: I said to Ali ibn Abdillah: Ibn Tihfah? He said: His name is Ya'ish. Hisham's hadith requires the hadith to be from Takhfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and Shayban's hadith requires it to be from Qays ibn Takhfah; and Allah knows best what is correct. And there was a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Ya'ish, whose lineage I do not know."
"2698","Al-Tufayl ibn Sakhbarah, A'ishah's maternal brother, may Allah be pleased with him. 154 — Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Aban al-Ju'fi narrated to us; Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bakka'i narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from al-Tufayl — Abd al-Malik said: he is A'ishah's maternal brother —: that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw in a dream as though I met some Christians, and I said: You are a people, were it not that you say: The Messiah is the son of Allah. He said: And you, were it not that you say: What Allah wills and what Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wills. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you narrate it to anyone before me? I said: Yes. So he stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: To proceed, your brother has seen what has reached you, or who has reached among you. Then he said: I used to hear it and dislike it, and was shy before you to forbid you; say: What Allah alone, with no partner, wills."
"2699","155 — And with it Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Ibrahim al-Sami narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from al-Tufayl, A'ishah's maternal brother, who said: I saw in sleep-visions as though I passed by a group of Jews. I said: Who are you? They said: We are the Jews. I said: You are indeed the people, were it not that you say: Uzayr is the son of Allah. They said: And you are the people, were it not that you say: What Allah wills and what Muhammad wills. And I passed by a group of Christians. I said: Who are you? They said: We are the Christians. He said: You are indeed the people, were it not that you say: The Messiah is the son of Allah. They said: And you are the people, were it not that you say: What Allah wills and what Muhammad wills. In the morning I informed some people of it, then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of it. He said: Did you inform anyone of it? I said: Yes. When he prayed Zuhr, he stood as a preacher, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Tufayl saw a vision and informed of it whomever he informed among you; you used to say a word that shyness prevented me from forbidding you; so do not say: What Allah wills and what Muhammad wills."
"2700","156 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present; Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us; Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us; Isma'il ibn Abdillah informed us; Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Rib'i, from al-Tufayl — A'ishah's brother through breastfeeding — who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say: What Allah wills and what Muhammad wills, but say: What Allah alone wills. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Bahz ibn Asad and Affan ibn Muslim, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Abd al-Malik, like Ibrahim al-Sami's hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib, from Abu Awanah, from Abd al-Malik, similarly."
"2701","Those named Talhah: Talhah ibn Amr al-Nasri, may Allah be pleased with him. 157 — Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us, in al-Harbiyyah, that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Dawud — meaning Ibn Abi Hind — narrated to us, from Abu Harb, that Talhah narrated to him — and he was among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — who said: I came to Madinah with no acquaintance there, so I stayed in al-Suffah with a man, and between me and him there was a mudd of dates each day. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day, and when he finished, a man of the people of al-Suffah said: O Messenger of Allah, dates have burned our stomachs and tattered cloaks have worn off us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended and delivered a sermon, then said: By Allah, if I found bread or meat I would feed it to you. But you will soon reach, or whoever of you reaches that time, when platters will be brought to you morning and evening, and you will wear like the curtains of the Ka'bah. He said: I and my companion stayed eighteen days and nights with no food for us except unripe dates, until we came to our brothers of the Ansar and they shared with us, and the best of what we obtained was these dates."
"2702","158 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us; Asad ibn Musa narrated to us; Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us. 159 — Al-Tabarani said: And Bakr ibn Sahl al-Dimyati narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ashkib al-Kufi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us — both — from Dawud Abu Hind, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Talhah ibn Amr who said: When a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with no notable in Madinah to stay with, he would stay with the people of al-Suffah. And I had relatives there. What would come to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) each day was two mudds of dates between two persons. While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in one of the prayers, a caller among his Companions called to him: O Messenger of Allah, dates have burned our stomachs and tattered cloaks have worn off us. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished prayer, he stood, praised Allah and extolled Him, then mentioned the hardship he met from his people, saying: I and my companion were a dozen-odd days with no food for us except unripe dates, until we came to our brothers of the Ansar and they shared their food with us, and the bulk of their food was dates. By the One besides Whom there is no god, if I found bread and meat for you I would feed it to you; and perhaps you will reach a time, or whoever of you reaches it, in which you wear like the curtain of the Ka'bah, brought to you morning and evening with platters."
"2703","160 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us; Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us; Khalid informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad, from Talhah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili, from Wahb ibn Baqiyyah. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Talhah ibn Amr al-Nasri, also said Talhah ibn Abdillah, one of Banu Layth among the people of al-Suffah; he has companionship; Abu Harb ibn Abi al-Aswad al-Dayli narrated from him mursal; so Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned it from his father. I say: And in Imam Ahmad's narration from Abd al-Samad is what indicates it is not mursal, for in it Talhah narrated to him, and Allah knows best what is correct."
"2704","Talhah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sulami, may Allah be pleased with him — and I do not think he has companionship. 161 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sulami, from his father who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want jihad in the way of Allah. He said: Is your mother alive? I said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stay at her feet, for there is Paradise. Al-Bukhari did not mention Talhah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sulami in al-Tarikh, nor did Ibn Abi Hatim. Imam Ahmad narrated, from Rawh, from Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father Talhah ibn Abdillah, from Mu'awiyah ibn Jahimah al-Sulami: that Jahimah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I wanted to campaign and came to consult you. He said: Do you have a mother? He said: Yes. So he said: Stay with her, for Paradise is at her feet. Then the second and third times, in different sittings, with similar wording. And this is what is correct, and Allah knows best."
"2705","Talq ibn Ali ibn al-Mundhir ibn Qays ibn Amr ibn Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Suhaym ibn Murrah ibn al-Du'al ibn Hanifah al-Hanafi al-Yamami, may Allah be pleased with him. 162 — Abu al-Qasim Hibatullah ibn Ali ibn Mansur ibn Thabit ibn Ghalib al-Ansari al-Busiri informed us, by my recitation to him in Fustat of Egypt — I said to him: Abu Sadiq Murshid ibn Yahya ibn al-Qasim al-Madini informed you, in Egypt in the year 517, and he acknowledged it — saying: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Naysaburi informed us; Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh al-Naysaburi narrated to us, verbally; Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Ali ibn Sinan ibn Bahr al-Nasa'i narrated to us; Hannad ibn al-Sari informed us, from Mulazim who said: Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to me, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali who said: We set out as a delegation until we came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we pledged allegiance to him and prayed with him. When we finished prayer, a man as though a Bedouin came and said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think of a man who touches his penis during prayer? He said: Is it but a piece of flesh of him? Or: a part of him?"
"2706","163 — And Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa al-Aquli informed us, in Baghdad, that Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Sallal informed them; Abu al-Hasan Jabir ibn Yasin informed us; Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas al-Mukhallas al-Dhahabi informed us; Abu al-Qasim Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi informed us; Abu Rawh Muhammad — he is Ibn Ziyad ibn Farwah al-Baladi — narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali who said: We set out as a delegation to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until we came to him; we pledged allegiance to him and prayed with him. Then a man as though a Bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of a man touching his penis during prayer? He said: Is it but a piece of flesh or a part? So said Abu Rawh. He said: Then another man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of praying in a single garment? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loosened his lower garment and draped his cloak over it, then wrapped himself in both, stood, and prayed with us, then said: Does every one of you find two garments?"
"2707","164 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, in Isfahan, that Fatimah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father: that a man said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think of praying in a single garment? So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loosened his lower garment and paired it with his cloak, wrapped himself in both, and prayed with us. When he finished his prayer he said: Does every one of you find two garments?"
"2708","165 — And Abu Abdillah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us, in al-Harim, that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us; Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir; Qays ibn Talq al-Hanafi narrated to me that his father informed him: that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He fell silent toward him. When the call to prayer was made, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) paired two garments and prayed in them. Imam Ahmad narrated the hadith of touching the penis from Abu al-Nadr and Hammad ibn Khalid, both from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Qays. And he narrated the hadith of prayer in a single garment from Abd al-Samad, from Mulazim, from Abdillah ibn Badr; and from Yunus ibn Muhammad, from Aban al-Attar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Isa ibn Khuthaym, from Qays, from his father. Shayban's narration from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir — Qays narrated to me — was mentioned earlier, so I think Yahya heard it from Isa, from Qays, and heard it from Qays, by evidence of Shayban's hadith. And Abu Dawud narrated both hadiths together from Musaddad, from Mulazim, from Abdillah ibn Badr. And al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i narrated the hadith of touching the penis from Hannad ibn al-Sari. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki', from Muhammad ibn Jabir, from Qays, the hadith of touching the penis. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated prayer in a single garment from Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'd al-Abid, from Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami, from Mulazim. It was narrated in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah: that a questioner asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about praying in a single garment, and he said: Does every one of you have two garments?"
"2709","Another, 166 — Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri informed us, in Baghdad, that Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Sallal informed them; Jabir ibn Yasin al-Jannabi informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallas informed us; Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us; Muhammad — he is Ibn Ziyad ibn Farwah — narrated to us; Mulazim narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Badr: Qays said: My father visited us in Ramadan and spent the evening with us. He led us that night and performed witr with us, then went down to the mosque and prayed with them until only witr remained. Then he put a man forward, then said: Perform witr with them, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no two witrs in one night."
"2710","167 — And Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Affan narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr al-Suhaymi narrated to us; my grandfather Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to me, saying: And Siraj ibn Uqbah narrated to me that Qays ibn Talq narrated to them that his father Talq ibn Ali came to us in Ramadan, staying with us until evening. He led us in the night prayer of Ramadan and performed witr with us, then went down to the mosque of Rayman and prayed with them until only witr remained. He put a man forward and he performed witr with them, saying: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There are no two witrs in one night. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yazid, from Ayyub ibn Utbah, from Qays, from his father, the musnad part of it. And Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Mulazim. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it abridged, and al-Nasa'i, both from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Mulazim. And al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan gharib hadith. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Anmati, from Nasr ibn Ali, from Mulazim in full."
"2711","Another, 168 — Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Muflih ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Dumi informed them; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Hafiz informed us; al-Qasim ibn Ja'far informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lu'lu'i informed us; Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn al-Nu'man who said: Qays ibn Talq narrated to me, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat and drink, and let not the rising, ascending brightness alarm you; eat and drink until the redness spreads across for you. So Abu Dawud narrated it. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Mulazim, and said: A hasan gharib hadith."
"2712","169 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us of it, in Isfahan, that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us; Abdan ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Nu'man who said: Qays ibn Talq came to me in Ramadan while I had lifted my hand from my sahur fearing dawn. I said to him: O uncle, if any of the night remained for you, I would admit you and you would eat food and drink with me. He said: So he was admitted, and we entered, and I presented to him tharid and meat and nabidh. He ate and drank, and compelled me, so I ate and drank with him while I feared dawn. Then he said: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat and drink, and let not the rising, ascending brightness alarm you; eat and drink until the redness spreads across for you. And he gestured with his hand. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Ibn Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not Bilal's adhan prevent any of you from his sahur, for he calls at night until your standing one returns and your sleeping one wakes; the dawn is not that it says like this — and he spread his fingertips — but the dawn is that it says like this, and he described opening his fingers. And in Muslim's narration: it is the spreading one, not the elongated one. And in Muslim from the hadith of Samurah ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let neither Bilal's adhan deceive you regarding your sahur, nor the elongated whiteness of the horizon like this, until it spreads like this — and Hammad demonstrated with his hands — meaning spreading across."
"2713","Another, 170 — Abu Abdillah Isma'il ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Wakkas al-Attar informed us, in Baghdad, that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them; Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah narrated to us; Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Kinani narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Qasim — the brother of Abu al-Layth al-Fara'idi — narrated to us; Abu Hammam — he is al-Walid ibn Shuja' — narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, saying: Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to me, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man calls his wife, let her come to him even if she is at the oven."
"2714","171 — And Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Aquli informed us, in Baghdad, that Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Sallal informed them; Jabir ibn Yasin al-Jannabi informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallas informed us; Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us; Muhammad — he is Ibn Ziyad ibn Farwah al-Baladi — narrated to us; Mulazim narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali who said: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man calls his wife, let her come to him even if she is at the oven."
"2715","172 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abdillah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us. 173 — Al-Tabarani said: And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us. 174 — He said: And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us; all said: Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq; my father narrated to me, saying: I heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When a man calls his wife, let her answer him even if she is at the oven. Al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i narrated it, both from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Mulazim. And al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan gharib hadith. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abu Khalifah, from Musaddad."
"2716","Another, 175 — Abu Abdillah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us, in al-Harim, that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Samad narrated to us; Mulazim narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Badr and Siraj ibn Uqbah narrated to us: that his uncle Qays ibn Talq narrated to him that his father Talq ibn Ali narrated to him: that he set out as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they came to him and informed him that in their land there was a church, and they asked him for some leftover of his purification water as a gift. So he called for water, performed ablution and rinsed his mouth, then poured it into a leather water-skin, and said: Go with this water; when you reach your land, break your church, sprinkle its place with this water, and take it as a mosque. He said: We said: O Prophet of Allah, we travel in a time of intense heat, and the water dries up? He said: Extend it with water, for much of it will remain, good. He said: So we set out until we reached our land; we broke our church, sprinkled its place with that water, and took it as a mosque."
"2717","176 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to me, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali who said: We set out, six as a delegation to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — five of Banu Hanifah and the sixth a man of Banu Dubay'ah ibn Rabi'ah — until we came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We came to him, prayed with him, and informed him that in our land there was a church of ours, asking him for some leftover of his purification water as a gift. So he called for water, performed ablution from it and rinsed his mouth, then poured it for us into a leather water-skin, and said: Go with this water; when you reach your land, break your church, then sprinkle its place with the water, and take its place as a mosque. We said: O Prophet of Allah, the land is far and the water dries up. He said: Extend it with water, for it will only increase it in goodness. So we set out with it until we reached our land, and did what he ordered. And our monk that day was a man of Tayyi'; we called the prayer, and the monk said: A call of truth. Then he fled and was never seen again. Al-Nasa'i narrated it similarly from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Mulazim."
"2718","Another, 177 — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us; Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us; Isma'il ibn Abdillah narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us; Hawdhah ibn Qays ibn Talq narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Talq ibn Ali who said: When we prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave salam, we would see the whiteness of his right cheek and the whiteness of his left cheek."
"2719","178 — And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Mujashi'i al-Asbahani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Ya'qub al-Kirmani narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us; Hawdhah ibn Qays narrated to me, from his father Qays ibn Talq ibn Ali, from Talq ibn Ali who said: When the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave salam in prayer, we would see the whiteness of his right cheek and the whiteness of his left cheek. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Ali ibn al-Madini — before he was tested — from Abd al-Samad, from Mulazim. It has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas who said: I would see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) giving salam to his right and to his left until I saw the whiteness of his cheek."
"2720","Another, 179 — And Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Arim Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us; Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to us, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali who said: A scorpion stung me in the presence of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he performed ruqyah on it."
"2721","180 — Abdillah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: I found in my father's book in his handwriting: One of our companions narrated to me; Mulazim narrated to me; Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to me, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father Talq ibn Ali who said: A scorpion stung me in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he performed ruqyah on me and wiped it."
"2722","181 — And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Ibrahim ibn Mattuwayh al-Asbahani narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Badr, from Talq ibn Ali who said: A scorpion stung Talq in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ruqyah on him and wiped him with his hand. He did not mention Qays in this narration. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it from Abdillah ibn Qahtabah, from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Abi al-Shawarib, from Mulazim, similarly."
"2723","Another, 182 — Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us; Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Zayd or Badr — I doubt — from Talq ibn Ali al-Hanafi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not straighten his spine in it between its bowing and its prostration. And in a narration: between its bowing; and perhaps it is what is correct."
"2724","183 — And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us; Bakr ibn Muqbil al-Basri narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated to us; my grandfather narrated to us; Ikrimah ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Badr; Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali narrated to me, from Talq ibn Ali who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not straighten his back in his bowing and prostration. This narration adds Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali. Ayyub ibn Utbah narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Shayban, from his father. Perhaps Abd al-Rahman heard it from his father and from Talq ibn Ali, and Allah knows best."
"2725","Another, 184 — Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Aquli informed us, in Baghdad, that Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Sallal informed them; Jabir ibn Yasin al-Hannani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallas informed us; Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us; Muhammad — he is Ibn Ziyad ibn Farwah al-Baladi — narrated to us; Mulazim narrated to us, from Siraj ibn Uqbah, from his paternal aunt Khaldah bint Talq who said: My father narrated to me, saying: We were sitting with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Suhar Abd al-Qays came and said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think of a drink we make from our fruits? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him until he asked him three times. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed with us. When he finished prayer he said: Who is the questioner about intoxicants? You ask me? Do not drink it, nor give it to your Muslim brother to drink. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no man ever drinks it seeking the pleasure of its intoxication but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will give him wine to drink on the Day of Resurrection."
"2726","185 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, in Isfahan, that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi' al-Kufi narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Siraj ibn Uqbah, from his paternal aunt Khaldah bint Talq, from her father Talq ibn Ali who said: We sat with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Suhar ibn Abd al-Qays came and said: O Prophet of Allah, what do you think of a drink we make from our fruits? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from him until he asked him three times. Then he stood and prayed with us. When he finished prayer he said: Who is the questioner about intoxicants? You ask me? Do not drink it, nor give it to your Muslim brother to drink. By the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, no man ever drinks it seeking the pleasure of intoxication but Allah will give him wine on the Day of Resurrection. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Samad, from Mulazim, similarly."
"2727","Another, 186 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Badr, from Qays ibn Talq, from his father who said: I built the mosque of Madinah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would say: Give the Yamami access to the clay, for he is among the best of you at handling it."
"2728","187 — And Abu Abdillah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Samad narrated to us; Mulazim narrated to us; Siraj ibn Uqbah and Abdillah ibn Badr narrated to us, that Qays ibn Talq narrated to them that his father Talq ibn Ali said: I built the mosque with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would say: Bring the Yamami near the clay, for he is the best of you at handling it, and the strongest of you in shoulder. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yunus ibn Muhammad, from Ayyub, from Qays, from his father, similarly."
"2729","Chapter of Ayn: Those named Asim. Asim ibn Adi ibn al-Jadd ibn al-Ajlan ibn Harithah ibn Dubay'ah ibn Haram al-Quda'i, ally of Zayd ibn Malik ibn Awf al-Ansari, kunyah Abu Amr, also said Abu Abdillah. 188 — Abu al-Hasan al-Mu'ayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Tusi informed us, by my recitation to him in Naysabur — I said to him: Abu Muhammad Hibatullah ibn Sahl ibn Umar, known as al-Sayyidi, informed you, recited to him while you were listening — Abu Uthman Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Buhayri informed us; Abu Ali Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Sarakhsi informed us; Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Samad al-Hashimi informed us, in Baghdad; Abu Mus'ab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri al-Madani narrated to us; Malik narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, that Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi informed him, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the camel herders to stay away from Mina overnight: they stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then stone the next day and the day after for two days, then stone on the Day of Departure."
"2730","189 — And Abu Abdillah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us, in al-Harim, that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Rawh informed us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr informed me, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah, from Asim ibn Adi: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the herders to stone one day and night, then stone the next day."
"2731","190 — And with it he narrated to me; Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the herders to stone one day and skip one day."
"2732","191 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Malik narrated to us. 192 — Al-Tabarani said: And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the camel herders to stay overnight away: they stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then stone the next day and the day after for two days, then stone on the Day of Departure."
"2733","193 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ibrahim ibn Salih al-Shirazi narrated to us; Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr informed me, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the camel herders to stone on the Day of Sacrifice, then skip a day and night, then stone afterwards. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abd al-Razzaq, both from Malik ibn Anas. And Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Qa'nabi and from Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh, from Ibn Wahb, from Malik; and from Musaddad, from Sufyan, from Abdillah and Muhammad, the two sons of Abu Bakr, from their father, from Abu al-Baddah, similarly, the first being fuller. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Malik, and from Ibn Abi Umar, from Sufyan, like Musaddad's hadith, and said: So Ibn Uyaynah narrated; Malik's narration is more authentic, and it is a sahih hadith. And al-Nasa'i narrated it from Amr ibn Ali, from Yahya, from Malik; and from al-Husayn ibn Hurayth and Ibn al-Muthanna, from Sufyan, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr; and from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Ibn Mahdi, from Malik. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Abd al-Razzaq; and from Ahmad ibn Sinan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, both from Malik; and from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Ibn Uyaynah, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, from Abu al-Baddah, from his father. So it came in this narration as Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr, while the well-known is Abdillah, from his father, as in Malik's narration, and Allah knows best."
"2734","Another, 194 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hamzah al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn A'idh narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, from Abu al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madinah on Monday, twelve nights having passed of Rabi' al-Awwal, and stayed in Madinah ten years."
"2735","Another, 195 — Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; Umar ibn Zurarah al-Hadathi narrated to us; Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Uthman al-Balawi, from Asim ibn Abi al-Baddah ibn Asim ibn Adi, from his father, from his grandfather Asim ibn Adi who said: My brother and I bought one hundred shares of Khaybar's shares. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Asim, two attacking wolves that find sheep whose owner neglected them are not more corrupting to them than a man's love of wealth and honor is to his religion."
"2736","Another, 196 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present; Abu Nu'aym Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abbad ibn al-Awwam, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Asim ibn Adi: that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when this verse was revealed, ""those who do not bring four witnesses,"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, until they bring four witnesses, the loser will have fulfilled his need. He said: He had not stood until his paternal cousin, his father's brother's son, came with his wife carrying a boy, saying: He is from you, while he said: He is not from me. So the verse of mutual cursing was revealed. He said: And I am the first who spoke of it, and the first who was tested with it. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Adi except al-Sha'bi; Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman is alone in it."
"2737","197 — And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us; Sa'id narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Abdillah, from Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Asim ibn Adi: that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when this verse was revealed, ""those who do not bring four witnesses,"" I said: O Messenger of Allah, until they bring four witnesses, the loser will have fulfilled his need. So he mentioned it, ending: and who was tested with it, without saying ""first."" Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated it from Abbad and from Khalid ibn Abdillah. Al-Daraqutni said: And he mentioned a group whose hadiths the Companions' inclusion requires al-Bukhari and Muslim, or one of them; he mentioned Asim ibn Adi. Malik and Rawh and Ibn Uyaynah narrated his hadith from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr, from his father, from Abu al-Baddah, from his father: he permitted the herders to stone one day. And he has another hadith narrated by Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from Asim ibn Adi, on li'an."
"2738","Asim al-Laythi Abu Nasr, may Allah be pleased with him. 198 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us. 199 — Al-Tabarani said: And Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni narrated to us; Uqbah ibn Sinan al-Dhari' narrated to us; both said: Ghassan ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Yazid Abu Maslamah, from Nasr ibn Asim al-Laythi, from his father who said: I entered the mosque of Madinah and the people were saying: We seek refuge in Allah from Allah's anger and His Messenger's anger. He said: I said: What is it? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon on his pulpit when a man stood, took his father's hand, and took him out of the mosque. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah curses the leader and the led; woe to this ummah from so-and-so, the one with buttocks."
"2739","Those named Amir: Amir ibn Rabi'ah ibn Ka'b ibn Umayrah ibn Malik ibn Kinanah ibn Amir ibn Sa'd ibn Abdillah ibn al-Harith ibn Rufaydah ibn Umayrah ibn Abdillah — he is Anz — ibn Wa'il ibn Hinb ibn Afsa ibn Judaylah ibn Asad ibn Rabi'ah ibn Nazzal, ally of the family of al-Khattab, and his lineage is disputed. 200 — Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) using the siwak while fasting."
"2740","201 — And Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us, in Baghdad, that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah informed us; my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us. And Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) countless, immeasurable times using the siwak while fasting. Abd al-Rahman said: Countless times brushing while fasting."
"2741","202 — And with it my father narrated to me; Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) using the siwak countless, immeasurable times while fasting."
"2742","203 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them, recited to him while he was present; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abu Bakr narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) using the siwak while fasting."
"2743","204 — And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; al-Thawri informed us. 205 — And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah ibn Asim, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) using the siwak while fasting countless times. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad, from Yahya; and from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Sharik, both from Asim. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, similarly, and said: A hasan hadith."
"2744","Another, 206 — Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubaydillah al-Sufi informed us, in Baghdad, that his father Abu Mansur informed him; Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us; Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah informed us; Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us; Ali — he is Ibn al-Ja'd — narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Amir, from his father: that a woman of Banu Fazarah married a man for two sandals, and that was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to her: Are you pleased for yourself with two sandals? She said: I deem that so. He said: And I deem that so."
"2745","207 — And Abu Ahmad Abdillah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father: that a man of Banu Fazarah married a woman for two sandals, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted his marriage."
"2746","208 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Hamad informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, both saying: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us. 209 — Al-Tabarani said: And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us; Asim ibn Ali narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father: that a woman of Banu Fazarah was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having married for two sandals. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Are you pleased for yourself and your wealth with two sandals? She said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted it."
"2747","210 — And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna and Yusuf al-Qadi and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us; Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: A man of Banu Fazarah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I married a woman for two sandals. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted his marriage. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj, from Shu'bah. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar, from Yahya and Ibn Mahdi and Ghundar, from Shu'bah, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Hafs ibn Umar al-Darir and Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Waki'."
"2748","Another, 211 — Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz informed us that Hibatullah informed them; al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdillah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Waki' narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Isa, from Umayyah ibn Hind ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abdillah ibn Amir who said: Amir ibn Rabi'ah and Sahl ibn Hunayf set out intending ghusl."
"2749","212 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Abi Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. 213 — Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; both said: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us; Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Isa, from Umayyah ibn Hind, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: Sahl ibn Hunayf and I set out seeking a secluded thicket; we found a thicket and a pond. He said: One of us would be shy to bathe while anyone saw him, so he screened himself from me until, when he saw he had done so, he removed a cloak of coarse cloth over him, then entered the water. I looked at him a glance that pleased me for his build, and I struck him with my eye. He was seized with shivering while in the water. I called him and he did not answer me. So I went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of the news. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand with us. So he came to him, lifted from his leg, and entered the water. When he came to him, he struck his chest and said: O Allah, remove its heat and its cold and its ailment. Then he said: Stand. So he stood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sees in himself or his wealth or his brother what pleases him, let him supplicate for blessing for him, for the eye is real. This is Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham's wording from Ammar ibn Zurayq. And Waki''s narration from his father is similar; we only included al-Jarrah, Abu Waki', as corroboration."
"2750","214 — And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them; Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr and Abu Hisham — meaning al-Rifa'i — narrated to us, both saying: Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Abdillah ibn Isa, from Umayyah ibn Hind, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The eye is real. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr, from Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham abridged: The eye is real. And al-Nasa'i narrated it in al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Ahmad ibn Sulayman, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl, from Amir; and from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham, similarly."
"2751","Another, 215 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, in Isfahan, that Fatimah informed them; Muhammad informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr al-Qatirani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Tufayl al-Nakha'i narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: A man sneezed in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise, until our Lord is pleased and after He is pleased. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he said: Who is the utterer of the words? The man said: I am, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I saw twelve angels racing to them, which of them would write them. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Sharik, similarly. Al-Bukhari narrated something like it from the hadith of Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' al-Zuraqi."
"2752","Another, 216 — Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us that his father informed them; Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Sarifini informed us; Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hababah informed us; Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us; Ali — he is Ibn al-Ja'd — narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah who said: I heard Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever sends one blessing upon me, the angels send blessings upon him as long as he sends blessings upon me; so let the servant do little of that or much."
"2753","217 — And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, in Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, both saying: Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us. 218 — Al-Tabarani said: And Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us; Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us; Shu'bah informed us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdillah ibn Amir, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim sends one blessing upon me except the angels send blessings upon him as long as he sends blessings upon me; so let him do little of that or much. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Hajjaj and Shu'ayb ibn Harb and Waki', from Shu'bah, similarly. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Bakr ibn Khalaf, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shu'bah, similarly."
"2754","Another, 219 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, in Isfahan, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, recited to him while he was present; Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us; Abdillah ibn Ja'far informed us; Isma'il ibn Abdillah informed us; Abdillah — he is al-Qa'nabi — narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz — he is al-Darawardi — narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd — he is Ibn al-Muhajir — from Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Rabi'ah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a fresh grave and said: What is this grave? They said: The grave of so-and-so woman. He said: Why did you not inform me? He said: You were sleeping and we disliked waking you. He said: Do not do that; call me for your funerals. Then he lined up over her and prayed."
"2755","220 — Abu Ja'far Muhammad also informed us that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them; Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us; Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us; Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, from Abdillah ibn Amir ibn Rabi'ah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a new grave and said: Whose grave is this? They said: The grave of so-and-so woman. He said: Why did you not inform me? They said: O Messenger of Allah, you were sleeping and we disliked waking you. He said: Do not do that; inform me of your funerals. Then he stood, lined up, and prayed over her. And Imam Ahmad narrated it from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Abd al-Aziz al-Darawardi, similarly. And Ibn Majah narrated it from Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib, from al-Darawardi, similarly. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from the narration of al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a moist grave and prayed over it, and they lined up behind him, and he said takbir four times; Muslim's wording. And both narrated from the hadith of Abu Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah: that a black woman who swept the mosque — or a youth — died, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed her and asked about her — or about him — and they said: He died. He said: Why did you not inform me? He said: As though they belittled her matter — or his matter. He said: Show me his grave. So they showed him, and he prayed over her, then said: These graves are filled with darkness over their people, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, illuminates them for them through my prayer over them."
"2756","Another 221 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad - Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili - informed us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, Asim ibn Ubaydillah informed me. (Ha). 222 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Asim ibn Ubaydillah ibn Asim informed me, Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah informed me: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers after me who pray the prayer at its time and delay it past its time, so pray with them; if they pray it at its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and for them, and if they delay it past its time then pray it with them, it is for you and upon them. Whoever separates from the community dies a pre-Islamic death, and whoever breaks the pledge and dies breaking the pledge will come on the Day of Resurrection with no proof. This is the wording of Abd al-Razzaq. And the wording of Hajjaj's hadith: Asim ibn Ubaydillah informed me: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers after me who pray the prayer outside its time and delay it past its time, so pray it with them; if they pray it at its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and for them, and if they pray it outside its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and upon them. Whoever separates from the community dies a pre-Islamic death, and whoever breaks the pledge and dies breaking the pledge will come on the Day of Resurrection with no proof. So I said: Who informed you of this report? He said: Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah informed me of it, from his father Amir ibn Rabiah, Amir ibn Rabiah reports it, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2757","223 - And Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Asim ibn Ubaydillah informed me, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers after me who pray the prayer at its time and delay it, so pray it with them; if they pray it at its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and for them, and if they delay it past its time and you pray it with them, it is for you and upon them. Whoever separates from the community dies a pre-Islamic death, and whoever breaks the pledge and dies breaking the pledge will come on the Day of Resurrection with no proof. I said: Who informed you of this report? He said: Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah informed me, from his father Amir ibn Rabiah, Amir ibn Rabiah reports, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yahya ibn Said and Abu Asim narrated it from Ibn Jurayj. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq, and the completion of its chain at its end is as in this narration."
"2758","Another 224 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi - at Baghdad - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yunus ibn Muhammad and Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us, they said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from his father who said: Surayj ibn Rabiah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umrah to Umrah is expiation for the sins and wrongs between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward but Paradise."
"2759","Another 225 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki and Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tammar and Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir informed us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for following up between them increases lifespan and provision, and they remove poverty as the bellows removes the dross of iron."
"2760","226 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. (Ha). 227 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for they remove poverty and sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron."
"2761","228 - And Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz - at al-Harbiyyah - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow up between Hajj and Umrah, for following up between them removes poverty and sins as the bellows removes the dross of iron. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Aswad ibn Amir, from Sharik. And he also narrated it from Sufyan, from Asim, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Umar, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And once he said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Sufyan said: His father is not in it."
"2762","Another 229 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi - there - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Nadr and Husayn narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir - meaning Ibn Rabiah - from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies with no obedience upon him dies a pre-Islamic death, and if he casts it off after its bond upon his neck he will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, with no proof. Behold, no man is alone with a woman not lawful to him, for their third is Satan, except a mahram, for Satan is with the one, and he is farther from the two. Whose evil deed grieves him and whose good deed pleases him, he is a believer. Husayn said it: After his binding it upon his neck."
"2763","230 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Khalifah al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies with no obedience upon him dies a pre-Islamic death, and whoever casts it off on the day of binding it will meet Allah with no proof. Behold, no man is alone with a woman except a woman with a mahram, for Satan is their third, and he is farther from the two. And whose good deed pleases him and whose evil deed grieves him, he is a believer."
"2764","Another 231 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi - at Asbahan - informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Ishaq - he is Ibn Abi Israil - narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to me, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send us with no food but borrowed dates, so we divided them handful by handful until we reached date by date, and by Allah after we lost them we missed them."
"2765","232 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi and Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, they said: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send us with no food but borrowed dates, so we divided them handful by handful until we reached date by date. I said: And what good could date by date do you, O father? He said: Do not say that, for by Allah no sooner had we lost them than we missed them."
"2766","233 - And Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, al-Masudi informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father - and he was a Badri - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to send us on expeditions, O my son, with no provision but borrowed dates, so we divided them handful by handful until it came to date by date. He said: So I said: O father, and what could a date avail you? He said: Do not say that, for after we lost them we came to miss them."
"2767","Another 234 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us, Amr ibn Malik narrated to us. (Ha). 235 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Mazini narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, from Umar - freedman of the family of Manzur ibn Sayyar - from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was circumambulating the House when his sandal strap broke, so a man took a strap from his sandal and went to fasten it on the Prophet's sandal (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: This is preferential treatment and I do not love preferential treatment."
"2768","236 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali narrated to us, Umar - freedman of Abu Manzur ibn Sayyar - narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from his father: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was circumambulating the House when his sandal strap broke, so a man took a strap from his sandal and went to fasten it on the Prophet's sandal (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he pulled it away and said: This is preferential treatment and I do not love preferential treatment."
"2769","237 - And with it Abu Yala informed us, Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Umar ibn Ali ibn Muqaddam narrated to us, Umar - freedman of Ibn Fazarah - narrated to us - and Umar said: al-Fazari - he said: I heard Asim ibn Ubaydillah, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from his father who said: I was circumambulating with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when his strap broke, so I took his sandal to strap it with my strap, so he said: Bring it, then he took it, and said: This is preferential treatment and I do not love preferential treatment."
"2770","Another 238 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar and Sufyan ibn Said narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydillah ibn Asim, from Abdullah ibn Amir ibn Rabiah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believer spends the forenoon calling talbiyah until the sun sets but it sets with his sins until they return as they were. Asim ibn Ubaydillah ibn Asim ibn Umar ibn al-Khattab - more than one of the scholars has spoken about him, and Shubah and Sufyan al-Thawri and others narrated from him. Al-Tirmidhi authenticated from his hadith the hadith of marriage for two sandals. And Ibn Adi said: And he mentioned some of his hadith, and despite his weakness his hadith is written."
"2771","Amir ibn Shahr al-Hamdani Abu al-Kanud - may Allah be pleased with him - 239 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz and Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said - at al-Harbiyyah - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Said al-Muaddib Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid and al-Mujalid ibn Said narrated to us, from Amir al-Shabi, from Amir ibn Shahr who said: I heard two phrases, one from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and another from the Negus. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Look to Quraysh, take from their speech and leave their action. And I was sitting with the Negus when his son came from school and recited a verse of the Gospel which I recognized or understood, so I laughed. He said: What do you laugh at? At the Book of Allah? For by Allah, among what Allah sent down upon Isa son of Maryam is: The curse will be in the land when its rulers are boys."
"2772","240 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Isa ibn Salim al-Shashi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, from Amir ibn Shahr who said: Two phrases I heard, one from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the other from the Negus, I would not love to have the world with all in it for either of them. As for what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Look to Quraysh and listen to them, and leave their action. Abu Usamah narrated it from Mujalid at length with a story in it. And Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Zakariyya ibn Adi, from Ubaydullah ibn Amr, like the two narrations at length. Al-Daraqutni mentioned that the hadith of Amir ibn Shahr, al-Shabi from him, is among what al-Bukhari and Muslim, or one of them, must bring of his hadith; Ismail and Bayan and Malik ibn Mighwal and more than one narrated it. I say: And Imam Ahmad narrated from Aswad ibn Amir, from Sharik, from Ismail, from Ata, from Amir ibn Shahr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Take the speech of Quraysh and leave their action. And the well-known is the hadith of al-Shabi, so if Sharik preserved it then Ismail heard it from al-Shabi and from Ata, and Allah knows best."
"2773","Amir ibn Abdillah al-Badri - may Allah be pleased with him - 241 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. (Ha). 242 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, they said: Khalid ibn Abdillah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from Amir ibn Abdillah al-Badri who said: The day of Badr was Monday morning, the nineteenth of Ramadan."
"2774","Amir ibn Umayr - may Allah be pleased with him - 243 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Abbadani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, from Amir ibn Umayr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed three days not coming out to a prescribed prayer, so he was spoken to about that, so he said: I found my Lord Majestic, Generous; He gave me with each one of the seventy thousand who enter Paradise without reckoning, with each one seventy thousand. So I said: My ummah will not reach or complete this. So He said: I will complete them for you from the bedouins."
"2775","Amir ibn Masud ibn Amir Khalaf ibn Wahb al-Qurashi al-Jumahi - may Allah be pleased with him - and there is disagreement about his companionship. Imam Ahmad said: I consider he has companionship, and Yahya ibn Main said: He has no companionship, and Allah knows best. 244 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Numayr ibn Urayb, from Amir ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Fasting in winter is the cool spoil."
"2776","245 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Numayr ibn Urayb, from Amir ibn Masud al-Jumahi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting in winter is the cool spoil."
"2777","246 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Numayr ibn Urayb, from Amir ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting in winter is the cool spoil."
"2778","247 - And with it al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Numayr ibn Urayb, from Amir ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting in winter is the cool spoil. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar, from Yahya ibn Said, and said: This is mursal; Amir ibn Masud did not meet the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he is the father of Ibrahim ibn Amir al-Qurashi."
"2779","Another 248 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us. (Ha). 249 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay narrated to us, Amir ibn Masud al-Qurashi narrated to me - and he crowded me at Makkah in the days of Ibn al-Zubayr at the Maqam in the first row - he said: I said to him: Was good said about the first row? He said: Yes, indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about it: If people knew what is in the first row they would not line in it but by lot or drawing."
"2780","Amir al-Muzani Abu Hilal - may Allah be pleased with him - 250 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Waiz al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hilal ibn Amir al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching to the people at Mina on a mule wearing a red cloak, with a man of the people of Badr before him expressing for him. He said: So I came until I put my hand between his foot and his sandal strap. He said: So I kept marveling at its coolness."
"2781","251 - And with it my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, a shaykh of Banu Fazarah narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Amir al-Muzani, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching to the people on a grey mule, with Ali - may Allah be pleased with him - expressing for him."
"2782","252 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us. (Ha). 253 - Al-Tabarani said: Abdullah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, they said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Hilal ibn Amir al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching to the people at Mina on a mule, wearing a red cloak, with a man of the people of Badr before him expressing for him. He said: So I came until I put my hand between his foot and his sandal strap, and I kept marveling at its coolness. Abu Dawud narrated it from Musaddad. And Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated it from Hilal ibn Amir, from Rafi ibn Amr al-Muzani, and it is in the Musnad of Rafi, and Allah knows best what is correct."
"2783","Amir ibn Wathilah ibn Abdillah ibn Umayr ibn Jabir al-Laythi - may Allah be pleased with him - 254 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Asbahani - there - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Jafar ibn Yahya informed us, my uncle Umarah ibn Thawban informed me: that Abu al-Tufayl informed him, he said: I was a boy carrying a camel limb, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributing meat at al-Jiranah, when a woman came to him and he spread his cloak for her. So I said: Who is this? They said: His mother who nursed him."
"2784","255 - And Abu Sad Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qattan al-Muaddib - at Asbahan - informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abdillah ibn Mandah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abdillah ibn Khurshidh informed us of his saying, al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Yahya ibn Thawban who said: My uncle Umarah ibn Thawban narrated to me, Abu al-Tufayl narrated to me: that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributing meat from Jiranah, when a woman came and he spread his cloak for her and she sat on it. So I said: Who is this? So it was said: This is his mother who nursed him, and I was that day a boy carrying the carcass bone."
"2785","256 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Jafar ibn Yahya ibn Thawban narrated to us, Umarah ibn Thawban narrated to us, that Abu al-Tufayl informed him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Jiranah distributing meat, and I was that day a boy carrying a camel limb. He said: Then a bedouin woman came, and when she drew near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he spread his cloak for her and she sat on it. So I asked: Who is this? They said: His mother who nursed him."
"2786","257 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recitation to him while present - Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Yahya informed me, he said: Umarah ibn Thawban informed me, that Abu al-Tufayl informed him, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a woman came until she drew near the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spread his cloak for her. So I said: Who is this? They said: This is his mother who nursed him. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna similarly."
"2787","Another 258 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Jumay, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah he sent Khalid ibn al-Walid to Nakhlah, where al-Uzza was. Khalid came to it, and it was upon three acacia trees, so he cut the acacias and demolished the house that was over them, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him; so he said: Go back, for you have done nothing. So Khalid returned, and when the custodians, who were its veil-keepers, saw him they fled into the mountain saying: O Uzza, afflict him with madness, O Uzza, blind him. Khalid came to it and there was a naked woman with her hair spread, throwing dust on her head, so he struck her head with the sword until he killed her, then he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he said: That was al-Uzza."
"2788","259 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad informed me, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Makkah he sent Khalid ibn al-Walid to Nakhlah, where al-Uzza was. Khalid ibn al-Walid came to it, and it was upon three acacia trees, so he cut the acacias and demolished the house that was over them, then he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he said: Go back, for you have done nothing. So Khalid returned, and when the custodians, who were its guards, saw him they fled into the mountain saying: O Uzza, afflict him, O Uzza, blind him, or else die in disgrace. He said: Khalid came to it and there was a naked woman with her hair spread throwing dust on her head, so he struck her head with the sword until he killed her, then he returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: That was al-Uzza. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ali ibn al-Mundhir. Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ziyad al-Qaddah - we brought him for corroboration, and the well-known is from the hadith of al-Walid ibn Jumay, from Abu al-Tufayl."
"2789","Another 260 - Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi - at al-Harim - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid narrated to us, al-Walid - meaning Ibn Abdillah ibn Jumay - informed us, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came back from the expedition of Tabuk he ordered a caller who called: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has taken the pass, so let no one take it. While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Hudhayfah leading him and Ammar driving him - was going, a group of veiled men came on mounts and crowded Ammar as he drove the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ammar came striking the faces of the mounts. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hudhayfah: Drive on, drive on, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended, and Ammar returned. Then he said: O Ammar, did you recognize the people? He said: I recognized most of the mounts, and the people were veiled. He said: Do you know what they intended? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They intended to startle the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so as to throw him. He said: Then Ammar reviled a man of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I adjure you by Allah, how many do you know were the people of the pass? He said: Fourteen. He said: If you were among them then they were fifteen. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) excused three of them. They said: By Allah, we did not hear the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we did not know what the people intended. So Ammar said: I bear witness that the remaining twelve are at war with Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the day the witnesses stand. Al-Walid said: And Abu al-Tufayl mentioned in that expedition: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the people when it was mentioned to him that water was scarce, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a caller who called that no one should come to the water before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to it and found a group had come to it before him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed them that day."
"2790","261 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Asfahani narrated to us, Abu Masud Ahmad ibn al-Furat narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Abdillah ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the expedition of Tabuk until he reached a pass, so he ordered his caller who called: Let no one take the pass, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) takes it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was going with Hudhayfah leading him and Ammar driving him, when a group of veiled men came on mounts until they crowded the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so Ammar turned back and struck the faces of the mounts. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Hudhayfah: Drive on, drive on, then Ammar caught up, so he said: Drive, drive, until he made the camel kneel. Then he said to Ammar: Do you know the people? He said: No, they were veiled, though I recognized most of the mounts. He said: Do you know what they intended against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They intended to plot against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and throw him from the pass. Then after that a dispute arose between Ammar and one of them as happens between people, so he said: I adjure you by Allah, how many were the people of the pass who intended to plot against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: You see they were fourteen; if you were among them then they were fifteen. And Ammar bears witness that twelve of them are at war with Allah and His Messenger in the life of this world and on the day the witnesses stand."
"2791","Another 262 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ubayd al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Prophethood has gone, so there is no prophethood after me, and there remain the bearers of glad tidings: the believer's dream which he sees or which is seen for him."
"2792","263 - And my maternal uncle, Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad informed them, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim ibn Bishr al-Narsi informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Shafii informed us, Muadh - he is Ibn al-Muthanna - narrated to us, Abdullah - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Asma - narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ubayd al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Prophethood has gone, so there is no prophethood after me, and there remain the bearers of glad tidings: the believer's dream which he sees or which is seen for him."
"2793","264 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Arim Abu al-Numan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ubayd al-Rasibi narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prophethood after me except the bearers of glad tidings. It was said: And what are the bearers of glad tidings? He said: The righteous dream. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yunus ibn Muhammad, from Hammad ibn Zayd. Al-Tabarani said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma and others narrated it from Mahdi ibn Maymun, from Uthman ibn Ubayd, from Abu al-Tufayl, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as Hammad ibn Zayd narrated it. And Abu Asim narrated it from Mahdi ibn Maymun, from Uthman, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2794","Another 265 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Najiyah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishkab narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Mihzam, from Maruf ibn Kharrabudh, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a she-camel between al-Safa and al-Marwah."
"2795","266 - And from Abu al-Tufayl who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to Zamzam; so he said: Draw water and give me to drink, for were I not afraid you would be overcome over it I would descend and draw."
"2796","267 - And Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Dimashqi - there - informed us, that his grandfather al-Husayn informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Missisi informed us, Talhah ibn Ali ibn al-Saqr informed us, Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Yahya al-Adami informed us, Abbas - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Duri - narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihzam informed us, from Maruf, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to Zamzam; so he said: Draw, give me to drink, for were I not afraid you would be overcome over it I would descend and draw."
"2797","Another 268 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Imran al-Mazini narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl when asked: Did you see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. It was said: Did you speak to him? He said: No, but I saw him set out to such-and-such place with Abdullah ibn Masud and some of his companions, until he came to a wide house and said: Open this door. So it was opened, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and I entered with him, and there was a blanket in the middle of the door, so he said: Lift this blanket. So they lifted the blanket and there was a one-eyed boy under the blanket. So he said: Stand, O boy. Then he said: O boy, do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? The boy said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this - twice."
"2798","269 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uqbah al-Shaybani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us. (Ha). Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, they said: Mahdi ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out with a group of his companions among them Abdullah ibn Masud, and they came to a great house, and there was a boy covered with a blanket. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? The boy said: Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge with Allah from the evil of this. Abu al-Tufayl said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day while I was a boy in a waist-wrapper."
"2799","270 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Imran narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl when it was said to him: Like whom were you when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent? He said: I was a boy who had tightened a waist-wrapper on myself."
"2800","271 - Another: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abjar or Ibn Abjar informed me, he narrated from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Describe him to me. He said: I saw a man on a camel at al-Safa, or at al-Safa and al-Marwah, with people crowding over him while he dried the back of his hand with the camel's fur. He said: That is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they were not pushed away from him nor rebuked. Zuhayr said: He dries his hand - I think from a wound. Khalaf al-Wasiti mentioned in Atraf al-Sahih that Muslim brought: I saw him on his she-camel at the standing place with many people over him, from Muhammad ibn Rafi, from Yahya ibn Adam, from Zuhayr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Said ibn Abjar, from Abu al-Tufayl. And it was said: It is not in Muslim; if Khalaf found it in some copies, Allah knows best."
"2801","Another 272 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: The Kabah in pre-Islamic times was built of piled stones with no clay in it, as high as a young goat could leap, and it was unroofed; its garments were only placed on it then let down over it. The Black Stone was placed on its wall exposed, and it had two corners like a ring. Then a ship came from Roman land, and when they were near Jeddah the ship broke, so Quraysh went out to take its timber, and they found a Roman with it, so they took the timber - he gave it to them. The ship was heading to Abyssinia, and the Roman in the ship was a carpenter. So they came with the timber and brought the Roman. Quraysh said: We will build with this timber in the ship the House of our Lord. When they wanted to demolish it, there was a snake on the wall of the House like a piece of a beam, black-backed and white-bellied. Whenever anyone approached the House to demolish it and take of its stones, it rushed at him with open mouth. So Quraysh gathered at the Maqam and cried out to Allah and said: Our Lord, You were not frightened; we intended honoring Your House and adorning it; if You are pleased with that, otherwise do what seems to You. Then they heard a rumble in the sky, and there was a bird black-backed and white-bellied and legged, greater than an eagle, which drove its talon into the head of the snake and carried it off dragging it, its trailing tail greater than such-and-such, falling. So it carried it toward Ajyad. Then Quraysh demolished it and built it with valley stones which Quraysh carried on their necks, and they raised it twenty cubits into the sky. While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was carrying stones from Ajyad wearing a striped garment, the garment became tight on him, so he went to put the garment on his shoulder and his private part showed from the smallness of the garment, so he was called: O Muhammad, cover your private part. So he was never seen naked after that. Between the building of the Kabah and his revelation were five years, and between his departure and its building fifteen years."
"2802","273 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi al-Kufi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: I said: Tell me about the building of the Kabah before Quraysh built it. He said: It was built of Wars stone, not clay, which a young goat could leap, and the covering was placed on the walls. Then a Roman ship came until at a place - he mentioned it - it broke. Quraysh heard of it and rode to it, took its timber, and a Roman called Balum, a carpenter. When they came to Makkah they said: If only we build the House of our Lord. So they gathered for that and carried stones, stones of the outskirts. While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was carrying them his private part became uncovered, so he was called: O Muhammad, cover your private part. That was the first time he was called, and Allah knows best, and his private part was never seen after that. When they gathered the stones and set about pulling it down, a snake came out, black-backed and white-bellied, its head like a kid's head, preventing them whenever they wanted to demolish it. When they saw that they withdrew at the Maqam and said: Our Lord, we intended building Your House. Then a bird descended, black-backed, white-bellied, yellow-legged, which seized it and dragged it until it brought it into Ajyad. Then they demolished it and built it twenty cubits high. Abu al-Tufayl said: So Quraysh borrowed some of the timber. Imam Ahmad narrated from it the mention of the building of the Kabah and his saying: While the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was carrying stones from Ajyad wearing a striped garment, and its end: He was never seen naked after that, from Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Tabarani narrated from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq al-Himsi, from Yahya ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Missisi, from Abdullah ibn Waqid, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Nafi ibn Sarjis who said: I said to Abu al-Tufayl: How was the Kabah in pre-Islamic times? So he mentioned like the hadith of Mamar."
"2803","Another 274 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fudayl narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Amir ibn Wathilah who said: On the day of Hunayn a man with cropped or shaved head came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: You did not act justly? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: If I do not act justly, who will act justly? He said: Then attention turned from the man and he left. So he said: Where is the man? So he was sought but not found. So he said: There will emerge from my ummah a people with this mark who pass through the religion as the arrow passes through the game; he looks at his arrow-shaft and sees nothing, looks at its binding and sees nothing, looks at its feathers and sees nothing. It has a witness in the Two Sahihs similarly from the hadith of Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Said al-Khudri."
"2804","Another 275 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar ibn Ahmad - at Naysabur - informed us, that Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them - recitation to him - Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Hamdun informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Khalid ibn Faris al-Dhuhli narrated to us. (Ha). 276 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, they said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Amir ibn Wathilah, that a man passed by people in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted them, and they returned the greeting. When he passed them, a man of the people said: By Allah, I hate this man for Allah. The gathering people said: By Allah, evil is what you said; by Allah we shall tell him. Stand, O so-and-so - to a man of them - catch him and tell him what this man said. So their messenger caught him and told him what the man said. So the man turned and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a gathering of Muslims among them so-and-so, and I greeted them and they returned the greeting. When I passed them a man of them caught me and said: So-and-so said: By Allah, I hate this man for Allah, so call him and ask him why he hates me? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and asked him about what the man told him, so he admitted it and said: I said that to him, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why do you hate him? He said: I am his neighbor and I know him well; by Allah I never saw him pray any prayer but this prescribed one. The man said: Ask him, O Messenger of Allah, did he ever see me delay it past its time, or perform its ablution badly, or its bowing or prostration badly? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him about that. He said: No. By Allah, I never saw him fast any day but this month which the righteous and the wicked fast. The man said: Ask him, O Messenger of Allah, did he see me break fast in it or diminish any of its right? He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him, and he said: No. He said: By Allah, I never saw him give a beggar or poor person anything, nor saw him spend of his wealth in any path of good except this charity which the righteous and wicked give. He said: Ask him, O Messenger of Allah, did I ever conceal any of the zakat or bargain with its seeker who asks it? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him about that, and he said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stand; I do not know, perhaps he is better than you. This is the wording of Muhammad ibn Yahya's hadith. 277 - Muhammad ibn Yahya said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, similarly, without mentioning Amir ibn Wathilah. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu Kamil Muzaffar ibn Mudrik, from Ibrahim ibn Sad with its chain at length. And Imam Ahmad said: Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab: that he informed him that a man in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people... without mentioning Abu al-Tufayl. Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: It reached me that Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated this hadith from memory and said: From Abu al-Tufayl, while his son Yaqub narrated it from his father without mentioning Abu al-Tufayl, so I think he erred, and the correct is Yaqub's narration, and Allah knows best. Al-Daraqutni was asked about it and said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Tufayl, while Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Qurashi of the Jazira opposed them and narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, while Mamar and others opposed them and narrated it from al-Zuhri as mursal, and that is the preserved."
"2805","Those named Aidh: Aidh ibn Amr ibn Hilal al-Muzani Abu Hubayrah - brother of Ibn Rafi Amr - may Allah be pleased with them both - 278 - Abu Zurah Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abdillah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Rawh informed us, Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalifah ibn Abdillah al-Ghubari say: I heard Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani say: While we were with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a bedouin pressed in begging, saying: O Messenger of Allah, feed me. So the Messenger of Allah stood and entered the house, took hold of the two doorposts of the room and turned to us with his face, and said: By Him in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, if you knew what is in begging as I know, no man would ask a man while he has a night's lodging. He said: Then he ordered food for him."
"2806","279 - And Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: I heard Khalifah ibn Abdillah al-Ghubari say: I heard Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani say: While we were with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a bedouin pressed him in begging, saying: O Messenger of Allah, feed me; O Messenger of Allah, give me. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, entered the house, took hold of the two doorposts of the room, turned to us with his face and said: By Him in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, if you knew what I know about begging, no man would ask a man while he has a night's lodging. Then he ordered food for him. Shubah narrated it from Bistam, from Abdullah ibn Khalifah."
"2807","280 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Yanal al-Sufi and Abu al-Fath Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi al-Asbahanis - in their book - informed us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them, Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Kassar al-Dinawari informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali al-Nasai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Umayyah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Bistam ibn Muslim, from Abdullah ibn Khalifah, from Aidh ibn Amr: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him, so he gave him. When he put his foot on the threshold of the door, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what is in begging, no one would walk to anyone asking him anything. Thus al-Nasai narrated it. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Khalifah ibn Abdillah, and it is said: Abdullah ibn Khalifah."
"2808","Another 281 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Shubah, Abu Shimr al-Dubai narrated to me, he said: I heard Aidh ibn Amr say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantam, dubba, naqir and muzaffat."
"2809","282 - And Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah who said: I heard Abu Shimr al-Dubai say: I heard Aidh ibn Amr. My father said: I said to Yahya ibn Said: al-Muzani? He said: Yes: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade hantam, dubba, naqir and muzaffat. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Jafar, from Shubah."
"2810","Another 283 - Abu Zurah al-Laftuwani - at Asbahan - informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abdillah ibn Hashraj informed us, my father narrated to me, from his father who said: Aidh ibn Amr said: I was struck by a throw while fighting before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn in my forehead."
"2811","284 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Zayd ibn al-Harish al-Ahwazi narrated to us, my father narrated to me. (Ha). 285 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn Salih al-Narsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Hashraj ibn Abdillah ibn Hashraj narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father who said: Aidh ibn Amr said: I was struck by a throw while fighting before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn in my face. When blood flowed over my face, beard and chest, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took with his hand and wiped that blood from my face and chest to my nipples, then prayed for me. Hashraj said: He used to describe to us the trace of the Messenger of Allah's hand (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the limit of what he told us: his chest, and there was a flowing white mark like a horse's blaze. This is the wording of Muhammad ibn Bashshar. In the narration of Zayd ibn al-Harish and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna: He took with his hand and wiped the blood from my face and chest to my nipples, then prayed for me. Hashraj said: Aidh used to tell us that in his life, and when he died and we washed him we looked at what people described of the trace of the Messenger of Allah's hand (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the limit of what he told us of his chest, and there was a flowing white mark like a horse's blaze."
"2812","Another 286 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Harish narrated to us. (Ha). 287 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhram narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us. (Ha). 288 - He said: And Buhlul ibn Ishaq narrated to us, my father narrated to us. (Ha). 289 - He said: And al-Qasim ibn Abbad al-Khattabi al-Basri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Buhlul al-Anbari narrated to us, they said: Hashraj ibn Abdillah ibn Hashraj informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Said who said: We visited Aidh ibn Amr on Ashura day; so he said: Milk for them, O boy. So the boy stood to a milch camel and milked it and brought them. So he said to the one on his right: Drink. He said: I am fasting. He said: May Allah accept from us and from you. Then he said to the second, who said: I am fasting, so he said the like. Then he said to the third, who said the like. So he said: Are all of you fasting? You are about to take this day as Ramadan. We used to fast this day before Ramadan was made obligatory upon us; when Ramadan was made obligatory upon us, the fast of Ramadan abrogated the fast of this day. This day is voluntary, not obligatory; whoever wishes let him fast, and whoever wishes let him break. When the people heard that from him they all broke fast. The wording is Zayd ibn al-Harish's hadith."
"2813","Another 290 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Saylahini narrated to us, Hashraj ibn Abdillah ibn Hashraj narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from Aidh ibn Amr who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a campaign, and when we returned toward Madinah the wife of a man martyred with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept. So he said: Who is this weeping woman? They said: Fatimah bint Adi. So he turned to Aidh ibn Amr and married her to him and commended her to him."
"2814","Another 291 - Abu Zurah Ubaydullah al-Laftuwani informed us: that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abdillah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, Hashraj ibn Abdillah - meaning Ibn Hashraj - narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Aidh ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Islam prevails and is not prevailed over. Hashraj ibn Abdillah ibn Hashraj ibn Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani Abu Sakhr - Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him without mentioning any criticism of him."
"2815","Another 292 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Shayban narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Ahwal, from Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever gets something of this provision without asking nor aspiring, let him expand in his provision; and whoever is independent of it, let him direct it to one more needy of it than him."
"2816","293 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us. (Ha). 294 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Aidh ibn Amr al-Muzani, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever gets something of this provision without asking nor aspiring of soul, let him expand in his provision; and whoever is independent of it, let him direct it to one more needy of it than him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Waki and Yunus and Hasan ibn Musa and Abd al-Samad, all from Abu al-Ashhab. In Abd al-Samad's narration I think he raised it. In Waki's narration I think he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah, blessed and exalted, brings provision without asking, let him accept it. Abdullah said: I asked my father, what is aspiring? He said: Your soul says: So-and-so will send to me, so-and-so will join me. Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid - some scholars spoke about him. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Trustworthy, no harm in him. Yahya ibn Main said: No harm in him, and Muslim narrated from him."
"2817","Aidh ibn Qurt - may Allah be pleased with him - 295 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Kharijah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays al-Sakuni who said: I heard Aidh ibn Qurt say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays a prayer without completing it, it is completed for him from his supererogatory prayers until it is complete."
"2818","Those named Abbad: Abbad ibn Bishr ibn Waqsh al-Ansari al-Ashhali - may Allah be pleased with him - (he witnessed Badr) 296 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz and Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, they said: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit al-Ansari, from Abbad ibn Bishr al-Ansari who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Ansar, you are the inner garment and people are the outer garment; let me not be reached from your side."
"2819","297 - And Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Sultan - at Baghdad - informed us, that Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Muqri informed them, Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khayyat al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Bishran informed us, Abu Muhammad Dalaj ibn Ahmad ibn Dalaj narrated to us, al-Qabbani - he is al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad - narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said al-Darimi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail and Abu Abdillah al-Khuzai narrated to us, that Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to them, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit, from Abbad ibn Bishr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Ansar, you are the inner garment and people are the outer garment, so let me not be reached from your side."
"2820","Abbad ibn Shurahbil al-Ghubari - may Allah be pleased with him - 298 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr who said: I heard Abbad ibn Shurahbil - and he was of us, of Banu Gh ubar - say: A year of drought struck us, so I came to Madinah and entered a garden of its gardens, took an ear, rubbed it, ate of it and carried some in my garment. The owner of the garden came, beat me and took my garment. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You neither taught him when ignorant, nor fed him when hungry or starving. So he returned my garment to me and ordered for me half a wasq or a wasq."
"2821","299 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Zurah Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us. (Ha). 300 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abu Muslim al-Kashshi and Uthman ibn Umar al-Dabbi narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abbad ibn Shurahbil who said: I came to Madinah struck by severe hunger, so I entered a garden, took an ear, ate it and put some in my garment. The owner of the garden came, beat me and took my garment. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You neither taught him when ignorant, nor fed him when hungry. And he ordered for me half a wasq of barley, and ordered him and he returned my garment to me. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Ghundar, from Shubah. And from Abdullah ibn Muadh, from his father, from Shubah. Al-Nasai narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Mansur, from Mubashshir ibn Abdillah ibn Razin, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from Abu Bishr. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Shabbabah. And from Bundar and Muhammad ibn al-Walid, from Muhammad ibn Jafar, all from Shubah."
"2822","Abbad ibn Amr - may Allah be pleased with him - 301 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Bishr ibn Suhar al-Araji narrated to me, al-Muarik ibn Bishr ibn Abbad - and more than one of my uncles - informed me, from Abbad ibn Amr: that he used to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); a Jew spoke to him and his cloak fell from his shoulder, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked the seal to be seen, so I straightened it on him. He said: Who did this? I said: I. He said: Move to me. So I sat before him, and he put his hand on my head and passed it over my face and chest, and said: When anything comes to us, come to me. So I came to him, and he ordered for me a young she-camel. The seal was on the edge of his left shoulder like a goat's knee."
"2823","Ubadah ibn al-Samit ibn Qays ibn Asram ibn Fihr ibn Thalabah ibn Ghanm ibn Salim ibn Awf ibn Amr ibn Awf ibn al-Khazraj al-Ansari, a Badri - may Allah be pleased with him - Abu al-Walid. Aswad ibn Thalabah al-Shami from Ubadah. 302 - Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi - at Asbahan - informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us. (Ha). 303 - And Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi - at al-Harim - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me. (Ha). 304 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi - at Asbahan - informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, they said: Waki narrated to us. Ahmad ibn Mani said from Ibn al-Jarrah: al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Thalabah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I taught writing and Quran to people of the Suffah, so a man of them gifted me a bow. I said: It is not wealth, and I will shoot with it in Allah's path. So I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If it pleases you to be collared with a collar of fire, accept it. In Ibn Mani's narration: I taught some people; with him: if I shoot with it; the rest of their wordings are the same."
"2824","305 - And Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us, that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us, Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah informed us - recitation to him - it was said to him: Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to you, my grandfather and Abu Khaythamah and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Abdullah ibn Amr narrated to us, the wording of my grandfather: Waki narrated to us, from Mughirah ibn Ziyad, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Thalabah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I taught people of the Suffah writing and Quran, so a man of them gifted me a bow. I said: It is not wealth, I will shoot with it in Allah's path. So I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: If it pleases you to be collared with a collar of fire from it, accept it."
"2825","306 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad, Ubadah ibn Nusayy narrated to me, from al-Aswad ibn Thalabah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I used to teach people of the Suffah writing and Quran, so a man of them gifted me a bow. I said: I will shoot with it - and it is not wealth - in Allah's path. Then it occurred to me to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a ruling, so I asked him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to teach people of the Suffah writing and Quran, so a man of them gifted me a bow. I said: I will shoot with it in Allah's path, and it is not wealth. He said: If you wish Allah to collar you with a collar of fire, accept it. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki and Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ruasi, from al-Mughirah. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Ahmasi, from Waki. Al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated it from al-Mughirah thus. And Bishr ibn Abdillah ibn Yasar narrated it from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Junadah, from Ubadah."
"2826","Another 307 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali - at Baghdad - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Surayj narrated to us, al-Muafa narrated to us, Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Thalabah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was sick with people of the Ansar visiting me, and said: Do you know what the martyr is? They fell silent. He said: Do you know what the martyr is? They fell silent. He said: Do you know what the martyr is? So I said to my wife: Prop me up. So she propped me, and I said: Whoever embraces Islam, emigrates, then is killed in Allah's path, he is a martyr. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: being killed in Allah's path is martyrdom, the belly is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, and the woman in childbed is martyrdom."
"2827","308 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari narrated to us, Ali ibn Harb al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from al-Aswad ibn Thalabah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I fell ill and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me with a group of Ansar, and they mentioned martyrdom. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you count martyrdom among you? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So I said: Prop me up to you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, whoever embraces Islam, emigrates, then is killed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: killing is martyrdom, drowning, the one with belly disease is martyrdom, and the woman dying in childbed is martyrdom."
"2828","Thabit ibn al-Simt al-Shami from Ubadah. 309 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Harawi - at Baghdad - informed us, that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Harithi narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sad ibn Aws narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Yahya al-Absi, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of my ummah will deem wine lawful under a name they call it."
"2829","310 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid and Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafis informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sad ibn Aws narrated to us, from Bilal al-Absi, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of my ummah will deem wine lawful under a name they call it."
"2830","311 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them - recitation to him while present - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab narrated to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sad ibn Aws, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of my ummah deems wine lawful under a name they call it."
"2831","312 - And Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sad ibn Aws al-Katib narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Yahya al-Absi, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of my ummah will deem wine lawful under a name they call it."
"2832","313 - And Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us, that Ismail ibn Ahmad al-Samarqandi informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us, Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sad ibn Aws narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sad, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of my ummah will drink wine under a name they call it."
"2833","314 - And with it Abdullah al-Baghawi narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Harun ibn Abdillah and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Sad ibn Aws, from Bilal ibn Yahya, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah will deem wine lawful under a name they call it. Abu al-Qasim said to us: This is the end of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah's hadith; Harun and Ahmad ibn Mansur added, the wording in the addition is Harun's. Sad said: Bilal met Ubadah ibn al-Samit while I was with him and mentioned that, so he said: Yes, that has happened. Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Sari, from Abdullah, from Sad ibn Aws similarly. Sad ibn Aws - al-Azdi weakened him, and he is Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Mawsili who was criticized, so his weakening is not accepted, and Allah knows best."
"2834","Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari from Ubadah - may Allah be pleased with them both - 315 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Hurdi - at Baghdad - informed us, that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb ibn Surayj ibn Miqal al-Shashi informed us, Abbas al-Duri narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, Shayban informed us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah who said: Jabir ibn Abdillah informed me: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed about umra that it belongs to whom it was granted."
"2835","He said: And he informed me that Ubadah ibn al-Samit asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying: Those who believed and were God-fearing - for them is glad tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have asked me about something none asked me before you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is the righteous dream which the Muslim sees or which is seen for him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Waki, from Ali ibn al-Mubarak, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Ubadah, without mentioning Jabir in it. And Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it from Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb, from Waki, likewise. This hadith with Jabir's narration from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is more fitting; but al-Haytham al-Shashi narrated it in the Musnad of Ubadah."
"2836","Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami from Ubadah. 316 - Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to them: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim man on the face of the earth who calls upon Allah - mighty and majestic - with a supplication but Allah gives it to him or averts from him like it of evil, so long as he does not call with sin or severing kinship."
"2837","317 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban narrated to us, from his father, from Makhul, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, that Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to them: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim man on the face of the earth who calls upon Allah with a supplication but Allah gives it to him and averts from him like it of evil, so long as he does not call with sin or severing kinship. A man of the people said: Then we will increase. He said: Allah is greater. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Darimi, from Muhammad ibn Yusuf similarly, and said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith from this path. Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam - we brought him for corroboration."
"2838","Another 318 - Abu Jafar Muhammad informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Amr ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala ibn Zibriq narrated to us, my uncle Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us. (Ha). 319 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ala al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, he said: I heard my father refer it to Makhul, refer it to Jubayr ibn Nufayr, refer it to Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul that dies in good standing with Allah which loves to return to you though it has the bliss of this world and all in it, except the one slain in Allah's path, for he loves to return and be killed again for what he sees of Allah's reward for him. It has a witness in the Two Sahihs similarly from Shubah's narration, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): None who enters Paradise loves to return to this world though he has all on earth except the martyr, for he wishes to return to this world to be killed ten times for what he sees of honor."
"2839","Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Azdi al-Shami from Ubadah. 320 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Haywah ibn Shurayh and Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, they said: Baqiyyah narrated to us, Bahir ibn Sad narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah that he narrated to them, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have told you about the Dajjal until I feared you would not understand. The false messiah, the Dajjal, is a short bow-legged man, curly-haired, one-eyed with the eye effaced, neither protruding nor sunken. If it is confused for you - Yazid said: your Lord - then know that your Lord, blessed and exalted, is not one-eyed, and you will not see your Lord, blessed and exalted, until you die. Yazid said: See your Lord until you die."
"2840","321 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Amr ibn al-Aswad, that Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to them, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I have told you about the Dajjal until I feared you would not understand. He is one-eyed, neither protruding nor sunken. Know that Allah is not one-eyed, and you will not see your Lord until you die."
"2841","322 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Bahir ibn Sad, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Amr ibn al-Aswad - meaning: from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah - from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have warned you of the Dajjal until I feared you would not understand. The false messiah, the Dajjal, is short, bow-legged, curly-haired, one-eyed with the eye effaced, neither protruding nor sunken. If it is confused for you, know that your Lord is not one-eyed, and you will not see your Lord until you die. Abu Dawud narrated it from Haywah ibn Shurayh. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq ibn Rahawayh."
"2842","Another 323 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Bishr ibn Abdillah ibn Yasar narrated to us. (Ha). 324 - Al-Tabarani said: And Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Nuaym ibn Hammad narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Bishr ibn Abdillah ibn Yasar narrated to me, Ubadah ibn Nusayy narrated to me, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be busy; when a man came emigrating to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he entrusted him to one of us to teach him Quran. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me a man who was with me in the house, or he said: with the household, and I taught him Quran. Then he left to his family, seeing he owed a right, so he gifted me a bow the like of whose wood in quality and curve in beauty I never saw. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What do you think, O Messenger of Allah, about it? He said: A coal between your shoulders you have shouldered or hung."
"2843","325 - And with it Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Ibn Irq - he is Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa and Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Bishr ibn Abdillah ibn Yasar narrated to us, Ubadah ibn Nusayy narrated to me, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be busy; when a man came emigrating to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he entrusted him to one of us to teach him Quran. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entrusted to me a man who was with me in the house; I gave him the household's supper and taught him Quran. Then he left to his family, seeing he owed a right, so he gifted me a bow whose wood in quality and curve I never saw better. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: What do you think about it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A coal between your shoulders you have shouldered or hung. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu al-Mughirah like the hadith of Amr and Ibn Musaffa. Abu Dawud narrated it from Amr ibn Uthman and Kathir ibn Ubayd, from Baqiyyah. Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated it from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Aswad ibn Thalabah, from Ubadah, already covered. I think Ubadah ibn Nusayy preserved it from both, and Allah knows best."
"2844","Another 326 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Salman - a man of Syria - from Junadah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I visited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he suffered pain whose severity Allah knows, and I visited him in the evening while recovered. So he said: O son of al-Samit, Jibril - peace be upon him - performed ruqyah on me and I recovered; shall I not teach it to you? I said: Yes. In Allah's name I perform ruqyah on you from everything that harms you, from the envy of every envier and the eye; in Allah's name He heals you. Al-Nasai narrated it in the Book of Day and Night, from Khushaysh ibn Asram al-Nasai, from Muhammad ibn al-Fadl Arim, from Thabit ibn Yazid, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Salman a man of Syria."
"2845","Another 327 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us. (Ha). 328 - And Abu Jafar informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, they said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us. 329 - In Muhammad ibn Ridhah's narration, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, and Muhammad ibn al-Abbas al-Muaddib narrated to us, Ali ibn Salih al-Ijli narrated to us, they said: Ibn Thawban narrated to us, Umayr ibn Hani narrated to me, he said: I heard Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah say: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that Jibril, peace be upon him, performed ruqyah on him while he ailed, saying: In Allah's name I perform ruqyah on you from every disease that harms you, from every envier when he envies, from every eye, and Allah heals you."
"2846","330 - And Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban informed us, from Umayr ibn Hani, that he heard Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Kindi say: I heard Ubadah narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that Jibril came to him while he trembled with fever and said: In Allah's name I perform ruqyah on you from everything that harms you; from every envy of an envier and every eye, and Allah's name heals you."
"2847","331 - And with it Abdullah narrated to us, my father said: Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us and mentioned the like except he said: from the envy of an envier and from every eye; Allah's name heals you. Ibn Majah narrated it from Amr ibn Uthman, from Said, from his father, from Ibn Thawban similarly. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from al-Sakhtiyani - he is Imran ibn Musa - from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Zayd ibn al-Hubab."
"2848","Another 332 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Abdillah al-Iyadi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ziyad al-Awzai narrated to us, Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to us, Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, keep me alive poor, make me die poor, and gather me among the poor."
"2849","333 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ziyad al-Awzai narrated to me, Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to us, Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, let me live poor, make me die poor, and gather me among the poor."
"2850","Al-Harith ibn Muawiyah al-Kindi from Ubadah - may Allah be pleased with him - 334 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi - at Baghdad - informed us, that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Khalili informed us, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khuzai informed us, al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq Abu Bakr narrated to us. (Ha). 335 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Ismail ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Karimah al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Abd al-Rahim, Mansur al-Khawlani narrated to me, from Abu Yazid Ghaylan, freedman of Banu Kinanah, from Abu Sallam al-Habashi, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Wahbi, from al-Harith ibn Muawiyah, Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to us - with Abu al-Darda with him - that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward a camel of the spoils; when he finished his prayer he took a lint between his fingers, a fluff, and said: Behold, this is of your spoils, and I have in it only the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. So render the thread and needle, smaller and greater, for misappropriation returns upon its people in this world and the Hereafter. Strive in Allah against near and far, care not in Allah the blame of a blamer, establish Allah's limits in settled and travel, and upon you is jihad, for it is a great gate of Paradise by which Allah saves from grief and worry. This is Musa ibn Harun's wording. In Muhammad ibn Ishaq's narration: toward a camel of the division; with him: I have of it only the fifth; with him: the near of you and far; with him: a gate of good; the rest the same. Abu al-Mughirah and Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu Sallam al-Aswad, from al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi, that he sat with Ubadah ibn al-Samit, Abu al-Darda and al-Harith ibn Muawiyah al-Kindi, and they mentioned the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the fifths."
"2851","Hubaysh al-Habashi Abu Hafsah al-Shami from Ubadah. 336 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us, that Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Karkhi informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Thabit al-Khatib informed us, al-Qasim ibn Jafar al-Hashimi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Lului informed us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn al-Ashath narrated to us, Jafar ibn Musafir al-Hudhali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Rabah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Abu Hafsah who said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: O my son, you will not find the taste of true faith until you learn that what struck you would never miss you, and what missed you would never strike you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first thing Allah created was the Pen; He said to it: Write. It said: Lord, what shall I write? He said: Write the decrees of everything until the Hour comes. O my son, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever dies upon other than this is not of me. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it."
"2852","Hamzah ibn al-Zubayr from Ubadah - may Allah be pleased with him - 337 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Irq narrated to us, Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hajir narrated to us, from Junayd ibn Maymun Abu Abd al-Hamid, from Hamzah ibn al-Zubayr, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer's dream is speech by which the servant's Lord speaks to him in sleep."
"2853","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yazani, and it is said Ibn Ubaydillah al-Muzani - I think more correct - from Ubadah. 338 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yazani narrated to me, that a man asked Ubadah ibn al-Samit about Allah's saying: For them is glad tidings in the life of this world. Ubadah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You have asked me about a matter none of my ummah asked me about. That is the righteous dream which the believer sees or which is seen for him."
"2854","339 - And the shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, al-Hawti narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr al-Saksaki and Umar ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Ahmusi narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Abdillah, that he narrated to them from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that a man asked him about this verse: For them is glad tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. Ubadah said: You have asked me about something none asked me before you, and I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You have asked about something none of my ummah asked me before you. It is the righteous dream which the righteous man sees or which is seen for him."
"2855","340 - And with it Ahmad ibn Musa al-Hafiz informed us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Sahl ibn Abdillah ibn al-Farrukhan narrated to us, Abu al-Qasim Zibriq al-Himsi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Humayd al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he was asked about His saying: For them is glad tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. He said: The righteous dream which the believer sees or which is seen for him. Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated it from Safwan ibn Amr, from Humayd ibn Abdillah."
"2856","Khalid ibn Madan al-Kalai al-Himsi from Ubadah. 341 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Rabi ibn Thalab narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Uqbah ibn Abi al-Ayzar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah say: Whoever recites ten verses in a night is not written among the heedless; whoever recites a hundred verses, a night's devotion is written for him; whoever recites two hundred verses is written among the devout; whoever recites four hundred is written among the humble; whoever recites a thousand verses wakes with a qintar of a thousand and two hundred ounces, an ounce better than what is between heaven and earth; and whoever recites two thousand verses is of those who earn Paradise."
"2857","Another 342 - Al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, Bahir ibn Sad narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Laylat al-Qadr is in the remaining ten; whoever stands them seeking their reward, Allah, blessed and exalted, forgives him his past and later sins. It is an odd night: ninth, seventh, fifth, third or last night. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sign of Laylat al-Qadr is that it is clear, bright, as if a shining moon in it, calm, serene, neither cold nor hot in it, and no star may be cast with in it until morning. Its sign is that the sun on its morning rises level with no rays, like the moon on full-moon night; Satan may not come out with it that day. Rabiah ibn Najidh al-Asadi, and it is said al-Azdi al-Kufi, from Ubadah."
"2858","343 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Abdullah ibn Salim al-Mafluj narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabiah ibn Najidh, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take a fluff from a camel's side of the spoils then say: I have in it only like one of you. Then he said: Beware misappropriation, for misappropriation is disgrace upon its doer on Resurrection Day. So render the thread and needle and above that, strive in Allah against near and far in settled and travel, for jihad is a gate of Paradise; it saves its doer from worry and grief. Establish Allah's limits for near and far, and let no blamer's blame seize you in Allah."
"2859","344 - And Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr al-Harimi - at al-Harim - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salim al-Kufi al-Mafluj - trustworthy - narrated to me, Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabiah ibn Najidh, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take a fluff from a camel's side of the spoils then say: I have in it only like one of you of it. Beware misappropriation, for misappropriation is disgrace upon its doer on Resurrection Day. Render the thread and needle and above that, strive in Allah's path against near and far in settled and travel, for jihad is a gate of Paradise's gates; Allah, blessed and exalted, saves by it from worry and grief. Establish Allah's limits for near and far, and let no blamer's blame seize you in Allah."
"2860","345 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani - there - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal and Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Hadrami narrated to us, they said: Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid, from Abu Sadiq, from Rabiah ibn Najidh, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to take a fluff from a camel's side of the spoils and say: I have in it only like one of you. Beware misappropriation, for it is disgrace upon its doer on Resurrection Day. So render the thread and needle and above that, establish Allah's limits for near and far, let no blamer's blame seize you in Allah. Jihad is a gate of Paradise's gates by which Allah saves its doer from worry and grief. Ibn Majah narrated some of it from Abdullah ibn Salim. Abu Sadiq's name is Muslim ibn Yazid al-Azdi, and it is said Abdullah ibn Najidh, brother of Rabiah ibn Najidh."
"2861","Abu Umamah Sudayy ibn Ajlan al-Bahili from Ubadah - may Allah be pleased with him - 346 - Abu Zurah Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani - at Asbahan - informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abdillah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to grant a fourth at the outset and a third on return."
"2862","347 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi - at Asbahan - informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam al-Araj, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted a fourth at the outset and a third on return."
"2863","348 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from al-Thawri, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to grant a fourth at his outset, and when returning a third. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Waki like Zuhayr's narration. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar and said: A hasan hadith. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ali ibn Muhammad al-Tanafisi, from Waki."
"2864","Ziyad ibn Abi Sawdah from Ubadah. 349 - Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibatullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn Tawus - at Damascus - informed us, that al-Sharif Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Abbas al-Husayni and Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Hinnai and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Tahir ibn Jafar al-Sulami said: Abu Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yahya ibn Sulwan al-Mazini informed us, he said: Abu al-Qasim al-Fadl ibn Jafar al-Tamimi al-Muadhdhin informed us, he said: Abu Bakr Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Faraj ibn Abd al-Samad al-Hashimi informed us, Abu Mushir Abd al-Ala ibn Mushir al-Ghassani narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Sawdah who said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit was seen on the eastern wall of Bayt al-Maqdis weeping. It was said: What makes you weep, O Abu al-Walid? He said: From here the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us he saw Hell. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi, from Abu Nasr al-Tammar, from Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Ziyad ibn Abi Sawdah. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: I do not think he heard from Ubadah ibn al-Samit. I say: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated from Ziyad ibn Abi Sawdah that he heard his brother Uthman ibn Abi Sawdah say: I saw Ubadah ibn al-Samit with his chest on the mosque wall overlooking the valley of Hell weeping, and he mentioned it."
"2865","Salamah ibn Shurayh al-Shami from Ubadah. 350 - Abu Zurah al-Laftuwani informed us, that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them, Abd al-Rahman al-Razi informed us, Jafar informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid informed us, Sayyar ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me. 351 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Allaf narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Qawdhar, from Salamah ibn Shurayh, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined on us seven traits, saying: Do not associate anything with Allah though you are cut, burned or crucified; do not deliberately abandon prayer, for whoever deliberately abandons it has left the religion; do not ride disobedience, for it is Allah's wrath; do not approach wine, for it is the head of all sins; do not flee from death or killing though you are in it; do not disobey your parents though they order you to leave the whole world, so leave; do not lift your stick from your family and be just to them from yourself. This is al-Allaf's wording; in Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahim's narration with seven qualities... Do not associate; with him: do not approach wine, for it is the head of sins; the rest the same."
"2866","Shurahbil ibn al-Simt from Ubadah. 352 - Al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Shubah who said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated to me, from Ibn al-Musabbih - or Abu al-Musabbih - from Ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Abdullah ibn Rawahah without moving from his bed for him. He said: Who are my ummah's martyrs? They said: A Muslim's killing is martyrdom. He said: Then my ummah's martyrdom is few: a Muslim's killing is martyrdom, plague is martyrdom, belly and drowning, and the woman killed by her child in full pregnancy."
"2867","353 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abu Musabbih or Ibn Musabbih - a man of Syria - from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Ibn Rawahah without moving from his bed for him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who are my ummah's martyrs? They said: Killing. He said: Then my ummah's martyrs are few: killing is martyrdom, plague is martyrdom, belly is martyrdom, and the woman killed by her child in full pregnancy."
"2868","354 - And with it, Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Abu Musabbih, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: We visited Abdullah ibn Rawahah when he fainted. We said: May Allah have mercy on you; we would love you to die otherwise, and we hope martyrdom for you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered while we mentioned this; so he said: What do you count martyrdom? The people fell silent, and Abdullah moved and said: Will you not answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Then he himself answered and said: We count martyrdom in killing. So he said: Then my ummah's martyrs are few: in killing is martyrdom, in plague is martyrdom, in belly is martyrdom, in drowning is martyrdom, and in the woman in childbed killed by her child in full pregnancy is martyrdom."
"2869","Another 355 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi - there - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a fluff from a camel's side and said: O people, nothing of what Allah granted you is lawful for me but the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you."
"2870","356 - And with it Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is jihad in Allah's path - blessed and exalted - for it is a gate of Paradise's gates by which Allah removes worry and grief."
"2871","357 - And with it Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq - meaning al-Fazari - narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Render the thread and needle, and beware misappropriation, for it is shame upon its people on Resurrection Day."
"2872","358 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is jihad in Allah's path, for it is a gate of Paradise's gates by which Allah removes worry and grief."
"2873","359 - And with it Muhammad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Render the thread and needle, and beware misappropriation, for it is shame upon its people on Resurrection Day. Al-Nasai narrated: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took on Hunayn day a fluff from a camel's side, to his saying: returned to you, from Amr ibn Yahya ibn al-Harith, from Mahbub ibn Musa, from Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash, from Sulayman with its chain without Sufyan in it. The next is not in Ahmad's narration with Sufyan mentioned; Muhammad ibn al-Nadr mentioned him. Perhaps Abu Ishaq heard it from Abd al-Rahman and from Sufyan from him, narrating once from Abd al-Rahman and once from Sufyan from him, and Allah knows best."
"2874","Another 360 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I witnessed Badr with him. People met and Allah - blessed and exalted - routed the enemy. A group set out in their tracks routing and killing, a group devoted to the camp guarding and gathering it, and a group surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lest the enemy catch him unaware. When night came and people returned to one another, those who gathered the spoils said: We collected and gathered it, none has a share in it. Those who went seeking the enemy said: You are no more entitled to it than us; we repelled the enemy from it and routed them. Those who surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are no more entitled to it than us; we surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fearing the enemy would catch him unaware, occupied with him. Then was revealed: They ask you about the spoils; say, the spoils are for Allah and the Messenger, so fear Allah and set right your relations. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it equally among the Muslims. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided enemy land he granted a fourth, and when returning with all people he granted a third. He disliked extra spoils and said: Let the strong of the believers return to their weak."
"2875","361 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Yazid al-Qaratis i narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Sallam al-Bahili, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Badr and met the enemy. When Allah routed them, a group of Muslims followed them killing them, a group surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a group seized the camp and plunder. When Allah repelled the enemy and those who sought them returned, they said: Ours is the extra share; we sought the enemy, by us Allah repelled and routed them. Those who seized the camp said: By Allah, you are no more entitled than us; we collected and seized it. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: They ask you about the spoils; say, the spoils are for Allah and the Messenger, so fear Allah and set right your relations and obey Allah and His Messenger if you are believers. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it among them. He used to grant them a fourth when they set out at the start, and a third when returning. He said: On Hunayn day he took a fluff from a camel's side and said: O people, nothing of what Allah granted you is lawful for me but the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. So render the thread and needle, beware misappropriation, for it is shame upon its people on Resurrection Day. Upon you is jihad in Allah's path, for it is a gate of Paradise's gates by which Allah removes grief and worry. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked extra spoils and said: Let the strong of the believers return to their weak."
"2876","362 - And with it Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, Muhriz ibn Salamah narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah narrated to us, from his father, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Badr... and he mentioned the hadith."
"2877","363 - And the shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shukr al-Tamimi al-Muaddib - at Asbahan - informed us, that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Ahmad ibn Salman ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Hamzah al-Zubayri informed us, al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abdillah ibn Ayyash informed us, from his father, from Sulayman ibn Musa al-Ashdaq, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam al-Bahili, from Abu Umamah, companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Badr and they met the enemy. When Allah routed them, a group of Muslims followed them killing them, a group surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a group seized the camp and plunder. When Allah repelled the enemy and those who sought them returned, they said: Ours is the extra share; we sought the enemy, by us Allah repelled and routed them. Those who surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are no more entitled to it than us; rather it is ours, we collected and seized it. So Allah revealed: They ask you about the spoils; say, the spoils are for Allah and the Messenger, so fear Allah and set right your relations and obey Allah and His Messenger if you are believers. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it equally among them. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to grant them a fourth when they set out at the start, and a third when returning."
"2878","364 - And with it Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Abdillah ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa al-Ashdaq, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam al-Bahili, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to Badr and met the enemy there. When Allah routed them, a group of Muslims followed them killing them, a group surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a group seized the plunder and camp. When those who sought the enemy returned they said: Ours is the extra share; we sought the enemy, by us Allah repelled and routed them. Those who surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are no more entitled to it than us; rather it is ours, we surrounded the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lest the enemy catch him unaware. Those who seized the camp and plunder said: You are no more entitled to it than us; rather it is ours, we seized and secured it. So Allah revealed to His Messenger: They ask you about the spoils; say, the spoils are for Allah and the Messenger, so fear Allah and set right your relations, the verse. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided it equally. He used to grant them a fourth at the outset, and a third when returning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a fluff from his camel's back and said: Nothing of the fay is lawful for me but the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. So render the thread and needle, beware misappropriation, for it is shame upon its people on Resurrection Day. Upon you is jihad, for it is a gate of Paradise's gates by which Allah removes grief and worry. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked extra shares and said: The strong of the people return to their weak."
"2879","365 - And with it Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Layth narrated to us, al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rabiah, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, from Abu Sallam, from Abu Umamah who said: When Allah routed the polytheists on Badr day... and he mentioned it abridged without mentioning Ubadah. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab, from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Muhammad ibn Jahdam, from Ismail ibn Jafar, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Makhul, similarly."
"2880","Amir ibn Sharahil al-Shabi from Ubadah. 366 - Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi - at al-Harim - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Ismail Abu Mamar al-Hudhali narrated to me, Jarir narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgives a bodily injury of his body, Allah, exalted, expiates for him sins in its measure."
"2881","367 - And with it Abdullah narrated to us, Shuja ibn Makhlad narrated to me, Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi who said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is wounded in his body and forgives it as charity, Allah, mighty and majestic, expiates for him sins in the measure he forgave. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Surayj ibn al-Numan, from Hushaym, from Mughirah, from al-Shabi, that Ubadah said: I heard. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ali ibn Hujr, from Jarir similarly."
"2882","Aidhullah ibn Abdillah Abu Idris al-Khawlani from Ubadah ibn al-Samit - may Allah be pleased with him - 368 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani - at Asbahan - informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Mahmud ibn Ali al-Asbahani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Zamah ibn Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Jibril, peace be upon him, came from Allah - mighty and majestic - saying: O Muhammad, Allah - mighty and majestic - says: I made five prayers obligatory upon your ummah; whoever fulfills them with their ablutions, times, bowings and prostrations, he has with Me a covenant to admit him to Paradise. Whoever meets Me having diminished any of that has no covenant; if I wish I punish him, if I wish I have mercy on him."
"2883","Another 369 - Abu Jafar Muhammad informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Dawud al-Makki narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Yala ibn Ata, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jurashi, from Abu Idris who said: I heard from Muadh ibn Jabal, he narrated to us, then I narrated it to Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: I narrate to you only what I heard on the Messenger of Allah's tongue (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My love is due to those who love one another for Me, My love is due to those who spend for one another for Me, and My love is due to those who visit one another for Me."
"2884","370 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Baghawi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Yazid, from Abu Idris, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, mighty and majestic, said: My love is due to those who sit together for Me, My love is due to those who spend for one another for Me, and My love is due to those who meet one another for Me."
"2885","371 - And Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Waiz informed us, that Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Yala ibn Ata, from al-Walid ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Idris al-Aidhi or al-Khawlani who said: I sat in a gathering with twenty of the Prophet's companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among them a young man of tender age, handsome, dark-eyed, bright-toothed. When they differed in anything and he spoke, they ended at his word. He was Muadh ibn Jabal. Next day I came and he was praying toward a pillar; he shortened his prayer, then sat on his haunches and fell silent. So I said: By Allah, I love you for Allah's majesty. He said: By Allah? I said: By Allah. He said: Those who love one another in Allah, I think he said: are in Allah's shade on a day with no shade but His; then no doubt in the rest, meaning the rest of the hadith: Thrones of light are set for them, envied for their gathering by the prophets, truthful and martyrs from the Lord - mighty and majestic. He said: Then I narrated to Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: I narrate to you only what I heard on the Messenger of Allah's tongue (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My love is due to those who love one another for Me, My love is due to those who visit one another for Me, My love is due to those who spend for one another for Me, My love is due to those who befriend purely for Me and keep ties. Shubah doubted about those who keep ties or visit."
"2886","372 - And with it Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Abu Salih al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Awzai, a man in Yahya ibn Abi Kathir's gathering narrated to me, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani who said: I entered the Hims mosque and sat with a circle of thirty-two of the Prophet's companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). One of them would say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then narrate, then another would say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then narrate. Among them a dark-eyed man bright-toothed; when they doubted anything they referred it to him and were content with what he said. I never sat before or after a gathering like it. The people dispersed, knowing neither any man's name nor home. I spent a night like no other."
"2887","373 - And Abu al-Qasim Hibatullah ibn Ali ibn Saud ibn Thabit ibn Hashim ibn Ghalib al-Ansari - at Egypt - informed us, that Abu Jafar Yahya ibn al-Musharraf ibn Ali ibn al-Khadir al-Tammar al-Bazzar informed them - recitation to him - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Said ibn Ahmad ibn Nafis al-Muqri informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Bundar ibn Ubaydillah ibn Bundar, judge of Adhana - at Egypt - informed us, Abu Tahir al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil al-Asadi al-Balisi the Imam - at Antioch city - informed us, Salih ibn Ziyad al-Muqri and Yusuf ibn Said al-Missisi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani who said: I entered the Hims mosque and there was a circle with over thirty of the Messenger of Allah's companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man would say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say such-and-such, the others listening to him. Among them a dark-eyed youth bright-toothed; when they differed they ended at his word. When I left to my home I spent the longest night, saying: I sat in a gathering with so many of the Prophet's companions, peace be upon him, knowing neither their homes nor names. In the morning I went to the mosque and the dark-eyed youth was sitting at a pillar. I sat with him and said: I love you for Allah, exalted. He took my cloak-knot and said: By Allah, do you love me for Allah? I said: By Allah, I love you for Allah, blessed and exalted. He said: Shall I not narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those who love one another in Allah, Allah shades them in His Throne's shade on a day with no shade but His. While thus, a man of the circle passed, so I stood to him and said: He narrated to me a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); did you hear it? He said: He would narrate to you only truth; what is it? So I told him. He said: I heard this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and better than it. I said: May Allah have mercy on you, what is better than it? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) transmit from Allah, exalted: My love is due to those who love one another for Me, My love is due to those who keep ties for Me, My love is due to those who visit one another for Me, and My love is due to those who spend for one another for Me. I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am Ubadah ibn al-Samit. I said: Who is the youth? He said: Muadh ibn Jabal. Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Missisi - we brought him for corroboration. This is Muhammad ibn Kathir's wording; Hiql's narration is similar without mentioning those who keep ties. The man al-Awzai did not name in Hiql's narration from him is Yunus ibn Maysarah, and Allah knows best."
"2888","Those named Abdullah: Abdullah ibn Thuwab al-Khawlani Abu Muslim from Ubadah. 374 - Abu Abdullah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us, that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani informed us, Jafar - meaning Ibn Burqan - narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Marzuq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Muslim al-Khawlani who said: I met Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), raising it to the Lord, exalted, who said: My love is due to those who love one another for Me, My love is due to those who visit one another for Me, My love is due to those who spend for one another for Me, and My love is due to those who keep ties for Me."
"2889","375 - And Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr al-Harimi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Ahmad Makhlad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to us - dictation from his book - al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Yahya al-Fazari and Bukayr Abu Abdillah, nicknamed Abu al-Malih - meaning al-Raqqi - narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Marzuq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Muslim who said: I entered the Hims mosque and there was a circle with thirty-two of the Messenger of Allah's companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then I went out and met Ubadah ibn al-Samit. He said: I told him what Muadh narrated to me. Ubadah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrate from his Lord, blessed and exalted, that He said: My love is due to those who love one another for Me - meaning Himself - My love is due to those who advise one another for Me, My love is due to those who visit one another for Me, and My love is due to those who spend for one another for Me, thus upon pulpits of light envied for their place by the prophets and truthful."
"2890","376 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah bint Abdillah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Askari narrated to us, Said ibn Hafs al-Nufayli narrated to us, Abu al-Malih narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Marzuq, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Abu Muslim al-Khawlani who said: I met Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and Ubadah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah, exalted, says: My love is due to those who love one another for Me, My love is due to those who visit one another for Me, My love is due to those who spend for one another for Me, and My love is due to those who advise one another for Me. Those who love one another for Me are upon pulpits of light envied for their place by the prophets, truthful and martyrs. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Waki, from Jafar ibn Burqan, with in it: Those who love one another in Allah are upon pulpits of light in the Throne's shade on a day with no shade but His. And he narrated it from Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas, from Abu al-Malih."
"2891","Abdullah ibn Abbad, and it is said Ibn Ubadah al-Zuraqi from Ubadah. 377 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recitation to him while present - Ahmad ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdullah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abdillah informed us, Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Yala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abdullah ibn Abbad al-Zuraqi, that he used to hunt sparrows in the well of Ihab, and Ubadah used to take the sparrow from me and release it, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made sacred what is between its two lava tracts."
"2892","378 - And Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah - known as Ibn al-Qaris al-Harimi - informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Jafar narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad Abu Damrah narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to me, from Yala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, that Abdullah ibn Abbad al-Zuraqi informed him: that he used to hunt sparrows in the well of Ihab, and it was theirs. He said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit saw me having taken the sparrow, so he seized it from me and released it, saying: O my son, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made sacred what is between its two lava tracts as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred. 379 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: And Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki and Abu Marwan al-Uthmani Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Khalid narrated to me, they said: Abu Damrah narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah, from Yala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, that Abdullah ibn Abbad al-Zuraqi informed him: that he used to hunt sparrows in the well of Abu Ihab, and it was theirs. Ubadah saw me having taken the sparrow, so he seized it from me and released it, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made sacred what is between its two lava tracts as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred. Ubadah was of the Messenger of Allah's companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2893","380 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Yala ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Abdullah ibn Ubadah al-Zuraqi informed him, that he used to hunt sparrows in the well of Ihab, and it was theirs. Ubadah saw me having taken a sparrow, so he seized it from me and released it, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made sacred what is between its two lava tracts as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred. He said: Ubadah was of the Messenger of Allah's companions (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Tabarani brought it in the biography of Ubadah ibn al-Samit and in the biography of Ubadah al-Zuraqi. He narrated from Ali ibn al-Madini that he said: He is Ubadah ibn al-Samit al-Ansari. Likewise in Imam Ahmad's narration from him."
"2894","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Qays Abu Ubayy, son of Ubadah's wife, from Ubadah. 381 - Abu Zurah Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us, Jafar ibn Abdillah informed us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu al-Muthanna, from Abu Ubayy, son of Ubadah ibn al-Samit's wife, from Ubadah who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when they mentioned rulers. He said: There will be rulers after me delaying prayer past its appointed time. He said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we pray it with them? He said: Yes. 382 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us with this chain, adding in it: And make your prayer with them voluntary."
"2895","383 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Matush informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu al-Muthanna, from the son of Ubadah ibn al-Samit's wife, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be rulers occupied by things, delaying prayer past its time; make your prayer with them voluntary."
"2896","384 - And Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Himsi, from Abu Ubayy, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There will be rulers delaying prayer past its appointed time, so pray the prayer at its appointed time. A man said: Shall we pray with them? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hajjaj, from Shubah. And from Yamur ibn Bishr, from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak. And from Waki, both from Sufyan, without Ubadah mentioned in Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak's narration nor in Muhammad ibn Jafar's narration. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari, from Waki. And from Muhammad ibn Qudamah, from Jarir, from Mansur, from Hilal, from Abu al-Muthanna, from the son of Ubadah's sister, thus he said. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar. Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Said - we brought him for corroboration."
"2897","Those named Abd al-Rahman: Abd al-Rahman ibn Usaylah al-Sunabihi Abu Abdillah from Ubadah. 385 - Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Said al-Harbi informed us, that Hibatullah informed them, al-Hasan informed us, Ahmad informed us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mutarrif informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah al-Sunabihi who said: Abu Muhammad claimed witr is obligatory. So Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: Abu Muhammad lied. I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Five prayers Allah made obligatory upon His servants; whoever perfects their ablution, prays them at their times completing their bowing and prostration, he has with Allah a covenant to forgive him. Whoever does not, has no covenant with Allah; if He wishes He forgives him, if He wishes He punishes him."
"2898","386 - And Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Abu Zurah narrated to us, Adam narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah al-Sunabihi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Five prayers... the hadith. Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti, from Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Mutarrif. Thus we narrated it naming him Abdullah al-Sunabihi, likewise in Abu Dawud's narration. The well-known is Abu Abdillah, named Abd al-Rahman."
"2899","Another 387 - Abu Jafar Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us, that Fatimah informed them, Muhammad informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas, from al-Sunabihi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No servant prostrates to Allah a prostration but Allah writes for him a good deed by it and removes from him a sin by it."
"2900","388 - And with it, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us, Ibrahim ibn Duhaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, my father narrated to us. (Ha). 389 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Hulwani narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, they said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Ibn Halbas, from al-Sunabihi, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No servant prostrates to Allah a prostration but Allah raises him a degree by it and removes from him a sin by it."
"2901","390 - Abu Ja'far also informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them — recited to him while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Isma'il ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd al-A'la ibn Mushir narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Salih ibn Subayh al-Muzani narrated to me: Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas narrated to me, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit and al-Sunabihi met at night in the land of Byzantium, and one of them recognized his companion by his voice. Al-Sunabihi said: O Abu al-Walid. He said: At your service, O Abu Abd Allah. He said: How did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) speak about prostration? He said: I heard him say: 'There is no servant who prostrates to Allah a single prostration except that Allah raises him a degree by it and removes a sin from him by it.' Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Abbas ibn Uthman al-Dimashqi, from al-Walid ibn Muslim. And in the narration of Hisham ibn Khalid: Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated to us; so it is possible that Salih ibn Subayh was given the kunya Abu Malik, or that he erred in his lineage, for Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik is other than Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Salih ibn Subayh. This hadith has a witness in Sahih Muslim from the narration of Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2902","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from Ubadah. 391 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to me: Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, he said: Abu al-Darda and Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us: Satan has despaired of being worshipped in the Arabian Peninsula; as for the hidden desire, we have known it — it is the desires of this world, its women and its lusts."
"2903","392 - Abu Hafs Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah informed us: Abd Allah al-Baghawi narrated to us: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bahram narrated to us, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm say: We entered the mosque of al-Jabiyah — I and Abu al-Darda met Ubadah ibn al-Samit — and he took my right hand and my left, and Abu al-Darda took his right hand, and he walked out. Ubadah said: If the life of one of you or both of you is prolonged, you will soon see a man from the midst of the Muslims who has recited the Qur'an upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), repeating and displaying it, declaring its lawful lawful and its unlawful unlawful, observing its stations — yet his recitation upon the tongue of any one of you carries no more weight than the head of a dead donkey. While we were thus, Shaddad ibn Aws and Awf ibn Malik came upon us and sat with us. Shaddad said: The thing I fear most for you, O people, is what I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about hidden desire and shirk. Ubadah and Abu al-Darda said: O Allah, forgiveness; had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not told us that Satan has despaired of being worshipped in the Arabian Peninsula — as for the hidden desire, He has forgiven us for it — it is the desires of this world, its women and its lusts."
"2904","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah al-Ansari from Ubadah. 393 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Humran narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us: my father Ja'far ibn Abd Allah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah al-Najjari, that he asked Ubadah ibn al-Samit about the witr, and he said: It is good; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Muslims after him acted upon it, but it is not obligatory."
"2905","Ata ibn Yasar, the freedman of Maymunah al-Madani, from Ubadah. 394 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Yazid narrated to us: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Paradise has one hundred degrees; between every two degrees is a journey of one hundred years. Al-Firdaws is its highest degree; from it gush forth the four rivers, and the Throne is above it. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws al-A'la.'"
"2906","395 - Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yazid narrated to us: Hammam ibn Yahya informed us. 396 - And Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Paradise has one hundred degrees; between every two degrees is a journey of one hundred years' — and Affan said: like what is between the heaven and the earth — 'and al-Firdaws is its highest degree; from it emerge the four rivers, and the Throne is above it. So when you ask Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, ask Him for al-Firdaws.'"
"2907","397 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati and al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab al-Jumahi narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us. 398 - Al-Tabarani said: And Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, they said: Hammam narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Paradise has one hundred degrees; between every two degrees is like what is between the heaven and the earth. Al-Firdaws is its highest degree; from it gush forth the rivers of Paradise. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws.' Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd al-Samad, from Hammam. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Ahmad ibn Mani', both from Yazid. It has a witness in Sahih al-Bukhari from the hadith of Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever believes in Allah and His Messenger, establishes the prayer and fasts Ramadan, it is due upon Allah to admit him to Paradise, whether he emigrates in the cause of Allah or sits in the land in which he was born.' They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not give people the glad tidings of that? He said: 'In Paradise there are one hundred degrees which Allah has prepared for the mujahidin in the cause of Allah; between every two degrees is like what is between the heaven and the earth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the middle of Paradise and the highest of Paradise, and above it is the Throne of the Most Merciful, and from it gush forth the rivers of Paradise.'"
"2908","Another. 399 - Abu al-Fadl ibn Abi Nasr ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Khalid and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu al-Qasim Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: Abd al-Razzaq ibn Umar ibn Musa informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Abu Musa Isa ibn Hammad Zughbah narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd informed us, from Hisham — that is Ibn Urwah — from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: 'Whoever wrongs the people of Madinah and frightens them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him.'"
"2909","400 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu al-Zinba' Rawh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us. 401 - And Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami' al-Misri narrated to us: Isa ibn Hammad narrated to us, they said: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Whoever wrongs the people of Madinah and frightens them, then frighten him; upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl will be accepted from him.'"
"2910","Uthman ibn Abi Sawdah al-Shami from Ubadah. 402 - Abu al-Majd al-Fadl ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim ibn Sulayman ibn al-Baniyasi informed us, at Damascus, that Abu al-Fadl Muhammad and Abu al-Hasan Ali, sons of al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Mawazini. 403 - And Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Tawus informed us, at Damascus, that al-Sharif al-Nasib Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ibrahim, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Hinna'i, and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Tahir ibn Ja'far al-Sulami said: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yahya ibn Sulwan al-Mazini informed us: Abu al-Qasim al-Fadl ibn Ja'far al-Tamimi al-Mu'adhdhin informed us: Abu Ja'far — that is Ibn al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi — narrated to us from dictation: Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us: Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Mawhab narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abi Sawdah narrated to me that he heard Uthman ibn Abi Sawdah say: I saw Ubadah ibn al-Samit with his chest placed upon the wall of the mosque overlooking the Valley of Hell, weeping. I said: O Abu al-Walid, what makes you weep? He said: Because of this place which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us that he saw Hell from."
"2911","404 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Umayyah Amr ibn Hisham al-Harrani narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from Yazid ibn Abi Sawdah, from his brother Ibn Abi Sawdah, he said: I saw Ubadah ibn al-Samit upon the wall — the wall of the mosque overlooking the Valley of Hell — with his chest placed upon it, weeping. I said: O Abu al-Walid, what makes you weep? He said: This is the place which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us that he saw Hell in."
"2912","Fadalah ibn Ubayd — a Companion — from Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him. 405 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us, at Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Isma'il ibn al-Hasan al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Abu Hani narrated to us, from Amr ibn Malik, from Fadalah ibn Ubayd, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day, traveling upon his mount with his Companions with him, none advancing ahead of him. Mu'adh ibn Jabal said: O Prophet of Allah, ask Allah to make our day before yours. Tell me, if something happens — and may Allah not show us that — which deeds should we do after you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent. He said: 'Jihad in the cause of Allah.' May my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'What a fine thing jihad in the cause of Allah is; yet what controls people is more decisive than that.' He said: Then fasting and charity? He said: 'What fine things fasting and charity are; yet what controls people is more decisive than that.' Mu'adh mentioned every good deed he could do, and each time the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'What controls people is more decisive than that.' He said: May my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, what is it that controls people more decisively than that? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed to his mouth and said: 'Silence, except from good.' He said: Will we be taken to account for what our tongues utter? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck the thigh of Mu'adh and said: 'O Mu'adh ibn Jabal, may your mother be bereaved of you' — or what Allah willed him to say — 'and does anything throw people upon their nostrils into Hell except what their tongues utter? Whoever believes in Allah, let him speak good or keep silent from evil. Speak good and you will gain; keep silent from evil and you will be safe.'"
"2913","Qays ibn al-Harith al-Madhhiji from Ubadah. 406 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abu Muhammad Isa ibn Musa narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Ubayd Allah, from Qays ibn al-Harith, that he heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: 'I narrate to you the hadith, so let the one present among you convey to the one absent.'"
"2914","Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami Abu Shajarah al-Rahawi from Ubadah. 407 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay' narrated to us: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ubadah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no soul that dies, having good with Allah, that wishes to return to you while the world is hers, except the one slain in battle; he wishes to return and be slain once more.'"
"2915","408 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ibn Jurayj, from Sulayman ibn Musa: Kathir ibn Murrah narrated to us that Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to them: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul upon the earth that dies, having good with Allah, that wishes to return to you, except the one slain in the cause of Allah; he wishes to return and be slain once more."
"2916","409 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ahmad ibn Khulayd al-Halabi narrated to us: Abu Tawbah narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah: Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to us: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul upon the earth that dies, having good with Allah, that wishes to return to you even if the world is hers, except the martyr; he wishes to return and be slain once more."
"2917","410 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed me that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us: Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abu Asim narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'There is no soul that dies, having good with Allah, that wishes to return to you, except the one slain in the cause of Allah; he wishes to return and be slain once more.' Al-Haytham ibn Humayd added in his chain Sulayman ibn Musa between Kathir and Zayd. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal al-Dimashqi, from Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay', from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Kathir ibn Murrah, without mentioning Sulayman ibn Musa; perhaps Zayd heard it from Kathir and from Sulayman from him, and Allah knows best."
"2918","Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' al-Ansari from Ubadah. 411 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Ja'far ibn Mihran al-Sabbak narrated to us: Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Makhul, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' al-Ansari — who used to live in Iliya' — from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Fajr prayer, and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he finished he said: 'I see you reciting behind your imam?' He said: We said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, indeed. He said: 'Do not do so except with the Mother of the Qur'an, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.'"
"2919","412 - Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq — that is Muhammad — from Makhul, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and recited, and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he finished he said: 'Are you reciting?' We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Then it does not harm you not to do so except with the Opening of the Book.'"
"2920","413 - With the same chain: my father narrated to me: Ya'qub narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq: Makhul narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn Rabi' al-Ansari, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Fajr prayer, and the recitation became heavy upon him. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer, he turned to us with his face and said: 'I see you reciting behind your imam when he recites aloud?' He said: We said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, indeed it is so. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Do not do so except with the Mother of the Qur'an, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.'"
"2921","414 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Makhul, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Isha prayer and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he finished he said: 'Perhaps you recite behind your imam?' We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, we do so. He said: 'Do not do so except with the Mother of the Qur'an, for there is no prayer except with it.' Thus this narration says al-Isha, while the well-known version is al-Fajr. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Yazid, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq. Abu Dawud narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Nufayli, from Muhammad ibn Salamah, from Ibn Ishaq. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad, from Abdah, from Ibn Ishaq, and said: a hasan hadith. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Ibn Khuzaymah, from al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Jazari, from Abd al-A'la, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"2922","Another. 415 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them — while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far informed us: Isma'il ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd al-A'la ibn Mushir narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Khalid ibn Dihqan informed us: that they were in the campaign of Constantinople. He said: We were at al-Dulfiyah, when a man from the people of Palestine, from their nobles and best, recognized as such, called Hani ibn Kulthum ibn Sharik, came forward and said: I heard Mahmud ibn Rabi' narrate, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that he heard him narrate from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Whoever kills a believer and then gloats over his killing, Allah will accept neither sarf nor adl from him.' And he said: 'The believer continues swift and unburdened, or light and swift, so long as he does not shed unlawful blood; when he sheds blood, he becomes stuck.'"
"2923","416 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, at Isfahan, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dihqan, from Hani ibn Kulthum, from Mahmud ibn Rabi'ah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Whoever kills a believer and then gloats over his killing, Allah will accept neither sarf nor adl from him.'"
"2924","417 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Ammar: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Khalid ibn Dihqan narrated to us, from Hani ibn Kulthum, he said: I heard Mahmud ibn Rabi'ah, from Ubadah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: 'Whoever kills a believer and gloats over his killing, Allah will accept neither sarf nor adl from him.'"
"2925","418 - With the same chain: Bakr ibn Sahl narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dihqan, from Hani ibn Kulthum, from Mahmud ibn Rabi'ah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The believer continues swift and righteous so long as he does not shed unlawful blood; when he sheds unlawful blood, he becomes stuck."
"2926","419 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Baqi ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Harawi informed us, at Baghdad, that Umar ibn Muhammad al-Bistami informed them: Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khuza'i informed us: al-Haytham ibn Kulayb al-Shashi informed us: Ibn Affan al-Amiri — that is al-Hasani — narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Dihqan, from Hani ibn Kulthum, from Mahmud ibn Rabi'ah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The believer continues swift and righteous so long as he does not shed unlawful blood; when he sheds unlawful blood, he becomes stuck.' Abu Dawud narrated it from Mu'ammal ibn al-Fadl al-Harrani, from Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb, from Khalid ibn Dihqan, from Hani ibn Kulthum ibn Sharik al-Kinani al-Filastini, from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', from Ubadah; and it is one hadith."
"2927","Maymun ibn Abi Shabib from Ubadah. 420 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ja'far ibn Sunayd ibn Dawud narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the rulers and said: 'There will be rulers over you; if you obey them they will admit you into the Fire, and if you disobey them they will kill you.' A man among them said: O Messenger of Allah, name them for us, perhaps we may throw dust in their faces. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Perhaps they will throw it in your face and gouge out your eye.'"
"2928","Nafi' ibn Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' al-Ansari from Ubadah. 421 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Zayd ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Hizam ibn Hakim and Makhul, from Nafi' ibn Mahmud ibn Rabi'ah al-Ansari, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the prayers in which the recitation is aloud and said: 'Let none of you recite aloud when I recite aloud, except with the Mother of the Qur'an.' Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman, from Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, from al-Haytham ibn Humayd, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Makhul, from Nafi'. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Hisham ibn Ammar with his chain, without mentioning Makhul."
"2929","Nusayy Abu Ubadah from Ubadah. 422 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us that Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Umar ibn al-Samarqandi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Hisham ibn Sa'd informed me. 423 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr al-Azdi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Hisham ibn Sa'd informed me, from Hatim ibn Abi Nasr, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from his father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"2930","424 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Mujallid informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us: Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us: Ahmad — that is Ibn Abd al-Rahman — narrated to us: my uncle — that is Ibn Wahb — narrated to us: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Hatim ibn Abi Nasr, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from his father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The best shroud is the hullah, and the best sacrifice is the horned ram.' And in al-Baghawi's narration: 'a sacrifice.'"
"2931","425 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi al-Asbahani informed us, at Damascus, that his grandfather, the imam and hafiz Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Taymi, informed them: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Faqih informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshidh stated his saying: Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad informed us: Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Hatim ibn Abi Nasr, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from his father, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'The best shroud is the hullah, and the best sacrifice is the horned ram.' Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Salih. Ibn Majah narrated it from Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la, both from Ibn Wahb."
"2932","Al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit from his father, may Allah be pleased with him. 426 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to me, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Abu Zayd al-Himsi: Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, from his father al-Walid, he said: I entered upon my father Ubadah while I imagined death in him, and I said: O father, advise me and exert yourself. He said: Seat me. So he was seated and said: O my son, you will not taste faith nor reach the true knowledge of Allah until you believe in qadar, its good and its evil. He said: He said: O father, how can I know the good of qadar from its evil? He said: You know that what missed you was never going to befall you, and what befell you was never going to miss you. O my son, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The first thing Allah created was the Pen. He said: Write. So it flowed in that hour with what is to be.' O my son, if you die and are not upon this, you will enter the Fire."
"2933","427 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Idris ibn Abd al-Karim al-Haddad narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us. 428 - Al-Tabarani said: And Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us. 429 - He said: And Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Sulaym al-Maliki narrated to us: Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated to us, he said: I asked al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit: How was it in your father's bequest? He said: When death came to him, he called me and said to me: O my son, fear Allah, and know that you will not fear Allah nor reach knowledge until you believe in Allah alone and believe in qadar, its good and its evil. I said: O father, how do I believe in qadar, its good and its evil? He said: You know that what befell you was never going to miss you, and what missed you was never going to befall you; this is qadar. If you die upon other than this, you will enter the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The first thing Allah created was the Pen, and He said: Write. It said: O Lord, what shall I write? He said: Qadar. So the Pen flowed in that hour with what was and what is to be, forever.'"
"2934","430 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah: Sulayman ibn Habib narrated to me, from al-Walid ibn Ubadah: that when Ubadah was dying, his son Abd al-Rahman said to him: O father, advise me. Ubadah said: Seat me. So they seated him, and he said: O my son, fear Allah; you will not fear Allah until you believe in Allah, and you will not believe in Allah until you believe in qadar, its good and its evil, and know that what befell you was never going to miss you, and what missed you was never going to befall you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Qadar is upon this; whoever dies upon other than it will enter the Fire.'"
"2935","431 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us: al-Layth — that is Ibn Sa'd — narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from Ayyub ibn Ziyad: Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to me: my father narrated to me, he said: I entered upon Ubadah while he was ill, death imagined in him or evident, and I said: O father, advise me and exert yourself for me. He said: Seat me. When they seated him he said: O my son, you have not tasted the taste of faith nor will you reach the true reality of knowledge of Allah until you believe in qadar, its good and its evil. I said: O father, how can I know the good of qadar from its evil? He said: You know that what missed you was never going to befall you, and what befell you was never going to miss you. O my son, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The first thing Allah created was the Pen, then He said: Write. So it flowed in that hour with what is to be until the Day of Resurrection.' O my son, if you die and are not upon that, you will enter the Fire. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abu al-Ala al-Hasan ibn Sawwar. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Yahya ibn Musa al-Balkhi, from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Sulaym, and said: a hasan sahih gharib hadith. Abd al-Wahid ibn Sulaym and Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah have been criticized, except that it was narrated from other than their route. Abu Zayd al-Himsi — and it is said Abu Ziyad — is Ayyub ibn Ziyad, and al-Tirmidhi declared it sahih."
"2936","Another. 432 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: al-Nu'man ibn Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn al-Walid, from his father al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: Two men of the Ansar disputed; one of them said: The witr after Isha is like the obligation. They went out until they came to Ibn Muhayriz and mentioned to him what they disputed about. Ibn Muhayriz said to them: It is like the obligation. They left him and met Ubadah ibn al-Samit and mentioned to him what they disputed about and what Ibn Muhayriz had answered them. He said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Allah has obligated five prayers upon His creation. Whoever performs them as obligated upon him, without diminishing any of their due out of disregard, then he has a covenant with Allah that He will not punish him. And whoever diminishes any of their due out of disregard for it, then he will meet Allah with no covenant for him; if He wills He will punish him, and if He wills He will forgive him.' But it is a sunnah which should not be abandoned."
"2937","Another. 433 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah al-Laftuwani informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman al-Razi informed us: Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us: al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub and Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, from his father al-Walid, from his grandfather Ubadah, he said: I used to perform ruqyah for the fever of the evil eye in the Jahiliyyah. He said: When we became Muslim, I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ubadah says: By Allah, had it not been for that, I would never have performed ruqyah upon any human with it again."
"2938","434 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us: Ayyash ibn al-Walid al-Raqqam narrated to us: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: I used to perform ruqyah for the poison of the evil eye in the Jahiliyyah. When I became Muslim, I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: 'Present it to me.' So I presented it to him, and he said: 'Perform ruqyah with it; there is no harm in it.' Ubadah said: Had it not been for that, I would never have performed ruqyah upon any human with it again."
"2939","Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah from his grandfather Ubadah. 435 - Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi Hanifah al-Harimi informed us, at al-Harim, that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from his grandfather Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever fights in the cause of Allah while intending in his fighting nothing but a hobbling rope, he shall have what he intended.'"
"2940","436 - With the same chain: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Bahz narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from his grandfather Ubadah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever fights in the cause of Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, intending in his fighting nothing but a hobbling rope, he shall have what he intended.' Bahz said in his hadith: Jabalah ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah."
"2941","437 - With the same chain, Abd Allah narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath and Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji narrated to me, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever fights...' Ibrahim said in his hadith: 'in the cause of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, intending in his fighting nothing but a hobbling rope, he shall have what he intended.'"
"2942","438 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah al-Laftuwani informed us that al-Husayn al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman al-Razi informed us: Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from his grandfather Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever fights in the cause of Allah and intends in his fighting nothing but a hobbling rope, he shall have what he intended.'"
"2943","439 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal al-Anmati narrated to us. 440 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Hasan ibn Hammad ibn Fadalah al-Basri narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, from Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from his grandfather Ubadah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'Whoever fights in the cause of Allah intending in his fighting nothing but a hobbling rope, he shall have what he intended.' Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Harun ibn Abd Allah, from Yazid ibn Harun, and from Amr ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman; in it: from Ibn al-Walid, without naming him."
"2944","And from the kunyas from Ubadah: Abu Sallam al-Aswad, whose name is Mamtur, from Ubadah. 441 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Ali ibn Hawshab al-Fazari narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Sallam al-Aswad narrate, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man in the rear of the mosque wearing a saffron-dyed wrapper, and said: 'Is there no man to screen between me and this Fire?' And a man did so."
"2945","442 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abu Amir al-Nahwi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us: Ali ibn Hawshab narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Sallam say: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit say: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the mosque, a man passed by him wearing a deeply saturated saffron-dyed garment, and he said: 'Is there no man to screen between me and this Fire?'"
"2946","Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Ubadah. 443 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us: Ibn Qutaybah informed us: Abu Umayr al-Nahhas narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit was seen upon the eastern wall of Bayt al-Maqdis weeping. He was asked, and he said: From here the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us that he saw Malik turning over embers like a cluster of dates."
"2947","Abu Qabil al-Ma'afiri, whose name is Huyayy ibn Abd Allah — and it is said Ibn Hani — from Ubadah. 444 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Harun narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Malik ibn al-Khayr al-Zabadi narrated to me, from Abu Qabil al-Ma'afiri. 445 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Isma'il ibn al-Khaffaf al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Malik ibn al-Khayr al-Zabadi narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'He is not of my ummah who does not honor our elder, have mercy upon our young, and recognize the right of our scholar.' The wording is one. Abd Allah ibn Ahmad said: And I heard it myself from Harun."
"2948","Abu Yazid al-Urdunni — and it is said al-Azdi — from Ubadah. 446 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Amr ibn Abi al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh al-Misri narrated to us: Mahmud ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Rabah ibn al-Walid al-Dhimari narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to me, from Abu Yazid al-Urdunni, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'The first thing Allah created was the Pen.' He said to it: Write. It said: O Lord, what shall I write? He said: Write the decrees of all things."
"2949","Al-Mukhdaji al-Kinani from Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him. 447 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu Sahl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'dawayh informed them — recited to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Raffa al-Surramarra'i informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Samad informed us: Abu Mus'ab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, from Ibn Muhayriz: that a man of Banu Kinanah called al-Mukhdaji heard a man in Syria called Abu Muhammad say: The witr is obligatory upon the people. Al-Mukhdaji said: So I went to Ubadah ibn al-Samit, intercepted him while he was going to the mosque, and told him what Abu Muhammad had said. Ubadah said: Abu Muhammad has lied."
"2950","448 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from Malik. 449 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ali ibn al-Mubarak al-San'ani narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us: Malik narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, from Ibn Muhayriz: that a man of Kinanah called al-Mukhdaji heard a man in Syria called Abu Muhammad say: The witr is obligatory. Al-Mukhdaji said: So I went out to Ubadah ibn al-Samit, intercepted him while he was going to the mosque, and told him what Abu Muhammad had said. Ubadah said: Abu Muhammad has lied. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Five prayers which Allah has prescribed upon the servants. Whoever comes with them without neglecting any of them out of disregard for their right, he shall have a covenant with Allah to admit him to Paradise. And whoever does not come with them has no covenant with Allah; if He wills He will punish him, and if He wills He will admit him to Paradise.' The wording of al-Qa'nabi and Isma'il. And in the narration of Abu Mus'ab: 'Whoever comes with them without diminishing any of them.'"
"2951","450 - Abu Zur'ah Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Laftuwani informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad al-Razi informed us: Ja'far ibn Abd Allah informed us: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Ruyani informed us: Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abd Rabbih, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, from Ibn Muhayriz, from al-Mukhdaji, he said: A man asked Abu Muhammad — a man of the Ansar — about the witr, and he said: The witr is obligatory like the obligation of prayer. So he came to Ubadah and mentioned that to him. He said: Abu Muhammad has lied. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'Five prayers which Allah has obligated upon His servants. Whoever comes with them without diminishing any of them out of disregard for its right, then Allah will make for them on the Day of Resurrection a covenant to admit him to Paradise. And whoever comes with them having diminished any of them out of disregard for their right has no covenant with Allah; if He wills He will punish him, and if He wills He will forgive him.' Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, and from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, similarly. Abu Dawud narrated it from al-Qa'nabi. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah, from Malik. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar. Abu Hatim al-Busti narrated it from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani, from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Ibn Abi Adi, from Shu'bah."
"2952","Ubadah ibn Qurs — and it is said Qurt — al-Laythi, may Allah be pleased with him. 451 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah, from Ubadah ibn Qurt or Qurs, he said: You do deeds which are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the deadly sins."
"2953","452 - With the same chain: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal: Abu Qatadah narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn Qurs or Qurt, he said: You today do deeds which are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the deadly sins. I said to Abu Qatadah: What if he had lived to see our time? Abu Qatadah said: He would have said that even more."
"2954","453 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Miqdam ibn Dawud narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated to us. 454 - Al-Tabarani said: And Umar ibn Hafs al-Sadusi narrated to us: Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah al-Adawi, from Ubadah ibn Qurs, he said: You do deeds which are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among the deadly sins."
"2955","455 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us: Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us: Abu Qatadah al-Adawi narrated to us, he said: Ubadah ibn Qurt said: You do deeds which are finer in your eyes than a hair; we used to count them as the deadly sins in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Qatadah al-Adawi — his name is Tamim ibn Nudayr, and it is said Ibn al-Zubayr — is among the men of Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj."
"2956","Another. 456 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Sabbah al-Raqqi narrated to us: Mu'alla ibn Asad al-Ammi narrated to us: Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us. 457 - Al-Tabarani said: And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna al-Anbari and Abdan ibn Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Ubadah ibn Qurs: that he went out on a campaign and remained in it as long as Allah willed, then returned until, when he was near al-Ahwaz, he heard the sound of the adhan. He said: By Allah, I have had no contact with prayer in the congregation of the Muslims for a long time. So he headed toward the adhan intending to pray, when he came upon the Azariqah. They said to him: What has brought you, O enemy of Allah? He said: Are you not my brothers? They said: You are the brother of Satan; we shall surely kill you. He said: What will you accept from me as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted from me? They said: And what did he accept from you? He said: I came to him while I was a disbeliever, and I testified that there is no god but Allah and that he is the Messenger of Allah, so he let me go. So they seized him and killed him."
"2957","Of those named al-Abbas: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim, Abu al-Fadl, the uncle of the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him — may Allah be pleased with him. 458 - The imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi informed us, at Isfahan, that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Musa al-Tahhan: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit narrated to us. 459 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Musa al-Tahhan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We wish to sweep Zamzam, for in it are these jinnan — meaning small snakes — so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that they be killed. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani'. Musa is Ibn Muslim al-Tahhan Abu Isa, known as Musa al-Saghir; it is said he died in Makkah behind the Maqam while prostrating."
"2958","Another. 460 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them — recited to him while he was present: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fadhshah informed us. 461 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them — recited to her while they listened: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us, they said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dawlabi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us. 462 - And Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar and Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, they said: al-Walid ibn Abi Thawr narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Amirah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: We were sitting at al-Batha in a group among whom was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a cloud passed. He looked at it and said: 'Do you know what this is called?' We said: Yes, this is sahab. He said: 'It is muz n and anan.' Then he said: 'Do you know the distance between the heaven and the earth?' We said: No. He said: 'Either one, or two, or three and seventy years; and the heaven is above it' — likewise until he counted seven heavens — 'and above the seventh heaven is a sea, between its bottom and its top like what is between one heaven and another; and above the sea are eight mountain goats, between their hooves and their knees like what is between one heaven and another; then upon their backs is the Throne, between its bottom and its top like what is between one heaven and another; then Allah, the Exalted, is above that.' The wording of Ibn Ridhah, from al-Tabarani. And with Ibn Fadhshah from him: 'between their hooves and their knees what is between one heaven and another; then above their backs is the Throne.' The wording of al-Tabarani's hadith, from Abd Allah ibn Ahmad."
"2959","463 - The free woman Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Sha'ri informed us, at Nishapur, that Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Abd Allah al-Katib al-Juwayni and Jawhar the servant, the freedman of Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn al-Amid, informed them; it was said to them: Musa ibn Imran al-Sufi informed you: al-Sayyid Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud ibn Ali ibn Isa informed us: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Bilal al-Bazzaz informed us: Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Amirah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that he said: A cloud passed over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2960","464 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ali al-Jarudi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd Allah ibn Amirah, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: A cloud passed over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: 'Do you know what this is?' We said: Sahab. He said: 'Or muzn.' They said: Or muzn. He said: 'Or anan.' We said: Or anan. He said: 'Do you know the distance between the heaven and the earth?' We said: No. He said: 'Seventy-one, or seventy-two, or seventy-three.' He said: 'And that which is above it is likewise, until he counted them seven heavens in that manner.' He said: 'Then above the seventh is the sea; its bottom from its top is like what is between one heaven and another. Then above it are eight mountain goats; between their hooves and their knees is like what is between one heaven and another. Then the Throne is above that; between its bottom and its top is like what is between one heaven and another. Then Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, is above that, above the Throne.' The wording is of the hadith of Abu Hamid ibn Bilal... and the hadith of al-Jarudi is similar. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ala, from his uncle Shu'ayb ibn Khalid, from Simak, from Abd Allah ibn Amirah, from al-Abbas, without mentioning al-Ahnaf; in it he said: 'Between them is a journey of five hundred, and from each heaven to a heaven is a journey of five hundred years, and the thickness of each heaven is five hundred years,' and at its end: 'And none of the deeds of the children of Adam is hidden from Him.' Abu Dawud narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, from Ahmad ibn Hafs, and from Ahmad ibn Abi Surayj, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Sa'd, and Muhammad ibn Sa'id, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Simak, with his chain and meaning. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd ibn Humayd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, with his chain and meaning, and said: a hasan gharib hadith. Sharik narrated part of this hadith from Simak, stopping it. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya, from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah."
"2961","Another. 465 - Abu Abd Allah Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman and Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafiyan informed us that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to ask Allah for. He said to me: 'O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter.'"
"2962","466 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us, there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Jamil al-Asbahani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us: Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to ask Allah for. He said: 'Ask Allah for well-being.' I waited some days, then I came and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to ask Allah for. He said to me: 'O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter.'"
"2963","467 - With the same chain, al-Tabarani informed us: Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us. 468 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ishaq al-Tustari narrated to us: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, they said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to ask Allah for. He said: 'Ask your Lord for well-being.' Then I came to him again and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to ask my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic. He said: 'O Abbas, O uncle of the Messenger of Allah, ask your Lord for well-being in this world and the Hereafter.' Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, Muhammad ibn Fudayl, and Sulayman ibn Mihran narrated it from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad."
"2964","469 - Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari, Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Hibat Allah al-Qasri — at Baghdad — and Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi — at Cairo — informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Shaybani informed them: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Bazzaz informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Bazzaz narrated to us: Ibn Najiyah — that is Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Najiyah — narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Sharik and Qays narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from al-Abbas: that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Teach me something to ask my Lord for. He said: 'Ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter.' He repeated it to him, and he said: O uncle, ask Allah for well-being."
"2965","470 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, from Abu Yunus al-Qushayri Hatim ibn Abi Saghir ah: my father narrated to me, from his father, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am your uncle; my age is advanced, my bones are thin, and my term is near, so teach me something by which Allah will benefit me. He said: 'O Abbas, you are my uncle, yet I avail you nothing against Allah; but ask Allah for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter.' He said it three times. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Husayn ibn Ali, from Za'idah, and narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Bakr, and Rawh ibn Hatim ibn Abi Saghir ah, from one of Banu al-Muttalib, he said: Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas came to us saying: My father Abd Allah ibn Abbas narrated to me, from his father al-Abbas. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Ahmad ibn Mani' and said: a sahih hadith; and Abd Allah ibn al-Harith heard from al-Abbas. We only brought it out because of al-Tirmidhi's declaring it sahih, for in its narration is Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad — except that we have brought it from other than his route."
"2966","Another. 471 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muhadir ibn al-Muwarri' narrated to us. 472 - Al-Tabarani said: And al-Husayn ibn Ja'far al-Qattat al-Kufi narrated to us: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Ali ibn Mushir informed us, both from al-A'mash, from Abu Sabrah al-Nakha'i, from Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, he said: Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib said: When Quraysh sat and conversed among themselves, and a man of us, the Ahl al-Bayt, came, they cut off their conversation. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him; and when something reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he admonished them and they took heed. So he addressed them, then said: 'What is with people who converse among themselves, and when they see a man of us, the Ahl al-Bayt, they cut off their conversation? By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, faith does not enter the heart of a man until he loves them for Allah and for their kinship to me.' Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Tarif, from Muhammad ibn Fudayl, from al-A'mash. I have not seen this hadith in Musnad Ahmad. Abu Sabrah's name is not known."
"2967","Another. 473 - Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari, Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Hibat Allah al-Mallah — at Baghdad — and Abu al-Hasan ibn Hamzah ibn Talhah al-Baghdadi — at Cairo — informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ghaylan informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Hadir narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Farra narrated to us: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Abbas, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'My ummah will remain upon the fitrah so long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars intertwine.' Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah narrated it from Awwam ibn Abbad ibn al-Awwam, narrating to us from Qatadah, from al-Hasan. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli, from Ibrahim ibn Musa. Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Abdi al-Basri narrates from Qatadah. Yahya ibn Ma'in said: Thiqah. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: He is not used as proof, without clarifying the criticism. Abd Allah ibn Hadir — al-Daraqutni said: Not strong; but he did not narrate it alone, since Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated it."
"2968","Another. 474 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Abu Maysarah, from al-Abbas, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he said: 'Look, do you see any star in the sky?' He said: I said: Yes. He said: 'What do you see?' He said: I said: I see al-Thurayya. He said: 'Indeed, those of your loins numbering it will rule this ummah — two of them in fitnah.'"
"2969","475 - Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Najiyah — that is Abd Allah ibn Muhammad — narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Abu Maysarah, he said: I heard al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib say: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he said: 'Look, do you see any star in the sky?' I said: Yes. He said: 'What do you see?' I said: I see al-Thurayya. He said: 'Indeed, those of your loins numbering it will possess this ummah.' It was said to Abu Sa'id ibn Yahya, who had omitted from the hadith 'two of them in fitnah' — he said: It is as I said."
"2970","476 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Abi Qurrah narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Qabil, from Abu Maysah — the freedman of al-Abbas — he said: I heard al-Abbas say: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: 'Look, do you see anything in the sky?' I said: Yes. He said: What do you see? I said: I see al-Thurayya. He said: 'Indeed, those of your loins numbering it will possess this ummah.'"
"2971","Another. 477 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Muttalib al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Ja'far ibn Tamam, from his grandfather al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade branding on the face. Al-Abbas said: I brand only on the buttocks."
"2972","478 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us: Ja'far ibn Tamam ibn al-Abbas narrated to me, from his grandfather al-Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me from branding on the face. Al-Abbas said: I brand only the farthest bone, so he branded on the buttocks. I am not certain whether Ja'far ibn Tamam heard from his grandfather or not; he has narrated from his father, from his grandfather, other than this."
"2973","Another. 479 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ya'qub narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Iyas ibn Afif al-Kindi, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: I was a merchant man. I came for Hajj and went to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib to buy some merchandise from him — and he was a merchant man. By Allah, while I was with him at Mina, a man came out of a tent near him, looked at the sun, and when he saw that it had declined — meaning he stood to pray. He said: And a woman came out of that tent from which the man had come out, and stood behind him praying. Then a boy on the verge of puberty came out of that tent and stood with him praying. He said: So I said to al-Abbas: What is this, O Abbas? He said: This is Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, the son of my brother. He said: So I said: Who is this woman? He said: This is his wife Khadijah bint Khuwaylid. He said: I said: Who is this youth? He said: This is Ali ibn Abi Talib, the son of his uncle. He said: So I said: What is this that he is doing? He said: He is praying, and he claims he is a prophet, and none has followed him in his affair except his wife and this youth, the son of his uncle; and he claims that the treasures of Kisra and Caesar will be opened to him. He said: And Afif — the cousin of al-Ash'ath ibn Qays — who later became Muslim and whose Islam was good, used to say: Had Allah granted me Islam that day, I would have been a third with Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him."
"2974","480 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Sari al-Naqid and Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, they said: Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq: Yahya ibn Abi al-Ash'ath narrated to me, from Isma'il ibn Iyas ibn Afif al-Kindi — meaning from his father, from his grandfather — he said: I was a merchant in the Jahiliyyah. I went to al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib to buy some merchandise from him — and he was a merchant man. By Allah, while I was with him, a man came out of a tent near him, and he mentioned the hadith similarly. Ali ibn al-Madini narrated it from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yahya ibn al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, with his chain."
"2975","Another. 481 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Husayn ibn al-Sumayda' al-Antaki narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Kathir al-Kahili, from Salih ibn Khabbab, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: that he said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is with Quraysh that they meet one another with faces almost dripping with affection, while they meet us with frowning faces? He said: 'O son of my mother, do they do that?' He said: Yes, by the One Who sent you with the truth. He said: 'By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, they do not believe until they love you for my sake.' Imam Ahmad narrated similar from Yazid, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, and from Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid, from Yazid, from Abd Allah. Al-Tirmidhi also narrated similar from Yusuf ibn Musa, from Ubayd Allah ibn Musa, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Yazid, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, and said: a hasan hadith. I say: Yahya ibn Kathir is al-Asadi al-Kufi; I know no criticism of him, and he is not Yahya ibn Kathir the companion of al-Basri. Abu al-Nadr — this one has been weakened."
"2976","Another. 482 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, thus; and written in the margin was that something had dropped after Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abbas, he said: Al-Abbas had a spout over the road of Umar ibn al-Khattab. Umar put on his clothes on Friday — and two chicks had been slaughtered for al-Abbas — and when he reached the spout, water mixed with the blood of the two chicks poured down, striking Umar, with the blood of the two chicks in it. Umar ordered it removed, then returned, discarded his clothes, put on other clothes, then came and led the people in prayer. Al-Abbas came to him and said: By Allah, it is indeed the place where the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed it. Umar said to al-Abbas: I adjure you to climb upon my back until you place it in the place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed it. Al-Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, did so."
"2977","Another. 483 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Ahmar al-Naqid narrated to us: Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Anmati narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah al-Dashtaki narrated to us: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas, he said: We used to carry stones to the House when Quraysh built the House; Quraysh set apart men two by two carrying stones, and the women carried mortar. I and my nephew were carrying upon our necks with our waist-wrappers beneath the stones; when people came upon us we wrapped ourselves. While I was walking with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ahead of me, wearing no wrapper, he fell flat upon his face. I came hastening, cast down my stone, while he was looking toward the sky. I said: What is the matter with you? He stood, took his wrapper, and said: 'I have been forbidden to walk naked.' I said: I concealed it, fearing they would say: mad. Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated it from Simak ibn Harb. It has a witness in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"2978","Another. 484 - Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Waki'i narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us. 485 - Al-Tabarani said: And Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Awdi narrated to us: Abu Ghassan Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: I said: I shall surely know how long the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remains among us. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, will you not take something such that when you are upon it people see you? He said: 'I shall remain among them, treading upon my heel, disputing my cloak with me, with their dust striking me, until Allah is the One Who relieves me of them.' Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it connected from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except Abu Ghassan. The people narrated it saying: from Ikrimah: that al-Abbas said — the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said — disconnected."
"2979","Another. 486 - Abu al-Majd Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Abu Ali, from Ja'far ibn Tamam, from his father, from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, he said: They used to enter upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) without using the siwak. He said: 'You enter upon me with yellowed teeth and do not use the siwak; so use the siwak. Had I not feared hardship upon my ummah, I would have obligated the siwak upon them as I obligated ablution upon them.' A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept mentioning the siwak until we feared a Qur'an would descend concerning it."
"2980","487 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Barbahari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ali al-Sayqal, from Ja'far ibn Tamam ibn al-Abbas, from his father, from al-Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'What is with you that you enter upon me with yellowed teeth? Use the siwak. Had I not feared hardship upon my ummah, I would have commanded them with the siwak at every prayer.' Abu Ali al-Sayqal — it is said his name is Isa, the seller of striped cloths of Kufa; it is said he is the freedman of Banu Asad; Sufyan al-Thawri and Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir narrated from him. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Isma'il ibn Umar, from Sufyan, from Abu Ali al-Zarrad, from Ja'far ibn Tamam, from his father; and from Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham, from Sufyan, from Abu Ali al-Sayqal, from Qutham ibn Tamam or Tamam ibn Qutham, from his father, without mentioning al-Abbas, placing it in the Musnad of Tamam ibn al-Abbas."
"2981","Another. 488 - Abu Ja'far al-Asbahani informed us, there, that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Idris ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas."
"2982","489 - The shaykh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi informed us that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Wahb ibn Hazm narrated to us: my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ishaq say: Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Allah obligated upon them that one fight ten; that weighed heavily upon them and was hard upon them, so Allah lightened it from them to one man fighting two. Allah sent down concerning that: 'If there are twenty steadfast among you, they will overcome two hundred' to the end of the verses, 'Had it not been for a decree from Allah that preceded, a great punishment would have touched you for what you took' — meaning the spoils of Badr — saying: Had I not refrained from punishing one who disobeys Me until I warn him beforehand. Then He said: 'O Prophet, say to those captives in your hands' — the verse. Al-Abbas said: By Allah, it was revealed concerning me when I told the Messenger of Allah of my Islam. I asked him to reckon for me the twenty ounces I had brought with me thus, and he gave me for them twenty slaves, each of whom traded with wealth in his hand, besides what I hope for of Allah's forgiveness. The wording of the hadith of Jarir. And in the narration of Yazid ibn Harun he said: It was obligated upon them that one fight ten; that weighed heavily upon them and was hard, so Allah lightened that from them and returned them to fighting the enemy when they were twice their number. Then this verse was sent down: 'It is not for a prophet to have captives' and this verse: 'O Prophet, say to those captives in your hands.' Al-Abbas used to say: This verse was revealed concerning me when I told the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of my Islam; I asked him to reckon for me the twenty ounces taken from me, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused, then gave me for the twenty ounces twenty slaves, each trading with wealth with him in his hand, besides what I hope for of Allah's forgiveness and mercy."
"2983","Al-Abbas ibn Mirdas al-Sulami, may Allah be pleased with him. 490 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz, Abu Muslim al-Kashshi, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna, and Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Surah al-Baghdadi narrated to us, they said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us. 491 - Al-Tabarani said: And Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from a son of Kinanah ibn Abbas ibn Mirdas al-Sulami, from his father, from his grandfather Abbas ibn Mirdas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for his ummah on the evening of Arafah for forgiveness and mercy, supplicating abundantly. He was answered: 'I have done so, except for the wrong they do one another; as for what is between Me and them, I have forgiven it. He said: O Lord, You are able to reward this wronged one better than his wrong, and forgive this wrongdoer.' He was not answered that evening with anything. When it was the morning of Muzdalifah, he repeated the supplication, and He answered him: 'I have forgiven them.' He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled. One of his Companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you have smiled at an hour in which you did not use to smile. He said: 'I smiled at the enemy of Allah, Iblis; when he learned that Allah had answered me, he began calling out woe and destruction, throwing dust upon his head.'"
"2984","492 - With the same chain, Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Saji narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Salihi narrated to us: Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Kinanah ibn Abbas ibn Mirdas al-Sulami, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"2985","493 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji narrated to me: Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari narrated to us: a son of Kinanah ibn al-Abbas ibn Mirdas narrated to us, from his father, that his father al-Abbas ibn Mirdas narrated to him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated on the evening of Arafah for his ummah for forgiveness and mercy, supplicating abundantly. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, answered him: 'I have done so and forgiven your ummah, except for one who wrongs another among them.' He said: 'O Lord, You are able to forgive the wrongdoer and reward the wronged one better than his wrong.' That evening there was nothing but that. When it was the next day, he supplicated on the morning of Muzdalifah, repeating his supplication for his ummah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) soon smiled. One of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom, you laughed at an hour in which you did not use to laugh; what made you laugh — may Allah make your tooth laugh? He said: 'I smiled at the enemy of Allah, Iblis, when he learned that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, had answered me concerning my ummah and forgiven the wrongdoer; he fell to calling out destruction and woe, throwing dust upon his head. So I smiled at what he did out of his anguish.' Abu Dawud narrated it from Isa ibn Ibrahim al-Biraki and Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi. Ibn Majah narrated it from Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Salihi, clarifying in his narration the name of the son of Kinanah."
"2986","Of those named Abd Allah: Abd Allah ibn Arqam ibn Abd Yaghuth ibn Wahb ibn Abd Manaf ibn Zuhrah al-Zuhri, may Allah be pleased with him. 494 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu Sahl Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'dawayh informed them — recited to him: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Razi informed us: the judge Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Raffa al-Surramarra'i informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Samad al-Hashimi informed us: Abu Mus'ab Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr al-Zuhri al-Madani narrated to us: Malik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father: that Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam used to lead his companions in prayer. One day the prayer came while he went to relieve himself, then returned and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'When one of you finds the need to defecate, let him begin with it before the prayer.'"
"2987","495 - Abu al-Fadl Isma'il ibn Ali ibn Ibrahim al-Janzawi informed us, at Damascus, that Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad al-Ansari informed them: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Hinna'i informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Hilal al-Hinna'i informed us: Abu Yusuf Ya'qub ibn Ahmad al-Jassas narrated to us: al-Fadl — that is al-Rukhami — narrated to us: al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam: that he was in a Hajj or Umrah, leading his companions in prayer. When the prayer came he said: 'Let one of you lead you, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When the prayer comes and one of you needs to relieve himself, let him begin with the need.'"
"2988","496 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them — while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us. 497 - And Abu Ja'far also informed us that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them — recited to her: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us, they said: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: We were with Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam al-Zuhri; he called the prayer, then went to the privy. It was said to him: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'When the prayer is called and one of you needs the privy, let him begin with the privy.' The wording of Abu Nu'aym. And in the narration of Ibn Ridhah, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — and he mentioned the same."
"2989","498 - With the two chains, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam, he said: We were with him on a journey, and he used to lead them. When the prayer came he said: Let one of you lead you, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: 'When the prayer comes and one of you needs to relieve himself, let him begin with the need.'"
"2990","499 - With the same chain, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Hisham ibn Urwah — meaning from his father — he said: We went out in a Hajj or Umrah with Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam al-Zuhri. He called the prayer, then said: Pray, and went to relieve himself. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'When the prayer is called and one of you needs the privy, let him begin with the privy.' A group narrated it from Hisham ibn Urwah, among them Shu'bah, Zuhayr, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, Za'idah, Ayyub ibn Musa, Hammad ibn Zayd, Murajja ibn Raja, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, and Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id. Abu Dawud narrated it from Ahmad ibn Yunus, from Zuhayr. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Hannad ibn al-Sari, from Abu Mu'awiyah, and said: a hasan sahih hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Qutaybah, from Malik. Ibn Majah narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah, all from Hisham. Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq, and Abu Damrah narrated this hadith from Hisham, from his father, from a man who narrated to him, from Abd Allah ibn Arqam. And most of those who narrated it from Hisham did as Zuhayr said. I say: In the narration of Ma'mar, al-Thawri, and Ayyub ibn Musa, from Hisham, from his father, is what indicates that Urwah heard it from Abd Allah ibn Arqam, and Allah knows best. Ibn Khuzaymah narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Abdah, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Hisham."
"2991","Abd Allah ibn Aqram ibn Zayd al-Khuza'i, may Allah be pleased with him. 500 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Aqram: my father narrated to me: that he was with his father at al-Qa' of Namirah. A caravan passed by us, and my father said to me: O my son, stay with your young sheep until I go to these people and question them. He drew near, and I drew near; I was looking at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was prostrating."
"2992","501 - With the same chain: my father narrated to me: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us: Dawud — meaning Ibn Qays — narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Aqram al-Khuza'i narrated to me: my father narrated to me that he was with his father at al-Qa' of Namirah. He said: A caravan passed by us and halted at the side of the road. My father said to me: O my son, stay with your young sheep until I go to this caravan and question them. He said: Thus, he drew near them and I drew near him; the prayer was called, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among them. So I prayed with them, and it was as if I was looking at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prostrated."
"2993","502 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us. 503 - Al-Tabarani said: And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Dawud ibn Qays, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Aqram narrate from his father: that he was with his father at al-Qa' of Namirah. A caravan passed by us and halted at the side of the road. He said to me: O my son, stay with our young sheep until I draw near this caravan. He said: So he drew near them and I drew near with him; the prayer was called, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among them. I was looking at the whiteness of the armpits of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he prostrated."
"2994","504 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi informed us, by ijazah, that Abu Tahir Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham informed them — recited to him while he was present: Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mu'tazz informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Ali — that is Ibn Hujr — narrated to us: Isma'il — that is Ibn Ja'far — narrated to us: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Aqram, from his father, that he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I used to see the whiteness of his armpit when he prostrated. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Kurayb, from Abu Khalid al-Ahmar, from Dawud, and said: a hasan hadith; we know it only from the hadith of Dawud ibn Qays, and we know no other hadith of Abd Allah ibn Aqram from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) besides this hadith. Al-Nasa'i narrated it from Ali ibn Hujr. Ibn Majah narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Waki', and from Bundar, from Ibn Mahdi and Safwan ibn Isa, all from Dawud. Al-Daraqutni mentioned: Abd Allah ibn Aqram, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I looked at the whiteness of his armpits when he prostrated. Dawud ibn Qays narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from his father; Muslim brought it out from him according to his method."
"2995","Musnad of Abd Allah al-Sadusi. Abd Allah ibn al-Aswad al-Sadusi, may Allah be pleased with him. 1 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that Fatimah al-Jawzdaniyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Miskin al-Yamami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Khushaysh, the freedman of Banu Qays ibn Tha'labah — a man of the people of Yamamah — narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Uqbah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from his father, from his grandfather, from the father of his grandfather Abd Allah ibn al-Aswad, he said: We went out to the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the delegation of Banu Sadus from al-Qurayyah, with Judhami dates as a gift to him. We brought them out from al-Burud — the burud of Banu Umayr of al-Qurayyah — and scattered the dates before the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon a leather mat. He took with his two hands from the dates, then said: What dates are these? We said: Judhami. He said: May Allah bless Judhami, and the garden from which this came — or: the orchard from which this came."
"2996","Musnad of Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Juhani. Abd Allah ibn Unays ibn As'ad ibn Haram, al-Juhani, Abu Yahya, may Allah be pleased with him. 2 - Abu Ali Umar ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Umar al-Wa'iz al-Harbi informed us, at al-Harbiyah, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh al-Taymi, from Abu Umamah al-Ansari, from Abd Allah ibn Unays al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among the greatest of major sins are: shirk with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the immersing oath. No swearer swears by Allah a binding oath, introducing into it even the like of a gnat's wing, except that Allah makes it a spot in his heart until the Day of Resurrection."
"2997","3 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Saydalani informed us, at Isfahan, that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, by ijazah: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sawwaf, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us, he said: I heard Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Harun ibn Rawh al-Bardiji: Ibn Sahl narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn al-Muhajir ibn Qunfudh, from Abu Umamah al-Ansari, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Beware the major sins, for they are seven: shirk with Allah, killing the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, zina, consuming riba, consuming the orphan's wealth, fleeing from battle, and disobedience to parents — if Allah wills it was in it: disobedience to parents."
"2998","4 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Umamah, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The greatest of major sins are: shirk with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the immersing oath. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none swears, even over the like of a gnat's wing, except that it becomes a mark in his heart until the Day of Resurrection. In this narration: Abd Allah ibn Abi Umamah."
"2999","5 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Asbahani informed us, there, that Fatimah bint Abd Allah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us: Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Umamah, from Abd Allah ibn Unays, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The greatest of major sins are: shirk with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the immersing oath. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, none swears, even over the like of a gnat's wing, except that it is in his heart until the Day of Resurrection. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abd ibn Humayd, from Yunus ibn Muhammad, and said: a hasan gharib hadith. Abu Umamah al-Ansari is Ibn Tha'labah; his name is not known, and he has narrated hadiths from the Prophet, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I say: And it has been said his name is Iyas ibn Tha'labah. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili. Al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated from the hadith of Abu Bakrah: Shall I not inform you of the greatest of major sins? They said: Yes. He said: Shirk with Allah, disobedience to parents, and false testimony."
"3000","Another. 6 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us. Abd Allah said: And I heard it myself from Harun: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us that Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hubab al-Ansari narrated to him that Abd Allah ibn Unays narrated to him that he and Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, discussed charity one day. Umar said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he mentioned misappropriation of charity: that whoever misappropriates a camel or a sheep from it will come carrying it on the Day of Resurrection? Abd Allah ibn Unays said: Yes."
